  <para style="h">Akpa Ñwed Samwel</para>
  <para style="toc1">Akpa Ñwed Samwel</para>
  <para style="toc2">Akpa Ñwed Samwel</para>
  <para style="toc3">1Sam</para>
  <para style="mt1">Akpa Ñwed Samwel</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="1SA 1" />
  <para style="s1">Emana Samwel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 1:1" />Amaaba awodeen keed a-aketooho Ramataim, awo Suuf a-aketooho abio abod Ifrem; anyịñ amọ akedo Elkana ayịn Yeroham, ayịn Elihu, ayịn Tohu, ayịn Suuf, awo Ifrem. <verse eid="1SA 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 1:2" />Anye akedọ ibaan iba; keed akekere Hana, anye ako akekere Penina. Penina amaanie nditọ ado Hana ikinieghe ndomo keed.<verse eid="1SA 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 1:3" />Isua ke isua awodeen ami amaasiwuọ ke abio amọ akekpono anyʌñ anam uwa anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan ke Silo, itie Họfni ye Finehas, nditọ ideen Elai iba ekedooñoke aku <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 1:4" />Ini akeedodo a-anaaha nte Elkana anam uwa, anye ayaadeeme mbaak unam anọ Penina anwaan amọ ye nditọ amọ ideen ye ibaan. <verse eid="1SA 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 1:5" />Ado ake Hana anye akesinọ udeeme awo iba sia adooho anye amaama anye, ñko <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakọp anye idịb. <verse eid="1SA 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 1:6" />Sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakọp Hana idịb, anwaan ufịb amọ amaasima adiyem anye ikọ nọ ato do esịd ayat anye. <verse eid="1SA 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 1:7" />Ñkpọ ami amaasika iso aba isua ke isua. Ini akeedodo Hana akaaha ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ana anwaan ufịb amọ anam esịd ayat anye tutu anye atua anyʌñ atre udia ndidia. <verse eid="1SA 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 1:8" />Elkana ebe amọ ayaabịp anye abo, “Hana nsoo inam afo atua? Ntak afo umuudiaha ñkpọ-ọ? Nsoo inam esịd ubʌññọ fiin? Ado nte ami mfọnnọ ñkan nditọ duob afo akpenieghe?”<verse eid="1SA 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 1:9" />Ini keed, ke ammọ emaekedia ñkpọ inyʌñ inwọñ ñkpọ ima ke Silo, Hana amaadakka ada. Idaha ntom, Elai a-akedooho aku mmọdo aketie ke ñkpọitie ke mben usʌñ ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 1:10" />Ke ayọhọ mfʌhọ ye ntuaayịd amọ Hana amaabọñ akam anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 1:11" />Anye amaanyʌñ anam akaaña, abo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan, adieke afo aduuse ukuud ayịnufọk mfo unyʌñ untoiyo miin unyʌññọ ufre ayịnufọk mfo ado anọ anye ayịn, ami ñyaayaak anye nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke afịd ayio uwem amọ, ñko akadañ idiidʌkkọ anye iwuod.”<verse eid="1SA 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 1:12" />Ke anye asʌkkọ abọñ akam anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akpeene, Elai amaase anye inua. <verse eid="1SA 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 1:13" />Hana akebọñ akam ke esịd amọ, ndin ñkpọkinua amọ anyeghe ado awo ikoppo uyio amọ. Elai akekere ke ukọd anaam anye. <verse eid="1SA 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 1:14" />Elai amaanyʌñ abo anye “Ukọd aduunaam fiin ikpeene die? Benne ukọd mfo sio.”<verse eid="1SA 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 1:15" />Hana amaabọọrọ, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmi, idooho ntoro. Ami ndo awonwaan ake esịd amọ anekkeke atịmede. Ami ñkinwọññọ ukọd me bie; ñkenwañña esịd mmi nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 1:16" />Kuudat ayịnufọk mfo nte awonwaan ibak; ami nsibọñ akam mi ato ke ayọhọ mfʌhọ ye ukuud mmi.”<verse eid="1SA 1:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 1:17" />Elai amaabọọrọ anye abo, “Nyọñ ke emem ñko yak Abasi Isrel unọ fiin se afo abeeñe ato anye.”<verse eid="1SA 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 1:18" />Anye amaabo, “Yak ayịnufọk mfo akịt mfọn ke iso mfo.” Ndin anye awuọ anyọñ akedia ñkpọ, ñko iso amọ itaaha efiad aba.<verse eid="1SA 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 1:19" />Usiere edem usen ammọ edakka eda etuak iwuod ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ndin ammọ etịmme enyọñọ ufọk ammọ ke Rama. Elkana amaanam ima ye Hana anwaan amọ, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anyʌñ adise anye. <verse eid="1SA 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 1:20" />Nte ini akaaha iso Hana amaayommo idịb anyʌñ aman ayịn awodeen. Anye amaasio ayịn ado anyịñ Samwel,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Samwel atie nte ikọ Hibru awuọñọke Abasi akop</char></note> abo, “Sia adooho ami ñkebeeñe anye nto <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="1SA 1:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Hana Aben Samwel Akediọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 1:21" />Ke ini Elkana ebe amọ akesañake ye afịd ufọk amọ adọọk aka adikinọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> uwa afịd isua amọ ye adisio akaaña amọ, <verse eid="1SA 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 1:22" />Hana ikikaaha. Anye akebo ebe amọ, “Ami mmaasio ayịn ke eba, ami ñyaaben anye ñkeyaak nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ndin anye ayaadʌñ do ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="1SA 1:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 1:23" />Elkana ebe amọ amaabọọrọ anye, “Nam se afo akịt abo ke ufọn fiin. Ba mi tutu afo asio anye ke eba; ado yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anam ikọ amọ afọn ama.” Ke ntoro mma ado amaatie ke ufọk akama ayịn amọ tutu anye awuọ ke eba.<verse eid="1SA 1:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 1:24" />Ke anye amaakewuọ ke eba, anye amaaben ayịn amọ naña akesịp ado, asaña ye ayaaraenañ isua ita, ndomuyo ke efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kilokram 16</char></note> keed ye akpọ ukọd aben anye adi ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Silo. <verse eid="1SA 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 1:25" />Ke emaekewa ayaaraenañ, ammọ emaeben ayịn ado esọk Elai, <verse eid="1SA 1:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 1:26" />anye anyʌñ adibo anye, “Dakka nnọ miin, abọọñ mmi. Adaña nte afo aduuho uwem, ami ndo awonwaan a-akedaaha udiana fiin abọñ akam anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 1:27" />Ami ñkebọñ akam mbeeñe ayịn ami, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anyʌñ annọ miin se ami ñkebeeñe anye. <verse eid="1SA 1:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 1:28" />Ke ntoro, idahami ami mmeyaak anye nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ke afịd uwem amọ ediiyaak anye inọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.” Anye amaanyʌñ atuak iwuod anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> do.<verse eid="1SA 1:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="1SA 2" />
  <para style="s1">Akam Hana</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 2:1" />Ndin Hana amaabọñ akam anyʌñ abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:1">Esịd mmi adaara ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:1">nnʌk<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Nnʌk awuọñọ adudu; se ñko ke 1 Sa 2:10</char></note> mmi akoñ ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:1">Inua mmi abuuro mbuuro akan mme asua mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:1">sia ami mmenem esịd ke adinyaaña mfo.<verse eid="1SA 2:1" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 2:2" />Ibaaha awo ndomokeed se isana nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:2">awo mfen ibaaha ke imiibọhọke afo;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:2">itiad ndomokeed ibaaha nte Abasi ñnyịn.<verse eid="1SA 2:2" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 2:3" />Kuukaa iso utañ ikọ ke ntañidem</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:3">me ayak inua mfo atañ ikọ usọñanyen-usọñanyen,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:3">sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado Abasi a-adiọọñọke ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:3">ñko ato ke anye edomo mme adinam ese.<verse eid="1SA 2:3" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 2:4" />“Ebuuñ mme utịgha mme ñkpọsọñ awo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:4">ado mbon e-eketuakka ukod eteññe edo mbon se inie adudu.<verse eid="1SA 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 2:5" />Mbon ekediaha eyʌkkọ enọ idem ammọ ke ukpekpe utom ebọ ndidia,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:5">ado mbon e-ekekoppo abiọọñ ikoppo abiọọñ aba.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:5">Anye a-akedooho ada aman nditọ itiaba,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:5">ado anye a-akenieghe uwak nditọ ideen aduọọk idodanyen.”<verse eid="1SA 2:5" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 2:6" />“<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aben ñkpa adi anyʌñ anịm uwem;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:6">anye asuuhọ awo asịn ke udi anyʌñ adịppe awo ke anyọñ.<verse eid="1SA 2:6" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 2:7" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adọñ uweene ye imọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:7">anye asuuhọ awo anịm ke isọñ anyʌñ adịppe ke anyọñ.<verse eid="1SA 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 2:8" />Anye adịppe uweene asio ke ntọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:8">anyʌñ adịppe mbon unana asio ke itie ntọñ;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:8">anye anịm ammọ ye nditọ mbọọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:8">anyʌñ anam ammọ enie ebekpo ukpono.”</para>
  <para style="b" vid="1SA 2:8" />
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:8">“Sia mme itiad idakisọñ ederimbod anie <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:8">do ke anye adot ederimbod.”<verse eid="1SA 2:8" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 2:9" />Anye ayaakpeme ñkpad mbon e-enamma akpanikọ ye anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:9">ado eyaekʌp inua mbon ibak ke ñkịm-ñkịm itie.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="1SA 2:9" />
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:9">Idooho ke adudu ke awo anie adikan;<verse eid="1SA 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 2:10" />eyaenuak mbon se ifaaña mfaaña ye <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char></para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:10">Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi ayaasiak aduma ato ke anyọñ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:10">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaakpe ikpe utịd ederimbod.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="1SA 2:10" />
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 2:10">“Anye ayaanọ adidem amọ inweek</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 2:10">anyʌñ abenne nnʌk mbon a-anye ayette adan ke anyọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 2:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 2:11" />Ndin Elkana amaanyọñ ufọk ke Rama, ado ayịn ado amaaba anam utom <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke idak Elai a-akedooho aku.<verse eid="1SA 2:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Ndoom Nditọ Elai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 2:12" />Nditọ Elai ekedu abʌd-abʌd uwem; ammọ ikinieghe mbaak ndomokeed inọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 2:13" />Ndin akedo ido mme aku ke ini akeedodo awo amaanam uwa, ke ayịnufọk aku ayaakama akuum anie ukod ita ke ubọk amọ ke ini esʌkkọ etem unam ado <verse eid="1SA 2:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 2:14" />ñko anyʌñ awuuk akuum ado ke ako ufrañ ñkpọ me ke ketịl me ako ukwak me usiọñ. Se adodo a-akuum asioho adiinie aku. Naña ekesinam afịd nditọ Isrel e-ekediighe Silo ado ami. <verse eid="1SA 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 2:15" />Ado mbemiso etetem akpọñ unam ami, ayịnufọk aku ayaadi adibo awo a-awaaha uwa ami, “Nọ aku usʌk unam yak afọp; anye idiibọọhọ utetem unam uto fiin, ibọhọke ndisi.”<verse eid="1SA 2:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 2:16" />Adieke awo ado abooho anye “Yak etem akpọñ unam ami diin, ndin afo asio se adodo ake afo ayemme,” ayịnufọk ado ayaabọọrọ, “Iyoo, yaak anye nnọ idahami; imiidooho ntoro, ami ñyaubọ ke ñkanubọk.”<verse eid="1SA 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 2:17" />Idiọọkñkpọ ñkparawa ami amaanekke akpon ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, sia ammọ ekesịn uwa <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ndek.<verse eid="1SA 2:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 2:18" />Ado Samwel akenam utom ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, etəkayịn a-asịneke afọñ aboditọñ ake linen. <verse eid="1SA 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 2:19" />Kwa isua eka amọ asikịm etək ewịra aben asọk anye ke ini anye asañake ye ebe amọ akewa uwa a-asidatta itie kwa isua. <verse eid="1SA 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 2:20" />Elai asidiọñ Elkana ye anwaan amọ, abo, “Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> unọ fiin nditọ ato awonwaan ami nọ ediidat itie anye a-anye akebọññọ akam abọ anyʌñ aben asọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.” Ndin ammọ eyaenyọñ ufọk. <verse eid="1SA 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 2:21" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadise Hana, afọn ido ye anye; anye amaaman nditọ ideen ita ye nditọ ibaan iba. Ñko Samwel amaakọt akpon ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="1SA 2:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 2:22" />Idahami Elai a-amaakenekke asọñ, amaakop abaña afịd se nditọ amọ ekenañña ye nditọ Isrel ye naña ammọ ekenaa ye mme ibaan e-ekesibonoke ke inuausʌñ atayad mbono. <verse eid="1SA 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 2:23" />Ndin anye amaabo ammọ, “Nsoo inam ndufo enam utọ ñkpọ ami? Ami mmekop nto afịd awo mbaña mme ibak adinam ake ndufo enamma. <verse eid="1SA 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 2:24" />Iyoo, nditọ mmi; etob a-ami ñkoppo naña asuana ke atu ikọd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ifọnnọ. <verse eid="1SA 2:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 2:25" />Adieke awo keed adueghe awo mfen, Abasi<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido mme abiideikpe</char></note> akeme adisịn emem ke ufọọd ammọ; ado adieke awo ndomokeed adueghe <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, anie awo idiikpe ubọk inọ anye?” Nditọ ideen amọ ikikoppo nsuannọ ete ammọ, sia akedooho uduak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adiwot ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 2:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 2:26" />Ñko Samwel etəkayịn ado amaakaa iso akọt ke ndaha anyʌñ anie mfọn ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye ke iso awo.<verse eid="1SA 2:26" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Prọfesi ke abaña Ufọk Elai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 2:27" />Akem awo Abasi keed amaadibịne Elai adibo anye, “Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ ado ami: ‘Nte ami ñkeyaarake idem mmi nnọ mme nsọbom mfo idaha ammọ ekebaaha ke Iyib ke idak Fero? <verse eid="1SA 2:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 2:28" />Ami ñkemek mme nsọbom mfo ke atu afịd esiin Isrel nte edo aku mmi, nọ esikaa akpokoro uwa mmi, ekefọp insensi, enyʌñ ekọñọ afọñ aboditọñ ke iso mmi.’ Ami mmaanyʌñ nnọ mme nsọbom ekpək ndufo afịd uwa ndidia ake nditọ Isrel ekenọọhọ. <verse eid="1SA 2:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 2:29" />Nsoo inam yak ndufo esọnnọ uwa mmi ake ami ñkewuuhọ ke itie idʌñ mmi ke ukod? Nsoo inam yak afo akpono nditọ mfo añkan miin ke adinam idem ndufo akpon añkan ke adimek itie afịd uwa ake mbon mmi nditọ Isrel enamma?”<verse eid="1SA 2:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 2:30" />“Mmọdo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Abasi Isrel abo ate: ‘Ami mmaanwọñọ ke mbon ekpək ndufo ediinam ñkpọ innọ miin ke nsi-nsi.’ Ado idahami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ abo ‘Nsaa mmi-o! Ami ndiikpono mbon eñkponoke miin, ado mbon ensịnne miin ke ndek ami ñyaasuenne. <verse eid="1SA 2:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1SA 2:31" />Ini asʌk adi ake ami ndiikpịkke nsọñidem ndufo ye nsọñidem ufọk mme aku ndufo nsio, nọ ato do awo ndomokeed adisịm isua usọñ, <verse eid="1SA 2:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="1SA 2:32" />afo ayaanyʌñ akịt ukuud ke itie idʌñ mmi. Akpesʌkado mfọn adiisịm Isrel, ibaaha awo ke ekpək mfo a-adiidu uwem isọñ. <verse eid="1SA 2:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="1SA 2:33" />Awo keed akeedodo ake ami mmeñkpịkkeke nsio ke edinam utom ke akpokoro uwa mmi, ami ndiinịm nọ ato do nnam anye ado nnan ñnyʌñ ñkoot nsọñidem amọ nsio, ñko afịd ubon ndufo eyaekpa ke ini ammọ ekoppo uko nte ideen.’ ”<verse eid="1SA 2:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="1SA 2:34" />“ ‘Ñko se idiitịppe inọ nditọ ideen mfo iba, Họfni ye Finehas, adiido idiọọñọ unọ fiin, ammọ awo iba ediikpa usen keed. <verse eid="1SA 2:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="1SA 2:35" />Ami ñyaasio aku anam akpanikọ nnọ idem mmi, anye ayaanam akeene se isịne ke esịd ye ke akikere mmi. Ami ñyaanekke nsọọñọ ufọk amọ ñko ammọ ediinam ñkpọ ke iso mbon ake ami ñyette adan afịd ini.’ ” <verse eid="1SA 2:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="1SA 2:36" />Ndin amaakem afịd awo se isʌhọ ke ekpək mfo eyaedibịne anye ekesuuk iwuod ke iso amọ ebeeñe silfa ye uyo enyʌñ ekpeiye ebo, “Mmek miin sịn ke itie utom mme aku nọ ato do nnie se ndia.”<verse eid="1SA 2:36" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="1SA 3" />
  <para style="s1">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Akoot Samwel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 3:1" />Samwel etəkayịn awodeen ado amaanam ñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke idak Elai. Ke mme usen ado, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikiwakka; mme ñkukịd ñko ikiwakka.<verse eid="1SA 3:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 3:2" />Akonayio keed Elai, a-anyen amọ amaaketọọñọ ikịm tutu anye inekkeke ikịt usʌñ, akena ke itie anye asinaaha. <verse eid="1SA 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 3:3" />Utuenikañ Abasi ikinịmeke diin, ndin Samwel akena ke ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke itie a-akebe edioomo Abasi akebaaha. <verse eid="1SA 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 3:4" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakoot Samwel.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 3:4">Samwel amaabọọrọ “Se miin mi.” <verse eid="1SA 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 3:5" />Ndin anye amaafeghe abịne Elai akebo, “Se ami mi; afo akeñkoot.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 3:5">Ado Elai amaabo, “Ami ñkukoodo; tịmme kaa kesuuk naa.” Anye amaatịmme akesuuk anaa.<verse eid="1SA 3:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 3:6" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaatịmme akoot, “Samwel!” Samwel amaadakka ada abịne Elai akebo, “Se ami mi; afo akeñkoot.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 3:6">Elai amaabo, “Ayịn mmi. Ami ñkukoodo fiin; tịmme kaa kesuuk naa.”<verse eid="1SA 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 3:7" />Idahami, Samwel ikidiọọñọke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> diin, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikiyaarake inọ anye diin.<verse eid="1SA 3:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 3:8" />Ayọhọ akañ ita <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakoot “Samwel!” Samwel amaadakka ada abịne Elai akebo, “Se ami mi; afo akeñkoot.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 3:8">Ndin Elai adidiọọñọ ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akoot etəkayịn ado. <verse eid="1SA 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 3:9" />Ke ntoro, Elai amaabo Samwel, “Kaa kesuuk naa, ndin anye akpemaana ukoot fiin, afo abo, ‘<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> tañ, sia ayịnufọk mfo asʌk akpañ utọñ.’ ” Samwel ndin amaamaana akesuuk anaa ke itie amọ.<verse eid="1SA 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 3:10" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaasọiyọ adida do, akoot nte ke mme ini ako, “Samwel! Samwel!”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 3:10">Ndin Samwel amaabọọrọ, “Tañ, ke ayịnufọk mfo asʌk akpañ utọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 3:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 3:11" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanyʌñ abo Samwel ate: “Se, ami mmebeeñe idem adinam ñkpọ ke Isrel a-adiinam nọ utọñ adeebe afịd awo se ikop. <verse eid="1SA 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 3:12" />Ke ini ado ami ñyaanam afịd se ñketañ mbaña ufọk Elai, tọọñọ ke akpa tutu akpatre. <verse eid="1SA 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 3:13" />Sia ami mmaadọkkọ anye ke ñyaakpe ikpe nnọ ufọk amọ ke nsi-nsi ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ a-anye akediọọñọke abaña; nditọ amọ ideen emaenam ñkpọ isuuñọ ke iso Abasi, ndin anye ikikpanna ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 3:14" />Ke ntak ado ami mmaanwọñọ nnọ ufọk Elai, ‘Ibaaha uwa me enọ ndomokeed se ediikama ikpe ubọk inọ ndudue ufọk Elai.’ ”<verse eid="1SA 3:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 3:15" />Samwel amaasuuk anaa tutu ayio asiere ndin anye abeere usʌñ ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Idem amaanyeñ anye adidọkkọ Elai ñkukịd ado, <verse eid="1SA 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 3:16" />ado Elai akoot anye anyʌñ abo, “Samwel, ayịn mmi.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 3:16">Samwel amaabọọrọ, “Se miin mi.”<verse eid="1SA 3:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 3:17" />Elai amaabịp anye ate, “Nsoo ke anye akudọkkọ fiin? Kundịp miin. Yak Abasi unọmọ fiin, anyʌñ anam ntoro ataa eti-eti, adieke afo andịppe miin ñkpọ ndomokeed se anye akudọkkọ fiin.” <verse eid="1SA 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 3:18" />Ke ntoro Samwel amaakoono afịd ñkpọ adọkkọ anye, idịppe anye ñkpọ ndomokeed. Ndin Elai abo, “Anye ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; yak anye anam se anye akịt abo ke afọn.”<verse eid="1SA 3:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 3:19" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaaba ye Samwel naña anye asʌkkọ akpon, ikinyʌññọ iyak ikọ amọ ndomokeed aduọ ke isọñ. <verse eid="1SA 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 3:20" />Ñko afịd Isrel tọọñọ ke Daan tutu akesịm Beeseba emaekịt ke akpanikọ ke Samwel ado prọfed <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 3:21" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakaa iso awọt idem amọ ke Silo, ndin do anye amaayaara idem amọ awọt Samwel ato ke ikọ amọ.<verse eid="1SA 3:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="1SA 4" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 4:1" />Ndin ikọ Samwel adi afịd Isrel.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="1SA 4:1">Mbon Filistia Eben Akebe Edioomo</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 4:1">Akem nditọ Isrel emaewuọ ekaa ekọñ ye mbon Filistia. Nditọ Isrel ekenam nnaaekọñ ammọ ke Ebenesa, mbon Filistia enam ake ammọ ke Afek. <verse eid="1SA 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 4:2" />Akem mbon Filistia etịm udịmekọñ ammọ nọ ekesoobo ye Isrel, ñko naña ekọñ akaiso atara, mbon Filistia emaekan nditọ Isrel, ewot awo ñkpọ nte ikie inaañ (400) ke ikọdekọñ. <verse eid="1SA 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 4:3" />Ke ini mbon ekọñ etịmmeke enyọñ itie nnaaekọñ ammọ, mme ñkpisọñ ke Isrel ebịp ebo, “Nsoo inam yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anam nọ mbon Filistia ikan ñnyịn ntom? Yak ikaa Silo ikiben akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> nọ anye adisaña ye ñnyịn inyaaña ñnyịn asio ke ubọk mme asua ñnyịn.”<verse eid="1SA 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 4:4" />Ke ntoro, ibon ado emaesio ideen edọñ nnọ ekaa Silo, ekeben akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan, anye a-atieghe ke ufọọd mme serubim. Ñko nditọ ideen Elai iba, Họfni ye Finehas, mmọdo ekeba do ye akebe edioomo Abasi.<verse eid="1SA 4:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 4:5" />Ke ini akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akediighe itie nnaaekọñ, afịd Isrel emaesio ñkpo ekamba-ekamba tutu isọñ anyeghe. <verse eid="1SA 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 4:6" />Ke adikop ñkpoyo, mbon Filistia emaebịp ebo, “Nsoo iben afịd uyom ami idi ke itie nnaaekọñ mme Hibru?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 4:6">Ke ammọ ekoppo ke akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adʌk adi itie nnaaekọñ, <verse eid="1SA 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 4:7" />idem amaanyeñ mbon Filistia. Ammọ emaebo, “abasi<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido Mme Abasi e-edi</char></note> a-adi nnaaekọñ. Ñnyịn imitak! Utọ ñkpọ anyem kpaanaanam itịppeke akpa. <verse eid="1SA 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 4:8" />Ñnyịn imitak! Anie awo idiifak ñnyịn isio ke ubọk mme ñkpọsọñ abasi ami? Ammọ edo mme abasi ekenọọhọ nditọ Iyib mme unọmọ ke utọ ke utọ ke anaan. <verse eid="1SA 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 4:9" />Isọñ idem, ndufo mbon Filistia! Edoñño ideen, imiidooho ntoro ndufo ediido ifʌn enọọ mbon Hibru, naña ammọ ekedo inọọ ndufo. Idoñño ideen enyʌñ enwana ekọñ!”<verse eid="1SA 4:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 4:10" />Ke ntoro, mbon Filistia emaenwana ekọñ enyʌñ ekan nditọ Isrel, ndin afịd awo enyʌñ efeeñe enyọñọ atayad ammọ. Uwot awo amaanekke akpon; mbon ekọñ Isrel tọsịn edịb mme duob (30,000) eketak. <verse eid="1SA 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 4:11" />Emaebọ akebe edioomo Abasi, ñko nditọ Elai naña iba, Họfni ye Finehas emaekpañña.<verse eid="1SA 4:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkpa Elai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 4:12" />Kpasʌk usen ado awo ubon Benyamin amaasiak itọk tọọñọ ke iso ekọñ akesịm Silo ye ñwaiya afọn ye ntọñ ke iwuod. <verse eid="1SA 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 4:13" />Ke anye asịmme, Elai mmọdo aketie ke ñkpọitie ke mben usʌñ ase, sia adooho idem amaanyeñ anye ke ntak akebe edioomo Abasi. Ke ini awo ami adʌkkọ idʌñ atañ se itịppe, afịd idʌñ emaetọọñọ aditua.<verse eid="1SA 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 4:14" />Elai amaakop akpọsọñ ayịd ado anyʌñ abịp abo, “Nsoo ido ntak ñkpoyo ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 4:14">Ete ado amaasọp akanna abịne Elai, <verse eid="1SA 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 4:15" />Elai akedo isua anaañ mme duob mme itiaita ndin anyen amọ amaakịm ndin anye ikikanna imọọnọ ñkpọ. <verse eid="1SA 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 4:16" />Anye amaabo Elai, “Ami nto udịmekọñ ndi idaha ado; ami nto do mfeghe ndi usen mfịn.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 4:16">Elai amaabịp anye abo, “Ayịn mmi nsoo ñkpọ ido?”<verse eid="1SA 4:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 4:17" />Ete a-akebenne etob ado adi amaabọọrọ abo, “Isrel emaefeeñe ke iso mbon Filistia, ndin e-ekan mbon ekọñ ñnyịn, mbon ñnyịn e-enyʌñ enekke ekpañña. Ñko nditọ mfo iba, Họfni ye Finehas, ekpañña, enyʌñ ebọ akebe edioomo Abasi.”<verse eid="1SA 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 4:18" />Ke ini anye atañña ikọ akesiak akebe edioomo Abasi, Eli amaadiañña ke ñkpọitie amọ aduọ edem-edem ke mben inuaatob. Itọñ amaabʌññọ anye, anye anyʌñ akpa, sia adooho anye akedo akaanadeen, ñko anye amaadoppo. Anye amaadat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">amaakpe ikpe</char></note> Isrel usʌñ ke isua aba.<verse eid="1SA 4:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 4:19" />Anwaan ayịn amọ, anwaan Finehas, akesaña ye idịb ndin amaakpere ini uman amọ. Ke ini anye akoppo ke e-eben akebe edioomo Abasi ñko ke ete ebe amọ ye ebe amọ emaekpañña, uman amaatọọñọ anye inikeed-inikeed; anye amaaman ayịn ado ubiakuman amaakan anye ubọk. <verse eid="1SA 4:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 4:20" />Ke anye ayemme ikpa, ibaan e-ekebaaha ye anye emaebo, “Kuukop mmemidem ke afo ameman ayịn.” Ado anye ikibọọrọke inyʌññọ inọ ñkpañutọñ.<verse eid="1SA 4:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 4:21" />Anye amaasio ayịn ado anyịñ Ikabọd, anyʌñ abo, “Ubọọñ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ikabọd awuọñọ ubọọñ ibaaha</char></note> amaakpọñ Isrel” ato ke ntak ebenne akebe edioomo Abasi ye ke ntak ñkpa ete ebe ye ebe amọ. <verse eid="1SA 4:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 4:22" />Anye amaabo, “Uku akpọñ Isrel sia eben akebe edioomo Abasi.”<verse eid="1SA 4:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="1SA 5" />
  <para style="s1">Akebe Edioomo ke Asdọd ye ke Ekrọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 5:1" />Ke mbon Filistia emaekeben akebe edioomo Abasi, ammọ emaeben anye ekpọñ Ebenesa ekenịm ke Asdọd. <verse eid="1SA 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 5:2" />Akem mbon Filistia emaedịppe akebe edioomo Abasi ado ekaa tembịd Dakọn enyʌñ ekenịm ekpere Dakọn. <verse eid="1SA 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 5:3" />Ke ini mbon Asdọd ekedemmeke idab edem usen, Dakọn amaaduọ akʌp iso ke isọñ ke iso akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>! Ammọ emaedịppe Dakọn enịm ke itie amọ. <verse eid="1SA 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 5:4" />Ado ubakusen edemusen ke ammọ emaekedemme, sese Dakọn anaaha mmi amaaduọ akʌp iso ke isọñ ke iso akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>! Iwuod ye ubọk amọ amaakpịkke akena ke itie mbio; sʌk idem ikpọọñ akesʌhọ. <verse eid="1SA 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 5:5" />Ntak ado anam tutu mfịn mme aku me mbon mfen ndomokeed e-edʌkkọ tembịd Dakọn ke Asdọd e-edotto ukod ke inuausʌñ ibaaha.<verse eid="1SA 5:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 5:6" />Ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakpon ke atu mbon Asdọd ye ñkanñkʌk amọ; anye amaaben nsobo asʌk amọ anyʌñ atọ ammọ inia. <verse eid="1SA 5:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 5:7" />Ke ini mbon awo ke Asdọd ekekịtte se ikitịppe, ammọ emaebo, “Inaaha akebe edioomo Abasi Isrel aba ye ñnyịn mi, sia ubọk amọ asọọñ ye ñnyịn ye abasi ñnyịn Dakọn.” <verse eid="1SA 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 5:8" />Ke ntoro ammọ emaekoot afịd mme andikara ke Filistia enyʌñ ebịp ammọ ebo, “Nsoo ke ñnyịn ikpinam ye akebe edioomo Abasi Isrel?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 5:8">Ammọ emaebọọrọ ebo, “Yak isio akebe edioomo Abasi Isrel inyọñ Kad.” Ke ntoro ammọ emaedịppe akebe edioomo Abasi Isrel esio.<verse eid="1SA 5:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 5:9" />Ado ke ammọ emaekedịppe anye isio, ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadoro abio ado ke idem, anam ammọ ediba ke ataa ñnyeñidem. Anye amaanọ mbon abio ado inia, ikpọ ye ntək. <verse eid="1SA 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 5:10" />Ammọ ndin emaeben akebe edioomo Abasi ekaa Ekrọn.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 5:10">Idaha esʌkkọ eben akebe edioomo Abasi esaña edʌk Ekrọn, mbon awo ke Ekrọn emaesio ñkpo ebo “Ammọ eben akebe edioomo Abasi Isrel esaña ikpere ñnyịn nọ adiwot ñnyịn ye mbon ñnyịn.” <verse eid="1SA 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 5:11" />Ke ntoro ammọ emaekoot afịd mme andikara ke Filistia atọ keed enyʌñ ebo, “Isio akebe edioomo Abasi Isrel ifep ke atu ñnyịn; yak anye atịmme anyọñ aka itie amọ, imiidooho anye ayaiwoot ñnyịn ye afịd ufọk ñnyịn.” Sia adooho ñkpa amaasịn ñnyeñidem ke abio; ubọk Abasi amaanekke akpon ke abio. <verse eid="1SA 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 5:12" />Mbon se imiikikpaaha emaenie unọmọ ndufuud, aseeme abio ado amaadọọk akaa anyọñ.<verse eid="1SA 5:12" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="1SA 6" />
  <para style="s1">Eben Akebe Edioomo Abasi Etịmme Esọk Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 6:1" />Ke ini akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakeba ke ñkanñkʌk Filistia ñkpọ nte afiọñ itiaba, <verse eid="1SA 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 6:2" />mbon Filistia emaekoot mme aku ye mbiaidiọñ enyʌñ ebịp ammọ, “Nsoo ke ñnyịn idiinam ye akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>? Idọkkọ ñnyịn naña ñnyịn idiinọ anye atịmme aka itie amọ.”<verse eid="1SA 6:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 6:3" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ ebo, “Adieke ndufo ediinam akebe edioomo abasi Isrel atịmme anyọñ, ikiiyak anye atịmme anyọñ ubọk-ubọk; idomo ke afịd usʌñ adinọ anye uwa ndudue. Ndin ndufo eyaekop nsọñidem, enyʌñ ediọọñọ ntak ubọk amọ idiidịppeke ikpọñ ndufo.”<verse eid="1SA 6:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 6:4" />Mbon Filistia emaebịp, “Nsoo utọ uwa ndudue ke ñnyịn ikpinọọ esọk anye?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 6:4">Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Akpasak kold ition ye ekpu kold ition, akeene ibad mme andikara Filistia, sia ukem unọmọ ado imʌm ndufo ye mme adaiwuod ndufo. <verse eid="1SA 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 6:5" />Inam ubobod akpasak ye ubobod ekpu e-ebiada afịd abio, inyʌñ inọ Abasi Isrel ubọọñ. Akemeido anye ayaabenne ubọk amọ asio ikpọñ ndufo ye mme abasi ndufo ye isọñ ndufo. <verse eid="1SA 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 6:6" />Ntak a-ndufo esọññọ esịd naña nditọ Iyib ye Fero ekenam-a? Ke ini Abasi Isrel akenamma akpọsọñ ñkpọ ke atu ammọ, nte ammọ ikisioho nditọ Isrel ibo enyọñọ nọ ammọ ekaa usʌñ ammọ?”<verse eid="1SA 6:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 6:7" />“Idahami ndin, ndufo iben ufa ukpadñkpọ, isịn umanenañ iba e-enieghe ñyịn ammiiwuọhọ ke eba inyʌññọ inam utom akpa. Itobo umanenañ ado idian ke ukpadñkpọ, ado ikoono mme ñyịn ammọ ikidọñ ke abaenañ. <verse eid="1SA 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 6:8" />Iben akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> idot ke ukpadñkpọ ado, ñko ke etək akebe ukpadñkpọ a-asịneke ke esịd isịn mme ñkpọ kold ado a-ndufo eyemme edinọ esọk anye nte ñkpọ uwa ndudue. Ndin isaana anye iyaak nọ anyọñ, <verse eid="1SA 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 6:9" />ado ikaa iso ise anye. Adieke anye adọọhọ anyọñ aka adaña amọ, ke ñkañ Bed Semes, awuọñọ ke ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inam ñnyịn ekamba ukuud ami. Ado adieke anye imiidọọhọ, ndin ñnyịn iyaidiọọñọ ke ikidooho ubọk amọ ado ke ñkpọ ami akekookoi inam ñnyịn.”<verse eid="1SA 6:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 6:10" />Ndin amọ emaenam ntom. Ammọ emaeben umanenañ iba etobo ke ukpadñkpọ enyʌñ ediañña nditọ ammọ ekesịn ke afe. <verse eid="1SA 6:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 6:11" />Ammọ emaedot akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ukpadñkpọ, enyʌñ edot akebe a-asịneke ubobod ekpu kold mme ekpu ye ubobodñkpọ ndufuud. <verse eid="1SA 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 6:12" />Ndin mme enañ ado emaedọọk ekaa ke usʌñ a-akaaha Bed Semes, ammọ emaesaña ke akpọusʌñ, esaña emai; ammọ ikiwakkake ufiin me nnasia. Mme andikara ke Filistia emaekeene ammọ tutu ekewuọ adaña Bed Semes.<verse eid="1SA 6:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 6:13" />Idaha ntoro, nditọ Bed Semes ekesʌk edọk abakpa ke itịkke, ndin ke ammọ edịppeke anyen ekịt akebe edioomo ado ammọ emaekop inemesịd adikịt. <verse eid="1SA 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 6:14" />Ukpadñkpọ ado akedʌk inwañ Yọsua ke Bed Semes, ndin do anye aketre ke mben ekamba itiad. Mme awo emaekpok eto ukpadñkpọ ado enyʌñ ekama enañ ado enam ufọfọb uwa enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 6:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 6:15" />Mme mbon Lifai emaedooro akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye ekamba akʌbọ ukʌb akebe se ikidọñọ mme kold enyʌñ edot ammọ ke anyọñ ekamba itiad. Ke usen ado mme mbon Bed Semes emaewa ufọfọb uwa enyʌñ enam mme uwa enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> <verse eid="1SA 6:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 6:16" />Mme andikara ition ke Filistia emaekịt mme ñkpọ ami, ndin kpa usen ado ammọ emaetịmme enyọñ Ekrọn.<verse eid="1SA 6:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 6:17" />Mme akpasak ake mbon Filistia ekedọññọ nte ñkpọ uwa ndudue enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> edo ami, keedekeed anie Asdọd, Kasa, Askelọn, Kad ye Ekrọn <verse eid="1SA 6:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 6:18" />Ñko ibad ekpu kold ado akekeene ibad idʌñ ke Filistia a-anieghe mme adaukara ition ado, mme idʌñ e-ekpemeke ye mme abio inwañ ammọ. Ekamba itiad ake mme Lifai ekedotto akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aba nte ntiense tutu usen mfịn ke inwañ Yọsua ake Bed Semes.<verse eid="1SA 6:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 6:19" />Ado Abasi amaawot usʌk mbon se ikidʌñọ ke Bed Semes, awot ammọ awo ata mme duob sia ammọ ekeseeghe akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Mbon awo emaefʌhọ ke ntak ekamba eta ufen <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akemiaha ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 6:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 6:20" />Ñko nditọ Bed Semes emaebịp ebo, “Anie ikpikan ida ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, adisana Abasi ami? Anie ke akebe edioomo ami adiibịne?”<verse eid="1SA 6:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 6:21" />Do ke ammọ ekedọñ mme isʌñutom enọ mbon Kiriad Yerịm, ebo, “Mbon Filistia e-esaana akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> eyaak. Idi idiben anye inyọñ idʌñ ndufo.”<verse eid="1SA 6:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="1SA 7" />
  <para style="nb">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 7:1" />Ke ntoro ke mbon Kiriad Yerịm ekediben akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ammọ emaeben edinịm ke ufọk Abinadab ke anyọñ abod emaenyʌñ esio Eliasa ayịn amọ ebo yak atie akpeme akebe edioomo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado. <verse eid="1SA 7:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 7:2" />Akebe edioomo ado amaaba ke Kiriad Yerịm akpeene, ke afịd isua edịb.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="1SA 7:2">Samwel Akan Mbon Filistia ke Mispa</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 7:2">Ndin afịd nditọ Isrel emaetịmme edem ekeene <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 7:3" />Ke ntoro, Samwel amaabo afịd nditọ Isrel, “Adieke ndufo etịmmeke ekeene <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke afịd esịd ndufo, ana ndufo esio idem ekpọñ mme asen abasi ye mme Astọred enyʌñ eyaak idem ndufo enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enyʌñ ekpono anye ikpọọñ, ndin anye ayainyaaña ndufo asio ke ubọk mbon Filistia.” <verse eid="1SA 7:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 7:4" />Ke ado, nditọ Isrel etoomo mme Baal ye mme Astọred ammọ eduọñọ, enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikpọọñ.<verse eid="1SA 7:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 7:5" />Ndin Samwel amaabo, “Ikoot afịd Isrel ibok ke Mispa, ndin ami ñyaakpe <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ubọk ke iwuod ndufo.” <verse eid="1SA 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 7:6" />Ke ammọ emaekeboho ke Mispa, ammọ emaekoi mmọọñ eduọk ke isọñ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ke usen ado, amọ emaetie utreudia, emaenyʌñ ekeyaara ndiọiñkpọ ammọ ete, “Ñnyịn iminam idiọọkñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.” Idahami, Samwel akenam utom nte adadusʌñ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7:6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">abiideikpe</char></note> Isrel ke Mispa.<verse eid="1SA 7:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 7:7" />Ke ini mbon Filistia ekekoppo ke Isrel emaeboho ke Mispa, mme andikara ke Filistia emaedakka ekaa adinwana ye ammọ. Ke ini nditọ Isrel ekekoppo, idem amaanyeñ ammọ ke ntak nditọ Filistia. <verse eid="1SA 7:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 7:8" />Mbon Isrel emaebo Samwel, “Kuutre aditua nnọọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyịn unọọ ñnyịn, yak anye inyaaña ñnyịn asio ke ubọk mbon Filistia.” <verse eid="1SA 7:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 7:9" />Ndin Samwel amaaben ñyịn edọñ a-asʌkkọ awọp eba anyʌñ akenam ayọhọ ufọfọb uwa anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Anye amaatua anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke iwuod nditọ Isrel, ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ anye.<verse eid="1SA 7:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 7:10" />Ke Samwel asʌkkọ anam ufọfọb uwa ado, mbon Filistia emaesaña ekpere adinwana ekọñ ye Isrel. Ado ke usen ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaatop nte akpọsọñ aduma ye mbon Filistia anyʌñ anam idem anyeñ ammọ tutu ammọ efeeñe ke iso nditọ Isrel. <verse eid="1SA 7:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 7:11" />Mme ideen ke Isrel emaefeeñe ewuọ ke Mispa enyʌñ ebịne mbon Filistia, ewoot ammọ ke usʌñ tutu ekesịm itie ke idak Bed Kaa.<verse eid="1SA 7:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 7:12" />Ndin Samwel amaaben itiad anịm ke ufọọd Mispa ye Sen. Anye amaakoot itie ado Ebenesa,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ebenesa awuọñọ itiad unwam</char></note> ate “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inyaaña ñnyịn adiwuọ idahami.”<verse eid="1SA 7:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 7:13" />Ndin emaekan mbon Filistia ammọ emaenyʌñ etre edisidʌk idʌñ Isrel. Ke afịd ayio uwem Samwel, ubọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanwana ye mbon Filistia. <verse eid="1SA 7:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 7:14" />Mme abio tọọñọ ke Ekrọn tutu asịm Kad ake mbon Filistia ekebọọhọ Isrel emaeyaak enọ Isrel, ñko Isrel emaenyʌñ efakka mme ñkanñkʌk idʌñ ammọ esio ke ubọk mbon Filistia. Ndin emem amaaba ke ufọọd Isrel ye mbon Amọọ.<verse eid="1SA 7:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 7:15" />Samwel amaakaa iso ado adaiwuod ke Isrel ke afịd ayio uwem amọ. <verse eid="1SA 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 7:16" />Ke isua ke isua anye amaasaña akanna abio atọọñọ ke Beteel akesịm Kilkal akesịm Mispa, akpe ikpe anọ Isrel ke afịd mme itie ado. <verse eid="1SA 7:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 7:17" />Ado anye amaasitịmme anyọñ Rama, itie u-ufọk amọ akebaaha, do ñko anye amaanie esob anọ Isrel. Anye amaabọp akpokoro uwa anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> do.<verse eid="1SA 7:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="1SA 8" />
  <para style="s1">Isrel Ayem Adidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 8:1" />Adikem ke Samwel amaakesọñ, anye amaasio ayịn amọ awodeen nte adadusʌñ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">mme abiideikpe</char></note> ke Isrel. <verse eid="1SA 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 8:2" />Akpa ayịn ammọ akekere Yuel ndin udiana akekere Abiya, ammọ ekenyʌñ enam utom ke Beeseba. <verse eid="1SA 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 8:3" />Ado nditọ ideen amọ ikikeeneke usʌñ amọ. Ammọ emaewakka ekeene idiọọk udod enyʌñ ebọ ubọkedem enyʌñ ekpe ukwañ ikpe.<verse eid="1SA 8:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 8:4" />Akem afịd mme ñkpisọñ ke Isrel emaeboho itie keed enyʌñ edika ebịne Samwel ke Rama. <verse eid="1SA 8:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 8:5" />Ammọ emaekebo anye, “Afo amesọñ, ñko nditọ mfo ikeeneke usʌñ mfo; ke ntoro, sio adidem inọ ñnyịn nọ idat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">abiideikpe; se ñko ke 1 Sa 8:6 ye 20</char></note> ñnyịn usʌñ, kpa naña mme idịd mfen enie.”<verse eid="1SA 8:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 8:6" />Ado ini a-ammọ ekebooho, “Inọ ñnyịn adidem yak idat ñnyịn usʌñ,” ado ikinemme Samwel esịd; ke ntak ado anye amaabọñ akam anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 8:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 8:7" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo Samwel: “Kpañ utọñ kop afịd se mme awo ami ubo fiin; idooho afo ke ammọ esịn ado ammọ ensịn miin nte adidem ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 8:8" />Kpa naña ammọ ekenam tọọñọ ke usen ami ñkesioho ammọ ke isọñ Iyib tutu adiwuọ usen mfịn, ekaiso ensịn miin ekekpono mme abasi mfen, ntoro ke ammọ enam ye afo. <verse eid="1SA 8:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 8:9" />Idahami kpañ utọñ nọ ammọ; ado nekke dʌt ammọ utọñ nyʌñ nam nọ ammọ ediọọñọ se adidem a-adiikara ammọ adiidat nte unen imọ.”<verse eid="1SA 8:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 8:10" />Samwel amaatañ afịd ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anọ afịd mbon e-ekebịppe anye ebaña adidem. <verse eid="1SA 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 8:11" />Anye amaabo ammọ, “Se adidem a-adiikara ndufo adiiyem nte unen amọ ado ami: Anye ayaakoono nditọ ideen ndufo anam ammọ enam utom ye mme sariọd ye mme enañmbakara amọ, ndin ammọ eyaefeeñe ke iso mme sariọd amọ. <verse eid="1SA 8:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 8:12" />Anye ayaanam usʌk ammọ edoñño mme adaiso ekọñ ke atu mme tọsịn (1,000) ye usʌk mme adaiso ekọñ ke atu mme aba mme duob, ñko usʌk eyaefʌñ isọñ amọ enyʌñ edọk idọk inwañ amọ, ndin usʌk eyaedo mme anam ñkpọ ekọñ amọ ye ukwak sariọd amọ. <verse eid="1SA 8:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 8:13" />Anye ayaaben nditọ ibaan ndufo anam edoñño mbon se iyet awo inem ufịk adan ye mme atem ndidia ye mbon unam ndomuyo. <verse eid="1SA 8:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 8:14" />Anye ayaaben inwañ ndufo se ifọọn ikan ye inwañ fain ye inwañ ọlif anyʌñ ayaak anọ nsaña amọ. <verse eid="1SA 8:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 8:15" />Anye ayaaben mbaak keed ke itie duob ke mme abakpa ye mme inwañ fain ndufo anọ mme adaaha ye nsaña amọ. <verse eid="1SA 8:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 8:16" />Anye ayaaben mme nditọufọk ndufo ideen ye ibaan ye nti enañ ndufo se ifọọn ikan ye mme dọñki ndufo adat anọ idem amọ. <verse eid="1SA 8:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 8:17" />Anye ayaaben keed ke mbaak duob ufene ndufo, ñko ndufo ke idem ndufo eyaekappa edoñño ifʌn enọ anye. <verse eid="1SA 8:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 8:18" />Ke usen ado amaadisịm, ndufo eyaetua eyem ubọkkọ ke ubọk adidem a-ndufo ekemekke mi, ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> idiibọọrọke ndufo ke usen ado.”<verse eid="1SA 8:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 8:19" />Ado mme awo emaesịn adikpañ utọñ nnọ Samwel. Ammọ emaebo, “Iyoo! Ñnyịn iyem adidem adikara ñnyịn. <verse eid="1SA 8:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 8:20" />Ndin ñnyịn iyaiba nte mme idịd mfen, inie adidem se idat ñnyịn usʌñ inyʌñ isiboiyo iso ekọñ ikinwana inọọ ñnyịn.”<verse eid="1SA 8:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 8:21" />Ke ini Samwel amaakekop afịd se mbon awo eketañ, anye amaaben akedọkkọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 8:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 8:22" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ anye abo, “Kpañ utọñ nọ ammọ ñnyʌñ nọ amọ adidem.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 8:22">Ndin Samwel amaabo nditọ Isrel, “Afịd awo itịmme inyʌñ isọñ idʌñ ndufo.”<verse eid="1SA 8:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="1SA 9" />
  <para style="s1">Samwel Ayet Sọọl Adan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 9:1" />Amaaba awo ke ubon Benyamin, awuọiso awo, anyịñ amọ akedo Kisi ayịn Abiel, ayịn Serọ, ayịn Bekorad, ayịn Afia ake ubon Benyamin. <verse eid="1SA 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 9:2" />Kisi amaanie ayịn awodeen a-anyịñ ammọ akedooho Sọọl, anye akedo uyaiya akparawa ekpekịtte ke Isrel, ñko anye amaanyọọñ anyan akan awo mfen.<verse eid="1SA 9:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 9:3" />Akem mme dọñki e-ekenieghe Kisi, ete Sọọl, emaesoomo, ndin Kisi amaanyʌñ abo Sọọl ayịn awodeen amọ, “Ben ayịnufọk keed yak asaña ye afo ekeyem mme dọñki esoppo do.” <verse eid="1SA 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 9:4" />Ke ntoro anye amaadakka asaña ukañ abod-abod abioinwañ a-abaaha ke idʌñ Ifrem ye ñkañ Salisa, ado ammọ ikikịtte mme dọñki ado. Ammọ emaesaña ekaa ñkañ Saalim, ado mme dọñki ado ikibaaha do. Akem ammọ emaesaña eboiyo ubeñ isọñ idʌñ Benyamin, ado ammọ ikisʌkkọ ikekịt mme dọñki ado.<verse eid="1SA 9:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 9:5" />Ke ini ammọ ekesịmme abio Suuf, Sọọl amaabo ayịnufọk a-akesañake ye anye ate, “Di, yak ñnyịn itịmme inyọñ imiidooho ete mmi ayaakpọñ adifịna mbaña mme dọñki akappa afịna ibaña ñnyịn.”<verse eid="1SA 9:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 9:6" />Ado ayịnufọk amaabọọrọ, “Awo Abasi keed aba ke idʌñ ami; anye anekke anie ukpono, ñko afịd se anye atañ asiwuọ asu. Yak ñnyịn ika do idahami. Akemeido anye ayaidọkkọ ñnyịn itie nte ikpikaa.”<verse eid="1SA 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 9:7" />Sọọl amaabo ayịnufọk amọ, “Ñnyịn ikpikaa, nsoo ke ñnyịn idiinọ ete ado? Ndidia akweeñe ke ekpad ñnyịn. Ñnyịn inieghe enọ se iben isọk awo Abasi ado. Nsoo ke ñnyịn inie?”<verse eid="1SA 9:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 9:8" />Ayịnufọk amaamaana abọọrọ anye Sọọl abo, “Sese ami mmenie keed ke mbaak inaañ sekel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9:8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kram 3</char></note> silfa. Ami ñyaayaak nnọ awo Abasi nọ anye idọkkọ ñnyịn nte ñnyịn idiidʌk.” <verse eid="1SA 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 9:9" />Ke ini akpa akesido ke Isrel, adieke awo akaaha adikibịp nto Abasi, ammọ ekesibo, “Idi, yak ñnyịn ikibịp akịdñkukịd,” sia ekesikoot mme prọfed ayio ado mme akịdñkukịd.<verse eid="1SA 9:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 9:10" />Sọọl amaabo ayịnufọk amọ, “A-afọn. Di yak ika.” Ke ntoro ammọ emaedaaña ekaa abio a-awo Abasi ado akebaaha.<verse eid="1SA 9:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 9:11" />Naña ammọ ekesʌkkọ esaña edọọk abod eka abio ado, ammọ emaekịt mme ubọikpa nte ewuọñọ edibọ mmọọñ, ammọ emaebịp ammọ, “Nte akịdñkukịd a-aba mi.”<verse eid="1SA 9:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 9:12" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Anye mmọdo. Anye akaa ako ke iso ndufo. Isọsọp idem ke anye adisʌk ndi idʌñ ñnyịn adodo, sia adooho mbon awo enie uwa adinam ke ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie. <verse eid="1SA 9:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 9:13" />Ndufo emaesʌk edọdʌk abio, ndufo eyaekịt anye mbemiso anye adọọk akaa ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie adidia ñkpọ. Mme awo idiitọọñọke edidia ñkpọ tutu anye adi, sia adooho ana anye adiọñ uwa ado; ado amaaboiyo, mbon e-ekekoodo eyaedia. Ndufo idọọk ikaa idahami; akpenam ndufo eyaekịt anye udomo ini ami.”<verse eid="1SA 9:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 9:14" />Ammọ emaedọọk edʌk abio, ke ammọ esʌkkọ edʌk eka, se Samwel mi, naña asasaña abịne ammọ adidọọk ñkaa ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie.<verse eid="1SA 9:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 9:15" />Ado mbemiso usen Sọọl akediighe, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayayaara awọt Samwel: <verse eid="1SA 9:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 9:16" />“Udomo ini ami ñkpọñ adiisiere mi, ami ñyaadọñ awo a-atooho isọñ Benyamin yak ubịne fiin. Yet anye adan nte andikara mbon mmi Isrel; anye ayaanyaaña ammọ asio ke ubọk mbon Filistia. Ami mmese mbon mmi, sia ntua ayịd ammọ adọọk adinsịm miin.”<verse eid="1SA 9:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 9:17" />Ke ini Samwel akekannake anyen akịt Sọọl, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadọkkọ anye abo, “Se awo ami ñketañña mbaña mmi; anye ayaakara ikọd mmi.”<verse eid="1SA 9:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 9:18" />Sọọl amaasaña akpere Samwel ke usʌñ inuaatob akebịp, “Mbọk akpandọkkọ miin nte ufọk akịdñkukịd aba?”<verse eid="1SA 9:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 9:19" />Samwel amaabọọrọ Sọọl, “Ami ndo akịdñkukịd,” “Tọọñọ dọọk sañ ke ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie, sia ana afo adia ñkpọ ye ami mfịn, ndin ubakusen ami ñyausio fiin unyọñ ñnyʌñ udọkkọ afịd se usịne fiin ke esịd. <verse eid="1SA 9:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 9:20" />Amaado mme dọñki e-ekesoomoke ke usen ita a-akeboiyoke ko, kuufịna idem ubaña ammọ; emaekịt ammọ. Ñko anie ke idodanyen Isrel awʌhọ ke imiidooho afo ye afịd ekpək ndufo?”<verse eid="1SA 9:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 9:21" />Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Nte ami ntooho ubon Benyamin, andisịb ñkan ke esiin Isrel, ñko idooho ubon ñnyịn asịp akan ke afịd esiin Benyamin? Ntaha afo atañña utọ ikọ ado ye ami-e?”<verse eid="1SA 9:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 9:22" />Akem Samwel amaaben Sọọl ye ayịnufọk amọ adʌk adi esịd afe anyʌñ adinam ammọ etie iwuod enọ afịd mbon se ekekoot, e-ekedooho edịb mme duob ke ibad. <verse eid="1SA 9:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 9:23" />Samwel amaakoot atem ndidia abo, “Ben unam anye ami ñkunọọhọ fiin do di, anye ami ñkubooho fiin yak asio anịm asaña-asaña.”<verse eid="1SA 9:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 9:24" />Akem atem ndidia amaaben ifʌkkọ unam ye abʌk se ikiyịre adinịm Sọọl ke iso. Samwel amaabo ate, “Se ekenịm unọọ fiin adom. Dia, sia ekesio anye ami enịm unọ fiin ke usọrọ ami tọọñọ ke ini ami ñkebooho, ‘mmekoot mme isenawo.’ ” Ndin Sọọl amaadia ñkpọ ye Samwel usen ado.<verse eid="1SA 9:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 9:25" />Ke ammọ emaekesọiyọ ke ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie idi abio, Samwel amaaneme nneme ye Sọọl ke anyọñ ufọk amọ. <verse eid="1SA 9:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 9:26" />Ammọ emaedakka eda ke usiere, ndin Samwel amaada ke anyọñ ufọk akoot Sọọl ate, “Beeñe idem ndin ami ñyausio fiin unyọñ.” Ke ini Sọọl akebeeñeke idem ama, anye amaasaña keed ye Samwel awuọ esiin. <verse eid="1SA 9:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 9:27" />Ke ammọ esʌkkọ esaña ekewuọ utịd abio, Samwel amaabo Sọọl, “Bo ayịnufọk mfo yak asaña aka iso ikpọñ ñnyịn,” ayịnufọk amaanyʌñ anam ntoro, “ado afo ba mi ke etək ini, nọ ami udọkkọ fiin etob a-atooho Abasi.”<verse eid="1SA 9:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="1SA 10" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 10:1" />Ndin Samwel amaaben ekpeme adan ọlif aduọk Sọọl ke iwuod anyʌñ atịm anye inua abo, “Nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> uyette fiin adan ibo ado andikara anọ udeeme amọ? <verse eid="1SA 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 10:2" />Afo umauñkpọñ miin mfịn ami, afo ayaakịt ideen iba ke ñkpere udi Ratiel, ke Selsa ke adaña Benyamin. Ammọ eyaubo fiin, ‘Mme dọñki afo akekaaha adiyem, emaekịt. Ñko idahami ete mfo atre adikere mbana ammọ akappa ayeeme nsia ubaña fiin.’ ” Anye abo, “Ndiinam die mbaña ayịn awodeen mmi?”<verse eid="1SA 10:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 10:3" />“Ndin afo ayaakaa iso asaña tutu afo akesịm itie ekamba eto Tabọ. Ideen ita e-edọọhọ eka edikpono Abasi ke Beteel eyausoobo fiin do. Keed adiikama ñyịn ebod ita, mfen akama uyo ita, keed ako akama atu ukọd. <verse eid="1SA 10:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 10:4" />Ammọ eyaukọọm fiin enyʌñ unọ fiin uyo iba, afo ayaabọ ammọ.”<verse eid="1SA 10:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 10:5" />“Ke ado amaaboiyo, afo ayaakaa Kibie ake Abasi, i-itie ukpeme mbon Filistia abaaha. Nte afo akpereke abio ado, afo ayaakịt udịm mme prọfed nte eto ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie edi ekama mme ndidoudʌk, mme ibịdubọk, mme adʌk ye mme ekpa ebre ekeene ammọ, ndin ammọ esʌk etañ prọfesi. <verse eid="1SA 10:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 10:6" />Ndin Sịbidịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaudoro fiin ke idem akpọsọñ-akpọsọñ, ndin afo ayaakeene ammọ atañ prọfesi; ñko afo ayaakappa ado awo mfen. <verse eid="1SA 10:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 10:7" />Ndin mme idiọọñọ ami emaewuọ ewọt idem, nam se adodo ake ubọk mfo atuuhọ adinam, sia Abasi mmọdo aba ye afo.”<verse eid="1SA 10:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 10:8" />“Mbem miin iso kaa Kilkal. Ke akpanikọ, ami nsʌk ndi ubịne fiin adinam ufọfọb uwa ye uwa adidiana keed, ado ana afo aba usen itiaba tutu ami ndi ubịne fiin ndudọkkọ fiin se afo adiinam.”<verse eid="1SA 10:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Enam Sọọl ado Adidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 10:9" />Adikem ke idaha Sọọl akewọññọke akpọñ Samwel, Abasi amaakpəho esịd Sọọl, ndin afịd mme idiọọñọ ado amaawuọ awọt idem usen ado. <verse eid="1SA 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 10:10" />Ke ini anye ye ayịnufọk amọ ekesịmme Kibie, udịm mme prọfed esoobo ye anye; Sịbidịd Abasi amaadoro anye ke idem ekamba-ekamba, ndin anye amaakeene ammọ atañ prọfesi. <verse eid="1SA 10:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 10:11" />Ke ini afịd mbon se imaikidọdiọọñọ anye ekekịtte anye nte atañ prọfesi, ammọ emaebịp emọ-emọ ete, “Nsoo ñkpọ itịppe ntom inọ ayịn Kisi? Nte Sọọl asịne ke atu mme prọfed?”<verse eid="1SA 10:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 10:12" />Awodeen a-akedʌññọ do amaabọọrọ, “Anie ado ete ammọ?” Ke ntoro adikappa ado ufiid: “Nte Sọọl asịne ke atu mme prọfed?” <verse eid="1SA 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 10:13" />Ke Sọọl amaaketañ prọfesi ima, anye amaadakka akaa ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie.<verse eid="1SA 10:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 10:14" />Akem ayịneka ete Sọọl amaabịp anye ye ayịnufọk amọ abo, “Ndufo ekeba ke mmọọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 10:14">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Adikiyem mme dọñki. Ado sia ñnyịn ikikịt ke awo ikikịtte ammọ, ñnyịn imaikaa ibịne Samwel.”<verse eid="1SA 10:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 10:15" />Ayịneka ete Sọọl amaabo, “Ndọkkọ se Samwel akibo ndufo.”<verse eid="1SA 10:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 10:16" />Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Anye akidọkkọ ñnyịn ke emaekịt mme dọñki.” Ado anye ikidọkkọke ayịneka ete amọ se Samwel aketañ abaña udaubọọñ amọ.<verse eid="1SA 10:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 10:17" />Samwel amaanọ nditọ Isrel ewʌhọ ate eboho ke atọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Mispa <verse eid="1SA 10:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 10:18" />amaanyʌñ abo ammọ, “Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Abasi Isrel atañ ado ami: ‘Ami ñkesio Isrel ke isọñ Iyib, ñko ami ñnyaaña ndufo nsio ke adudu Iyib ye afịd idịd e-ekifiighe ndufo.’ <verse eid="1SA 10:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 10:19" />Ado idahami ndufo emesịn Abasi ndufo, a-akinyaañake ndufo asio ke afịd ukuud ye mbaba. Ndin ndufo emebo, ‘Iyoo, mek adidem inọ ñnyịn.’ Ndin idahami, idida ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke esiin ye ubon ndufo.”<verse eid="1SA 10:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 10:20" />Ke Samwel amaakenam afịd Isrel ewuọñọ edi ke esiin ke esiin, emaekama ukañ esio ubon Benyamin edat. <verse eid="1SA 10:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 10:21" />Ndin anye amaasio esiin Benyamin adaaha ke ekpək ke ekpək, ndin emaemek ubon Matri. Ke akpatre emaemek Sọọl ayịn Kisi. Ado ke ini ekeyemme anye awo ikikịtte anye. <verse eid="1SA 10:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 10:22" />Ke ntoro, ammọ emaana ebịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> “Nte awo ado adi mmi diin?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 10:22">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanyʌñ abọọrọ, “Ii, ado anye adịbe ke atu ñkpoduoho.”<verse eid="1SA 10:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 10:23" />Ammọ emaefeghe ekesio anye edi, ndin ke ini anye akewuọhọ ada ke atu awo anye amaanyọọñ akan afịd awo se ikida. <verse eid="1SA 10:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 10:24" />Samwel amaabo afịd mbon awo, “Nte ndufo emekịt awodeen se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amek? Ibaaha awo se iba nte anye ke atu afịd mbon awo.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 10:24">Ndin mbon awo emaebọñ, “Itọñ uwem asọñ adidem!”<verse eid="1SA 10:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 10:25" />Samwel amaanam anwaña mbon awo se unen ye utom adidem ado. Anye amaawet ammọ ke ikpañwed anyʌñ anịm ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ndin Samwel amaasuan mbon awo ate enyọñ ufọk ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 10:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 10:26" />Sọọl ñko amaanyʌñ anyọñ ufọk amọ ke Kibie, asaña ye mme uko ideen ake Abasi amaaketuuk esịd ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 10:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 10:27" />Ado usʌk mme abʌd-abʌd awo emaebo, “Utọ awo ami abiinam die inyaaña ñnyịn?” Ammọ emaese anye ke ndek inyʌññọ iben enọ ndomokeed isọk anye. Ado Sọọl ikisioho uyio.<verse eid="1SA 10:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="1SA 11" />
  <para style="s1">Sọọl Anyaaña Abio Yabes</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 11:1" />Akem Nahas ayịn Amọn amaadọọk akaa akekanna Yabes Kilied akʌk nọ adiinwana ekọñ. Ñko afịd ideen Yabes emaebo anye, “Nam edioomo ye ñnyịn ndin ñnyịn iyaido ikọd mfo.”<verse eid="1SA 11:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 11:2" />Ado Nahas ayịn Amọn amaabọọrọ, “Ami ndiinyịmme adinam edioomo ye ndufo akpedo ndufo emenyịmme yak ami ikappa ndufo anyen nnasia afịd ndufo nsio nọ ato do mben ndọk nsọk afịd Isrel.”<verse eid="1SA 11:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 11:3" />Mme ñkpisọñ ke Yabes emaebo anye, “Inọ ñnyịn usen itiaba nọ ñnyịn idọñ isʌñutom etob inọ afịd Isrel; adieke awo idiibaaha se inyaaña ñnyịn, ñnyịn iyaiyaak idem unọ fiin.”<verse eid="1SA 11:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 11:4" />Ke ini asañautom adisịmme Kibie ake Sọọl anyʌñ atañ se ido anọ mme awo do, afịd mbon abio ado emaebenne uyio ammọ etua ayịd. <verse eid="1SA 11:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 11:5" />Kpa idaha ado ke Sọọl akenyọñ inwañ amọ asaña ke edem mme enañ, ndin anye abịp, “Nsoo inam afịd awo? Ntaha ammọ etuañake-e?” Ndin emaeben edọkkọ anye se ideen Yabes eketañ.<verse eid="1SA 11:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 11:6" />Ke ini Sọọl akekoppo se amọ etañ, Sịbidịd Abasi amaadoro anye ke idem ekamba-ekamba, esịd amaanekke ayat anye. <verse eid="1SA 11:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 11:7" />Anye amaaben enañ iba akpok ke mbaak ke mbaak anọ mme isʌñutom ate eben esaña ke afịd adaña Isrel etañ ebo, “Se ediinam ye mme enañ afịd awo se imiidikeeneke Sọọl ye Samwel ado ami.” Ndin uteeñe <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadoro mme awo ke idem, ammọ enyʌñ ewuọñọ edi ke esịd keed. <verse eid="1SA 11:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 11:8" />Ke ini Sọọl abatta ammọ ke Besek, ideen Isrel emaesịm tọsịn ikie ita (300,000) ñko mbon Yuda ekedo tọsịn edịb mme duob (30,000).<verse eid="1SA 11:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 11:9" />Ammọ emaebo mme isʌñutom e-ekediighe, “ibo ideen Yabes Kilied, ‘Ñkpọñ ke utịn amaasakka ndufo eyaenie adinyaaña.’ ” Ke ini mme isʌñutom ekekaaha ekedọkkọ ideen Yabes ñkpọ ami esịd amaadat ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 11:10" />Mbon Yabes emaebo mbon Amọn, “Ñkpọñ ñnyịn iyaisuuk iwuod inọ ndufo yak inam ñnyịn se ndufo ema.”<verse eid="1SA 11:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 11:11" />Edem usen ado Sọọl amaabakka mme ideen amọ ke itie ita; ke ufọọd akonayio ammọ esiaha edọñọ itie nnaaekọñ mbon Amọn enyʌñ ewot ammọ tutu utịn asakka edem usen. Mbon se ikidu uwem emaesuana, tutu awo amọ iba ibaaha itie keed.<verse eid="1SA 11:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Esọọñọ Sọọl nte Adidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 11:12" />Ndin mbon awo emaebo Samwel, “Anie awo ikibịp ibo, ‘Nte Sọọl adiido adidem ñnyịn?’ Yaak ibon ado inọ ñnyịn nọ ñnyịn iwot ammọ.”<verse eid="1SA 11:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 11:13" />Ado Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Ibaaha awo se ediiwot mfịn sia usen mfịn <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anyaaña Isrel.”<verse eid="1SA 11:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 11:14" />Ndin Samwel amaabo mbon awo, “Idi, yak ñnyịn ika Kilkal ikitịmme idemme ubọọñ ke ndo.” <verse eid="1SA 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 11:15" />Ke ntoro mme awo emaekaiya Kilkal ekenam Sọọl adidem ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Do ammọ emaenam uwa ewuana ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin Sọọl ye afịd nditọ Isrel emaenam akwa idaara.<verse eid="1SA 11:15" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="1SA 12" />
  <para style="s1">Ikọ Unyọñọ Samwel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 12:1" />Samwel amaabo afịd Isrel ate, “Ami mmaakpañ utọñ nnọ afịd se ndufo eketañ ye ami ñko mmenam adidem inọ ndufo. <verse eid="1SA 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 12:2" />Idahami ndufo emenie adidem nte adat usʌñ. Amaado ami, ami mmesọñ ñnyʌñ mfịd iwad, ñko nditọ mmi mmọ mi ye ndufo. Ami mmaado adadusʌñ ndufo tọọñọ ke uyịn mmi tutu adiwuọ usen mfịn. <verse eid="1SA 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 12:3" />Se ami ndaaha mmi. Itañ ikọ ntiense indian miin ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye mbon a-anye ayette adan. Abaakenañ anie ke ami mben kpaanam? Dọñki anie ke ami mben kpaanam? Anie ke ami ntʌk akpa? Anie ke ami mfiik? Anie ke ami mbọ ubọkedem kpaanam adibọp anyen nnọ idiọọk? Akpedo ami mmenam ndomokeed ke atu mme ñkpọ ami akpa, ñyaanam yak afọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 12:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 12:4" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Afo utʌkkọ unyʌññọ ufiik ñnyịn. Afo unyʌññọ ubọ ñnyịn ñkpọ ndomokeed ke ubọk kpaanam.”<verse eid="1SA 12:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 12:5" />Samwel amaabo ammọ, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado atie ntiense inọ ndufo, ñko mbon se anye ayet adan etie ntiense enọ usen mfịn, ke ndufo ikịtte ñkpọ ndomokeed ke ubọk mmi.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 12:5">Ammọ emaebo, “Anye ado ntiense.”<verse eid="1SA 12:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 12:6" />Ndin Samwel amaabo mme awo ate, “Ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akeyet Moses ye Erọn adan anyʌñ aben mme eteete ndufo asio ke isọñ Iyib. <verse eid="1SA 12:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 12:7" />Idahami ndin, ida mi, sia ami ñyaaben mme ñkpọ mme ñkpọ ye idiọọñọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> iwọt ndufo afịd mme ndinen utom se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akenam inọọ ndufo ye mme eteete ndufo.”<verse eid="1SA 12:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 12:8" />“Ke Yekọb amaakedʌk Iyib, ammọ emaeseeme enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> eyem unwam, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanyʌñ adọñ Moses ye Erọn, ekesioño mme eteete ndufo ke isọñ Iyib eben ammọ edinọ itie ami.<verse eid="1SA 12:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 12:9" />“Ado ammọ emaefre <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ; ke ntak ado, anye amaanyam ammọ anọ Sisera, a-akedooho adaiso mbon ekọñ Hasọ, ye ke ubọk mbon Filistia ye adidem Mọb, e-ekenwanake ekọñ ye ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 12:10" />Ammọ emaeseeme enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enyʌñ ebo, ‘Ñnyịn iminam idiọọkñkpọ; ñnyịn imiwuọ ikpọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inyʌñ ikikpono Baal ye Astọred. Ado idahami inyaaña ñnyịn isio ke ubọk mme asua ñnyịn, ndin ñnyịn iyainam ñkpọ unọ fiin.’ <verse eid="1SA 12:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 12:11" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadọñ Yerub-Baal,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">E-ekenyʌññọ ekoot Kidiọn</char></note> Barak,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ekoot Bedan</char></note> Yefta ye Samwel,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru; usʌk mme ikpañwed Septuakin ye usem Siriak ado Samsịn</char></note> ndin anye amainyaaña ndufo asio ke ubọk mme asua ndufo i-ikannake ndufo ekʌk, nọ ato do ndufo edʌñ ke ifuuro.<verse eid="1SA 12:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 12:12" />“Ado ke ini ndufo ekekịtte ke Nahas adidem mbon Amọn asʌk adi adinwana ye ndufo, ndufo emaembo miin, ‘Iyoo ñnyịn iyem adidem yak adikara ñnyịn,’ akpesʌkado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ndufo akedooho adidem ndufo. <verse eid="1SA 12:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 12:13" />Sese ndin adidem ake ndufo ekemekke, anye a-ndufo ekebeeñeke; ise do ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> i-inịm ndufo adidem ke iso. <verse eid="1SA 12:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 12:14" />Adieke ndufo ebaaha <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọọ anye enyʌñ ekop item enọọ anye inyʌññọ itre utọñ ke mme ewʌhọ amọ, ñko adieke ndufo ye adidem i-ikarake ndufo ekeeneke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ndufo, afọn! <verse eid="1SA 12:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 12:15" />Ado adieke ndufo imiidikoppo item inọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñko adieke ndufo etreke utọñ enọọ mme item, ubọk amọ ayaidoro ndufo ke idem kpa naña akedoro mme eteete ndufo.<verse eid="1SA 12:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 12:16" />“Ndufo ituak ida ndin inyʌñ ikịt mme ikpọ ñkpọ ake <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayemme inam ke iso ndufo! <verse eid="1SA 12:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 12:17" />Idooho ini idọk abakpa ado mmi? Ami ñyaaseeme nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> nte yak anye adọñ aduma ye edịm. Ndin ndufo eyaediọọñọ utọ idiọọkñkpọ a-ndufo ekenamma ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ini ndufo ekebeeñeke anye yak inọ adidem.”<verse eid="1SA 12:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 12:18" />Ndin Samwel amaakoot anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ñko kpa usen ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanam aduma asakka, edịm anyʌñ adep. Ke ntoro afịd awo emaeda ke uteeñe enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye Samwel.<verse eid="1SA 12:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 12:19" />Afịd awo emaebo Samwel, “Bọñ akam nọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mfo nọ nditọufọk mfo mbaak ñnyịn idikpañña, sia ñnyịn imidian idiọọkñkpọ ke ndiọiñkpọ ñnyịn mfen ke adiyem adidem.”<verse eid="1SA 12:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 12:20" />Samwel amaabọọrọ, “Ikiiyak idem inyeñ. Ndufo emenam afịd ndiọi ñkpọ ami; ado ikiiwọññọ ikpọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado inam ñkpọ inọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke afịd esịd ndufo. <verse eid="1SA 12:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 12:21" />Ikiiwakka ikeene mme abasi ubọk awo. Ammọ inamma ufọn ndomokeed inọ ndufo, me adinwam ndufo sia ammọ ibaaha ufọn. <verse eid="1SA 12:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 12:22" />Ke ntak akwa anyịñ amọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> idiisịnne ikọd amọ, sia adooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakop inem adinam ndufo edo ake amọ. <verse eid="1SA 12:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 12:23" />Amaado ami, nsaa mmi-o ami adinam <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> idiọọkñkpọ ke aditre ibọñ akam inọọ ndufo. Ami ñyaanyʌñ ikpeep ndufo usʌñ a-afọnnọ anyʌñ anen. <verse eid="1SA 12:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 12:24" />Ado ikịt ibo ke emebaak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> enyʌñ enam ñkpọ enọ anye ke mbuọdidem ke afịd esịd ndufo; ise utọ ikpọ ñkpọ se anye anam inọ ndufo. <verse eid="1SA 12:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 12:25" />Ado adieke ndufo ekaaha iso enam idiọọkñkpọ, eyaesobo ndufo ye adidem ndufo.”<verse eid="1SA 12:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="1SA 13" />
  <para style="s1">Samwel Asua Anọ Sọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 13:1" />Sọọl akedo isua edịb mme duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru isua edịb mme duob iwereke</char></note> idaha a-anye akedooho adidem, ndin anye amaakara Isrel ke isua aba<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru isua edịb mme aba iwereke (se ke Utom Mme Abọsịd 13:21) </char></note> mme iba.<verse eid="1SA 13:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 13:2" />Sọọl amaasio ideen tọsịn ita (3,000) ato Isrel; tọsịn iba (2,000) ekeba ye anye ke Mikmas ye ke abod a-abaaha ke Beteel, tọsịn keed (1,000) ekenyʌñ eba ye Yọnatan ke Kibie ke Benyamin. Ideen se ikiyọhọ isʌhọ, anye amaanọ etịmme enyọñọ ufọk ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 13:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 13:3" />Akem Yọnatan amaasuan mbon ekọñ nditọ Filistia ke Keba, ndin mbon Filistia emaekop ebaña. Ndin Sọọl amaafịt adukpoñ ke afịd isọñ ate yak afịd Hibru ekop! <verse eid="1SA 13:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 13:4" />Ndin afịd Isrel emaekop etob ado: “Sọọl amaasuan mbon ekọñ Filistia, Isrel idahami akedido ubiak anọ mbon Filistia.” Ñko emaekoot mbon awo yak ediana ye Sọọl ke Kilkal.<verse eid="1SA 13:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 13:5" />Mbon Filistia emaesoobo idem itie keed adinwana ye Isrel, ekama sariọd tọsịn ita (3,000), mbon uwat sariọd tọsịn itiokeed (6,000), ye mbon ekọñ e-ekewakka nte ntan a-abaaha ke mben akpainyañ. Amọ emaewuọ ekenịm nnaaekọñ ammọ ke Mikmas, ke usakkautịn Bed Afịn. <verse eid="1SA 13:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 13:6" />Ke ini Isrel ekekịtte ke mbaba mmimọ akpon ñko ke enekke efiik mbon ekọñ mmimọ, ammọ emaekedịbe ke mme abaitiad ye ke mme ikọd ñkukịm, ke ufọọd ikpọitiad ye ke ube ye ke ntotəño itie. <verse eid="1SA 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 13:7" />Usʌk mbon Hibru emaekaaña Yọdan ekaa idʌñ Kad ye Kilied.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 13:7">Sọọl akesʌk aba ke Kilkal, ñko afịd udịm se ikiba ye anye ekeba ke ñnyeñidem. <verse eid="1SA 13:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 13:8" />Anye amaabet usen itiaba, usen se Samwel akenịm anọ anye; ado Samwel ikidiighe Kilkal, ñko mme ideen Sọọl emaetọọñọ esuana. <verse eid="1SA 13:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 13:9" />Ke ntoro anye amaabo, “Iben ufọfọb uwa ye uwa ewuana insọk” Ndin Sọọl amaawa ufọfọb uwa ado. <verse eid="1SA 13:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 13:10" />Kpa idaha anye amaaha uwa ado, Samwel abiọññọ, Sọọl amaanyʌñ awuọ akekọọm anye.<verse eid="1SA 13:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 13:11" />Samwel amaabịp, “Nsoo ke afo anam?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 13:11">Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Ke ini ami ñkekịtte ke ideen mmi ekesʌk esuana, ñko ke afo ukudiighe idaha a-afo akenịmme, ñko ke mbon Filistia mmọdo ekeboho ke Mikmas, <verse eid="1SA 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 13:12" />ami mmaakere, ‘Idaha ado mbon Filistia eyaedi embịne miin ke Kilkal ñko ami ñkebọọhọ mfọn nto <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ Ke ntoro ami mmaakere ke akpena nnam ufọfọb uwa.”<verse eid="1SA 13:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 13:13" />Samwel amaabo Sọọl, “Afo amenam ndisịme ñkpọ. Afo unịmme mbed <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mfo akunọọhọ fiin; akpedo afo amaanam, anye akpaawuuk abioubọọñ mfo ke Isrel ke afịd mme ini. <verse eid="1SA 13:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 13:14" />Ado idahami, abioubọọñ mfo idiisọọñọke ida; <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> a-ayem awo ake esịd amọ amaaha anyʌñ amek anye andikara ikọd amọ, sia adooho afo unịmme ewʌhọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="1SA 13:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 13:15" />Ndin Samwel amaadakka akpọñ Kilkal anyʌñ akaa Kibie ke abio Benyamin, ñko Sọọl amaabat mbon se iba ye anye. Ammọ edo awo ikie itiokeed.<verse eid="1SA 13:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Isrel Enana Ñkpọ Ekọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 13:16" />Sọọl ye ayịn amọ Yọnatan ye mme ideen ekebaaha ye ammọ ekebañña ke Kibie<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Hibru ado Keba, asʌkkọ ado Kibie</char></note> ke abio Benyamin, ke ini mbon Filistia ekenịmme nnaaekọñ ammọ ke Mikmas. <verse eid="1SA 13:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 13:17" />Mme udịmekọñ emaewuọ ke atu mbon Filistia ke ikpeghe ita. Keed akaa ñkañ Ọfra ke ñkañ Sual. <verse eid="1SA 13:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 13:18" />Mfen amaakaa ñkañ Bed Họrọn, ñko ayọhọ ita emaedʌk utịd adaña a-aseeghe Abedeñ Seboyịm a-aseeghe anaan.<verse eid="1SA 13:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 13:19" />Awo ikikịtte adomutịm ndomokeed ke afịd isọñ Isrel, sia mbon Filistia emaebo, “Imiidooho ntoro mbon Hibru eyaenam mme akañkañ ye mme eduad!” <verse eid="1SA 13:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 13:20" />Ke ntoro afịd mbon Isrel emaekaa ebịne mbon Filistia nọ ekeban mme ukịmisọñ, mme ukwak, mme ekịd ye mme akọbọ. <verse eid="1SA 13:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 13:21" />Ekọmudua adiban ukịmisọñ ye ekịd akedo mbakka iba sekel keed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kram 8</char></note> ndin adiban nsọbọ inua ukwak akedo mbakka sekel keed ke mbaak ita<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kram 4</char></note>.<verse eid="1SA 13:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 13:22" />Ndin ke usen ekọñ baaba awo ekọñ ndomokeed a-akebaaha ye Sọọl me ye Yọnatan a-akenieghe eduad me idañ ikibaaha; sʌk Sọọl ye ayịn amọ Yọnatan ikpọọñ ekenie.<verse eid="1SA 13:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yọnatan Anwana Mbon Filistia.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 13:23" />Akem mbon Filistia emaewuọ ekaa iboiyo ke Mikmas.<verse eid="1SA 13:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="1SA 14" />
  <para style="nb">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 14:1" />Usen keed Yọnatan ayịn Sọọl amaabo akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ ate, “Di yak ñnyịn ikanna ika ñkañ mbon ekọñ Filistia ke edem uko.” Ado anye ikidọkkọke ete amọ.<verse eid="1SA 14:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 14:2" />Sọọl akeba ke edem idʌñ Kibie ke idak eto pomekrened ke Mikrọn. Mbon awo se ikiba ye anye ekedo ñkpọ nte ideen ikie itiokeed, <verse eid="1SA 14:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 14:3" />ke atu ammọ akedo Ahiya, akesịneke afọñ aboditọñ. Anye akedo ayịn ayịneka awodeen Ikabọd, Ahitub ayịn Finehas, ayịn Elai, aku <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Silo. Ibaaha awo se ikidiọọñọ ke Yọnatan amaawuọ.<verse eid="1SA 14:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 14:4" />Kwa mbeñ ukañ ake Yọnatan akeyemme adiboiyo ñkaa ñkesịm itie mbon ekọñ Filistia, ekamba ededitiad amaanaa; ekekoot keed Bọses, anye ako ekoot Sene. <verse eid="1SA 14:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 14:5" />Mbañ itiad keed akeda anọ ubeñ ñkañ edem adoro a-asakkaiso ase Mikmas, anye ako ada ke edem usuuk a-asakkaiso ase Keba.<verse eid="1SA 14:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 14:6" />Yọnatan amaabo akparawa a-akebiommo ñkpọ ekọñ amọ, “Di yak ñnyịn ifrọ ikaaña ikaa itie ekọñ ideen ake imiifọọrọke edʌd mi. Akemeido <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaanam ñkpọ ke ntak ñnyịn. Ibaaha se ikpan <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adinyaaña me adikama uwak me adikama etək-etək ñnyaaña.”<verse eid="1SA 14:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 14:7" />Akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ amaabo, “Nam afịd se usịne fiin ke esịd,” “Kaa iso; ami mmọdo ye afo ke esịd ye ke ukpọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 14:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 14:8" />Yọnatan amaabo, “Imaa, saña di yak ikiboiyo ke ubeñ ñkañ ammọ inyʌñ iyak ammọ ikịt ñnyịn. <verse eid="1SA 14:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 14:9" />Adieke ammọ ibooho ñnyịn ‘Ibet do tutu ñnyịn idi ibịne ndufo,’ ñnyịn iyaiba ke nte ñnyịn iba, idiikaaha ibịne ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 14:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 14:10" />Ado ammọ ekpebo, ‘Idi ibịne ñnyịn’ ñnyịn iyaidọọk ika sia ado adiido idiọọñọ inọ ñnyịn ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaak ammọ isịn ñnyịn ke ubọk.”<verse eid="1SA 14:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 14:11" />Ke ntoro ammọ awo iba emaewọt mbon ekọñ Filistia idem. Mbon Filistia emaebo, “Sese! Mme mbon Hibru esʌk enyọọn ewuọ ke ube ake ammọ ekedịbeke ke esịd.” <verse eid="1SA 14:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 14:12" />Ideen mbon ekọñ ado emaebọọñ ekoot Yọnatan ye akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ ebo, “Idọọk ibịne ñnyịn ndin ñnyịn iyaikpeep ndufo ñkpọ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 14:12">Ndin Yọnatan amaabo akama ñkpọ ekọñ ammọ, “Dọọk ñkene miin; <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaak ammọ asịn Isrel ke ubọk.”<verse eid="1SA 14:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 14:13" />Yọnatan amaakama ubọk ye ukod amọ adọọk akaa ye akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ ke edem amọ. Mbon Filistia emaeduọ ke iso Yọnatan, akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ amaakeene anye ke edem awoot ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 14:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 14:14" />Ke akpa anwan ado Yọnatan ye akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ emaewot mme ideen edịb ke ibio ubaak isọñ.<verse eid="1SA 14:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Isrel Ekan Mbon Filistia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 14:15" />Ndin idem amaanyeñ afịd mbon ekọñ, mbon se ikiba ke itie nnaaekọñ ye ke anwaekọñ, ye mbon se ikiba ke itie ukpeme ye mbon se ikikaa umʌm awo, ndin isọñ amaanyʌñ anyeñ. Akedo ndịk a-aketooho Abasi.<verse eid="1SA 14:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 14:16" />Sọọl ase ke Kibie ke Benyamin anyʌñ akịt nte atu ekọñ enuaha ke afịd ubeñ. <verse eid="1SA 14:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 14:17" />Ndin Sọọl abo ideen e-ekebaaha ye anye, “Ndufo ibat mbon ekọñ yak ise mme anie imiibaaha ye ñnyịn.” Ke ini ammọ enamma ami, emaekịt ke akedo Yọnatan ye akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ imiikibaaha do.<verse eid="1SA 14:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 14:18" />Sọọl amaabo Ahiya, “Ben akebe edioomo Abasi di.” (Idaha ntoro akeba ye nditọ Isrel.) <verse eid="1SA 14:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 14:19" />Ke ini Sọọl asʌkkọ atañ ikọ ye aku, adutịm ke nnaaekọñ mbon Filistia anekke asọñ akan naña akedo. Ndin Sọọl amaabo aku ate, “Sio ubọk mfo fep.”<verse eid="1SA 14:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 14:20" />Ndin Sọọl ye afịd ideen amọ emaeboho keed enyʌñ edakka anwan. Ammọ emaekịt Filistia ke ataa ndutịme, naña ekpeeñe emọ-emọ ke akañkañ ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 14:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 14:21" />Mbon Hibru e-ekebaaha akpa ye mbon Filistia ekenyʌññọ esaña ye ammọ emaedọọk ekaa itie nnaaekọñ ammọ ekeene ebịne nditọ Isrel e-ekebaaha ye Sọọl ye Yọnatan. <verse eid="1SA 14:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 14:22" />Ke ini afịd Isrel e-ekedịbeke ke abod isọñ idʌñ Ifrem ekoppo ebo ke mbon Filistia efeeñe, ammọ emaekeene ediana ebịne ammọ ke akpọsọñ ubịne. <verse eid="1SA 14:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 14:23" />Ke ntoro usen ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanyaaña Isrel, ñko anwan amaasaña aboiyo Bed Afịn.<verse eid="1SA 14:23" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Yọnatan Adia Adanakwọọk</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 14:24" />Ndin nditọ Isrel ekeba ke ekaha usen ado, sia Sọọl amaanọ mme awo unwọñọ, abo, “Esuuñọ awo akeedodo se idia ñkpọ mbemiso ndubiayio adi, mbemiso ami nsio mme asua mmi usiene!” Ke ntoro baaba awo ndomokeed ikidiaha ñkpọ.<verse eid="1SA 14:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 14:25" />Afịd atu ekọñ emaedʌk akai, ndin adanakwọọk amaaba ke isọñ itie ado. <verse eid="1SA 14:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 14:26" />Ke ini ammọ ekedʌkkọ akai, ammọ emaekịt adanakwọọk naña asʌk awuọñọ; ado baaba awo ndomokeed ikisịnne ubọk idọppọ isịn ke inua, sia ammọ emaekop ndịk ebaña unwọñọ. <verse eid="1SA 14:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 14:27" />Ado Yọnatan ikikoppo ibaña ke ete imọ amaanọ mme awo unwọñọ, ke ntoro, anye amaanyan utịd esañ amọ a-akebaaha anye ke ubọk asịn ke efọk adanakwọọk ado. Anye amaadọppọ aben akaa inua, ndin anyen amaanwaña anye.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14:27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido adudu amọ amaana ademme; ukem ado ke 1 Sa 14:29</char></note> <verse eid="1SA 14:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 14:28" />Ndin awo ekọñ keed amaabo anye, “Ete mfo amaanọ ñnyịn mbon ekọñ unwọñọ abo, ‘Adọdiọọk anọ awo se idia ñkpọ mfịn ami!’ Ado asịn idem amem ideen ami.”<verse eid="1SA 14:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 14:29" />Yọnatan amaabo, “Ete mmi anam mfịna anọ idʌñ. Se naña anyen mmi anwaña naña ami ndiaha etək-etək adanakwọọk ami. <verse eid="1SA 14:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 14:30" />Akpaakenekke afọn adieke ideen ami emaedia ubaak ñkpọ se ammọ ekekoono eto itie ekọñ mme asua ammọ edi. Nte uwot mbon Filistia ikpikikanna ado?”<verse eid="1SA 14:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="1SA 14:31" />Ke usen ado ke mme nditọ Isrel emaekewoot mbon Filistia tọọñọ ke Mikmas tutu asịm Aiyalọn, idem amaamem ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 14:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="1SA 14:32" />Ndin afịd awo ebịmme ebịne akama mbịme ekọñ, enyʌñ eben edọñ, enañ ye ntək enañ, ammọ ewoot ammọ ke isọñ enyʌñ eta ammọ ye iyiib. <verse eid="1SA 14:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="1SA 14:33" />Ndin awo amaabo Sọọl, “Se, ideen esʌk enam idiọọkñkpọ ke isọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ammọ edita unam se inie iyiib ke esịd.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 14:33">Anye amaabo, “Ndufo enie mbuọdidem amaakeduọkkọ. Iwere ekamba itiad idi mmi ini keed.” <verse eid="1SA 14:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="1SA 14:34" />Ndin anye amaabo Sọọl, “Ikaa ke atu ideen ado inyʌñ ikidọkkọ ammọ, ‘Ndufo keedekeed iben enañ ye edọñ ndufo insọk miin, inyʌñ iwot ammọ mi inyʌñ ita ammọ. Ikiinam idiọọkñkpọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke adita unam asʌkkọ asesịne iyiib.’ ”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 14:34">Ke ntoro afịd awo emaeben enañ ammọ akonayio ado ediwot do. <verse eid="1SA 14:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="1SA 14:35" />Ndin Sọọl amaabọp itieukpono do anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; ami akedo akpa anye adinam ñkpọ ntom.<verse eid="1SA 14:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="1SA 14:36" />Sọọl amaabo, “Yak ñnyịn isọiyọ ika ikibịne mbon Filistia ke akonayio inyʌñ ibịme ammọ tutu ayio asiere, ñko ke ñnyịn isʌhọ ammọ ndomokeed ye uwem.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 14:36">Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Inam se adodo i-inemme ndufo esịd.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 14:36">Ado aku amaabo, “Yak ñnyịn ibịp Abasi ke itie ami.”<verse eid="1SA 14:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="1SA 14:37" />Ndin Sọọl amaabịp Abasi, “Ami nsọiyọ mbịne mbon Filistia? Afo ayaayaak ammọ asịn Isrel ke ubọk?” Ado Abasi ikibọọrọke anye usen ado.<verse eid="1SA 14:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="1SA 14:38" />Ke ntak ado Sọọl amaabo, “Idi mi, afịd ndufo se ido adaukara atu ekọñ, yak ñnyịn ise me nsoo idiọọkñkpọ ke inam mfịn ami. <verse eid="1SA 14:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="1SA 14:39" />Ke akpanikọ adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akenyaañake Isrel aduuho uwem, akpekọm ayịn mmi Yọnatan ado andidue, ana anye akpa.” Ado ibaaha awo ammọ nte keed se ikisio uyio.<verse eid="1SA 14:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="1SA 14:40" />Sọọl ndin amaabo afịd mbon Isrel, “Ana ndufo eda ke udo; ami ye Yọnatan ayịn mmi iyaida ke umi.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 14:40">Ammọ emaebọọrọ “Nam se afo akịt abo ke ufọn fiin.”<verse eid="1SA 14:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="1SA 14:41" />Ndin Sọọl amaabọñ akam anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi Isrel, “Ntaha afo umuubọọrọke ayịnufọk mfo mfịn ami-e? Adieke mfịna antooho miin me ayịn mmi awodeen Yọnatan, bọọrọ ye Urim, ado adieke mfịna atooho ideen Isrel bọọrọ ye Tumịm.” Ukañ amaatịp Yọnatan ye Sọọl, anyʌñ atoppo afịd mme ideen ndin ammọ emaebọkkọ. <verse eid="1SA 14:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="1SA 14:42" />Sọọl amaabo, “Sịn ukañ ke ufọọd mmi ye Yọnatan ayịn mmi.” Ndin ukañ amaatịp Yọnatan.<verse eid="1SA 14:42" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="1SA 14:43" />Ndin Sọọl amaabo Yọnatan, “Ndọkkọ miin se afo akenam.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 14:43">Ndin Yọnatan amaabo anye, “Ñketʌm etək adanakwọọk ke nsịm esañ mmi. Ndin idahami ana ami ñkpa!”<verse eid="1SA 14:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="1SA 14:44" />Sọọl amaabo, “Yak Abasi ammia miin ufen, ñko yak anye anekke anam ntoro, adieke afo umuukpaaha, Yọnatan.”<verse eid="1SA 14:44" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="1SA 14:45" />Ado mme ideen ado emaebo Sọọl, “Akpena nte Yọnatan akpa, anye a-akedatta ekamba ufak ami adi ke Isrel? Ibaaha! Adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aduuho uwem, ided iwuod amọ ndomokeed idiitakka, sia anye akenam ami mfịn ato ke unwam Abasi.” Ke ntoro, ideen ado emaenyaaña Yọnatan, ndin awo ikiwotto anye.<verse eid="1SA 14:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="1SA 14:46" />Ndin Sọọl amaatre adibịne mbon Filistia, ndin ammọ emaenyọñ idʌñ ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 14:46" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" sid="1SA 14:47" />Ke Sọọl amaakedọọk ada nte adaukara ke Isrel, anye amaanwana ye mme asua ammọ ke afịd usʌñ: Mọb, mbon Amọn, Edọm, adidem Soba ye mbon Filistia. Nte anye akekanna aka, anye amaanọ ammọ ufen. <verse eid="1SA 14:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="1SA 14:48" />Anye amaanwana ye uko akan mbon Amalek, anyaaña Isrel asio ke ubọk mbon se ikibọi ammọ ñkpọ.<verse eid="1SA 14:48" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekpək Sọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="1SA 14:49" />Nditọ ideen Sọọl ekedoñño Yọnatan, Isfi ye Malki-Sua. Anyịñ adiaha amọ akedo Merab, etəkayịn awonwaan amọ akedo Maikal. <verse eid="1SA 14:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="1SA 14:50" />Anyịñ anwaan amọ akedo Ahinoam ayịn awonwaan Ahimaas. Anyịñ adaiso ekọñ Sọọl akedo Abna ayịn Nee, ñko Nee akedo ayịneka ete Sọọl. <verse eid="1SA 14:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="1SA 14:51" />Kisi ete Sọọl ye Nee ete Abna ekedoñño nditọ ideen Abiel.<verse eid="1SA 14:51" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" sid="1SA 14:52" />Ke afịd ayio uwem Sọọl, idod-idod ekọñ amaaba ye mbon Filistia, ñko ini akeedodo Sọọl akekịtte akpọsọñ awo me awo uko, anye amaasiben anye adian idem.<verse eid="1SA 14:52" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="1SA 15" />
  <para style="s1">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Asịn Sọọl nte Adidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 15:1" />Samwel amaabo Sọọl, “Ami ndo awo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akedọññọ yak uyet fiin adan nte adidem anọ ikọd amọ Isrel; ke ntoro ndin kpañ utọñ nọ etob a-atooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 15:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 15:2" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ado ami: ‘Ami ñyaanọ nditọ Amalek ufen ke se ammọ ekenam ye Isrel ke usʌñ ammọ ekesañake ewuọ ke Iyib. <verse eid="1SA 15:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 15:3" />Kaa ndin, kenwana ye mbon Amalek nyʌñ sobo ataa afịd se ammọ enie. Kuusʌhọ awo ammọ ndomokeed; wot ideen ye ibaan, ntəkayịn ye nsek nditọ, mme enañ ye mme edọñ, mme kamel ye mme dọñki.’ ”<verse eid="1SA 15:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 15:4" />Sọọl ndin amaakoot afịd ideen ate edi anyʌñ atịm ammọ adọñ ke udịm ke Telaim, mbon ekọñ tọsịn ikie iba (200,000) esaña ke ukod ye tọsịn duob (10,000) e-etooho Yuda. <verse eid="1SA 15:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 15:5" />Sọọl amaadakka akaa abio Amalek anyʌñ akenịm mbon udịbe ke abedeñ. <verse eid="1SA 15:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 15:6" />Ndin anye Sọọl amaabo mbon Keen, “Iwuọñọ, ikpọñ mbon Amalek mbaak ami ndisobo ndufo ye ammọ; sia adooho ndufo emaefọn ido ye nditọ Isrel idaha ammọ ekewuọhọ ke isọñ Iyib.” Ndin mbon Keen emaewuọñọ ekpọñ mbon Amalek.<verse eid="1SA 15:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 15:7" />Ndin Sọọl amaasuan mbon Amalek ke afịd usʌñ tọọñọ ke Hafila tutu ke Sọọ, a-akpereke adaña edem usakkautịn Iyib. <verse eid="1SA 15:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 15:8" />Anye amaaben Akak adidem mbon Amalek ye uwem anyọñ, ado anye amaawot afịd mbon amọ ke akañkañ. <verse eid="1SA 15:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 15:9" />Ado Sọọl ye mbon ekọñ amọ emaesʌhọ Akak uwem ye mme edọñ ye mme enañ se ifọọn ikan, mme ikpọ ñyịn enañ ye mme ñyịn edọñ, afịd ñkpọ se ikifọọn. Ammọ ikinyịmmeke adisobo mbon ado afịd-afịd. Ado afịd se ikinekke idiọi inyʌñ iba mmeem-mmeem ammọ emaesobo.<verse eid="1SA 15:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 15:10" />Akem uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadisịm Samwel abo: <verse eid="1SA 15:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 15:11" />“Ami mmetua ñkpọfiọk ke adikinam Sọọl ado adidem, sia adooho anye awọññọ akpọñ usʌñ mmi inyʌññọ ikop item mmi.” Esịd amaayat Samwel ndin anye amaanyʌñ asemme anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> afịd akonayio ado.<verse eid="1SA 15:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 15:12" />Ke usiere ubakusen Samwel amaabak adakka adikikịt Sọọl, ado emaebo anye, “Sọọl amaakaa Kamel. Anye amaabot ñkpọ aditoiyo anịm anọ idem amọ ke udo ñko awọññọ asọiyọ adika Kilkal.”<verse eid="1SA 15:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 15:13" />Ke ini Samwel asịmme anye, Sọọl amaabo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> udiọñ fiin! Ami mmenam afịd se uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akebo yak nam.”<verse eid="1SA 15:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 15:14" />Ado Samwel amaabo, “Nsoo ndin ido umai edọñ ami ke utọñ mmi? Nsoo ido uyom enañ ake ami ñkoppo mi?”<verse eid="1SA 15:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 15:15" />Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Mme mbon ekọñ ekeben ammọ eto mbon Amalek edi; ammọ emaesʌhọ mme enañ ye mme edọñ se ifọọn ikan nọ eben enam uwa enọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mfo, ado ñnyịn imaisobo afịd ñkpọ mbio ako.”<verse eid="1SA 15:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 15:16" />Samwel amaabo Sọọl “Akem! Yak ami udọkkọ fiin se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akembo miin ñkpọñ akonayio.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 15:16">Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Ndọkkọ miin.”<verse eid="1SA 15:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 15:17" />Samwel amaabo, “Akpesʌkado ini keed afo akedo etək-etək ke anyen mfo, nte afo ukududooho adidem mme esiin Isrel? <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akuyet fiin adan nte adidem ke Isrel. <verse eid="1SA 15:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 15:18" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaudọñ fiin utom abo, ‘Kaa nyʌñ ke sobo mbon ibak ado afịd-afịd, mbon Amalek ado; nwana ekọñ ye ammọ tutu afo asọọk ammọ asio afịd ke iso isọñ.’ <verse eid="1SA 15:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 15:19" />Ntaha ake afo umuukukoppo uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ọ? Ntaha afo akebịmeke mbịme ado anyʌñ anam idiọọk ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ọ?”<verse eid="1SA 15:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 15:20" />Sọọl amaabo Samwel, “Ado ami mmaakop uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ami mmaakaa utom <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akendọññọ miin. Ami mmaasobo mbon Amalek afịd-afịd ndin mmaaben Akak adidem ammọ ñnyọñ ndi. <verse eid="1SA 15:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 15:21" />Mbon ekọñ emaeben mme enañ ye mme edọñ nte mbịme, asaña-asaña ñkpọ andifọn ñkan se ekpekama enam uwa enọ Abasi, nọ ato do ediiben iwa inọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mfo ke Kilkal.”<verse eid="1SA 15:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 15:22" />Ado Samwel amaabọọrọ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 15:22">“Nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akop inemesịd ke ufọfọb uwa ye uwa emem</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 15:22">nte adikop item nnọọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>?</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 15:22">Adikop item afọn akan uwa,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 15:22">ñko ñkpañutọñ afọn akan akpọñ akukịmedọñ.<verse eid="1SA 15:22" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 15:23" />Sia emiom atie nte idiọọkñkpọ uwa idiọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 15:23">ñko ñkịdidem abit ukpono ndem.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 15:23">Sia adooho afo amaasịn ikọ a-atooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 15:23">anye usịn fiin nte adidem.”<verse eid="1SA 15:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 15:24" />Ndin Sọọl amaabo Samwel, “Ami mmenam idiọọkñkpọ. Sia adooho ami ñkikoppo uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye mme item mfo. Ami mmaafeghe mme ideen ado ndin ami mmaanyʌñ ñkop se ammọ eketañ. <verse eid="1SA 15:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 15:25" />Idahami ami mmukpe fiin ubọk, dakka nnọ ke ndudue mmi nyʌñ tịmme ñkene miin, nọ ato do ami ñkekpono <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="1SA 15:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 15:26" />Ado Samwel amaabo anye Sọọl, “Ami ndiitịmmeke ukeene fiin. Afo amaasịn ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñko <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anyʌñ usịn fiin nte adidem ke Isrel!”<verse eid="1SA 15:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 15:27" />Ke Samwel akannake iso adinyọñ, Sọọl amaamʌm mben afọñ amọ, ndin awakka. <verse eid="1SA 15:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 15:28" />Samwel amaabo anye, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> a-awai abioubọọñ Isrel ukpọñ fiin mfịn ami anyʌñ ayaak anọ keed ke atu mbọhọidʌñ mfo, anọ anye a-afọnnọ ukan fiin. <verse eid="1SA 15:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 15:29" />Anye a-adooho Ubọọñ Isrel isisʌhọke nsu inyʌññọ ikpəho esịd; sia anye idooho awo, se ebo ke anye akpəho esịd.”<verse eid="1SA 15:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 15:30" />Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Ami mmenam idiọọkñkpọ. Ado mbọk ñkpono miin ke iso mme ñkpisọñ ye ke isọ Isrel; tịmme ñkeene miin, nọ ato do ñkekpono <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mfo.” <verse eid="1SA 15:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1SA 15:31" />Ke ntoro Samwel amaatịmme akeene Sọọl, ndin Sọọl akekpono <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="1SA 15:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="1SA 15:32" />Ndin Samwel amaabo, “Iben Akak adidem mbon Amalek insọk.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 15:32">Akak amaawuọ abịne anye ye ñkpọnọ. Ndin anye amaakere, “Ke akpanikọ ubiak ñkpa a-aboiyo afep.”<verse eid="1SA 15:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="1SA 15:33" />Ado Samwel amaabo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 15:33">“Kpa naña akañkañ mfo anam mme ibaan enana nditọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 15:33">kpa ntoro ke eka mfo adiido anana ayịn ke atu ibaan.”</para>
  <para style="m" vid="1SA 15:33">Ndin Samwel amaawot Akak ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke Kilkal.<verse eid="1SA 15:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="1SA 15:34" />Ndin Samwel amaatịmme anyọñ Rama, ado Sọọl amaanyọñ akaa ufọk ammọ ke Kibie ake Sọọl. <verse eid="1SA 15:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="1SA 15:35" />Tutu usen Samwel akekpaaha, anye ikitịmmeke ikikịt Sọọl aba, akpesʌkado Samwel amaafʌhọ abaña anye. Ñko <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaatua ñkpọfiọk ke anye adikinam Sọọl adidem ke Isrel.<verse eid="1SA 15:35" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="1SA 16" />
  <para style="s1">Samwel Ayet Defid Adan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 16:1" />
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo Samwel, “Afo uduufʌhọ Sọọl yak akpeene die, sia adooho ami mmesịn anye nte adidem ke Isrel? Tọkkọ adan sịn yak ayọhọ ke nnʌk mfo nyʌñ dakka isañ dʌk usʌñ; ami mmudọñ fiin nnọ Yesi ke Betlehem. Ami mmemek ayịn awodeen amọ keed nte adidem.”<verse eid="1SA 16:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 16:2" />Ado Samwel amaabo, “Ami ndiisaña die ñka? Adieke Sọọl akoppo abaña, anye ayañwot miin.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 16:2">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo, “Ben ñkpʌk ñyịn umanenañ kama kaa nyʌñ bo, ‘Ami mmedi adinam uwa nnọọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ <verse eid="1SA 16:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 16:3" />Koot Yesi yak adiwuana ke uwa, ndin ami ñyauwọt fiin se adiinam. Ana afo ayet awo ake ami nduuwọt fiin adan.”<verse eid="1SA 16:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 16:4" />Samwel amaanam se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akebo. Ke ini anye akesịmme Betlehem, mme ñkpisọñ abio emaenyeñ idem ke ini ammọ ekekịtte anye. Ammọ emaebịp, “Afo adi ke emem?”<verse eid="1SA 16:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 16:5" />Samwel amaabọọrọ, “Ii, ke emem; ami ndi adiwa uwa nnọọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ndufo inam idem ndufo asana inyʌñ iñkeene miin idi uwa.” Ndin anye amaanam Yesi ye nditọ amọ ideen esana anyʌñ akoot amọ edi uwa.<verse eid="1SA 16:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 16:6" />Ke ini ammọ ekesịmme, Samwel amaakịt Eliab anyʌñ akere “Ke akpanikọ anye <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayette adan ada ami ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="1SA 16:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 16:7" />Ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo Samwel, “Kuuse naña anye aba me unyọọñ amọ, sia adooho ami mmesịn anye. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> isiseeghe mme ñkpọ se mme awo ese. Mme awo esise anyọñidem awo ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ase esịd.”<verse eid="1SA 16:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 16:8" />Ndin Yesi amaakoot Abinadab anam anye asaña aboiyo Samwel ke iso. Ado Samwel amaabo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> imekke anye ami ñko.” <verse eid="1SA 16:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 16:9" />Yesi amaanyʌñ anam Sama asaña aboiyo. Ado Samwel amaabo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inyʌññọ imek anye mmi.” <verse eid="1SA 16:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 16:10" />Yesi amaanam nditọ ideen amọ itiaba esaña eboiyo Samwel ke iso, ado Samwel amaabo anye, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> imekke mbio ami.” <verse eid="1SA 16:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 16:11" />Akema, anye amaabịp Yesi, “Ukweeñe nditọ ideen se afo anie edoñño ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 16:11">Yesi amaabọọrọ, “Andisịb ñkan mmọdo. Anye akpeme edọñ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 16:11">Samwel amaabo, “Dọñ ekoot anye; ñnyịn idiisuuho itie tutu anye anyọñ adi.”<verse eid="1SA 16:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 16:12" />Ke ntoro, anye amaadọñ ekekoot anye anyʌñ anam eben anye edʌk edi. Anye amaanekke akop nsọñidem anyʌñ anie uyaiya ikpaidem anyʌñ ado uyaiya awodeen.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 16:12">Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo, “Dakka da yet anye adan; anye ado ami.”<verse eid="1SA 16:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 16:13" />Ke ntoro, Samwel amaaben adan ke nnʌk anyʌñ ayet anye ke iwuod ke iso nditọeka amọ, ndin tọọñọ ke usen ado, Sịbidịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adidoro ke idem Defid ekamba-ekamba. Ndin Samwel amaanyọñ Rama.<verse eid="1SA 16:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Defid Anam Utom anọ Sọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 16:14" />Akem Sịbidịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaawuọ akpọñ Sọọl, ndin ndedeghe<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido idiọọk; se ñko ke 1 Sa 16:15, 16, ye 23; 1 Sa 18:10</char></note> sịbidịd a-atooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adidoro anye ke iwuod atịmede anye.<verse eid="1SA 16:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 16:15" />Nditọufọk Sọọl emaebo anye, “Sese, idiọọk sịbidịd a-atooho Abasi u-utʌkkọ fiin. <verse eid="1SA 16:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 16:16" />Yak abọọñ ñnyịn anọ nditọufọk amọ uyio ke mmi yak eyem awo se ikan ibre ndidoudʌk. Anye ayaabre ke ini idiọọk sịbidịd a-atooho Abasi udoroke fiin ke iwuod, ndin afo ayaakop nsọñidem.”<verse eid="1SA 16:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 16:17" />Sọọl ndin amaabo ayịnufọk amọ, “Yem awo se ikan inekke ibre ben nsọk.”<verse eid="1SA 16:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 16:18" />Ayịnufọk amọ keed amaabọọrọ abo, “Ami mmekịt ayịn Yesi a-atooho Betlehem a-adiọọñọke naña esibre ndidoudʌk. Anye ado awo uko ye awo ekọñ. Anye adiọọñọ naña etañ ikọ anyʌñ ado uyaiya awodeen. Ñko <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aba ye anye.”<verse eid="1SA 16:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 16:19" />Ndin Sọọl amaadọñ isʌñutom utom anọ Yesi abo, “Nọ Defid ayịn mfo a-abaaha ye mme edọñ ensọk miin.” <verse eid="1SA 16:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 16:20" />Ndin Yesi amaaben dọñki a-akebenne uyo, ukọd ke ikịm ye ñyịn ebod anọ ayịn amọ Defid yak adat asọk Sọọl.<verse eid="1SA 16:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 16:21" />Defid amaadika abịne Sọọl anyʌñ akenam utom anọ anye. Sọọl amaanekke ama anye, ndin Defid amaakeene ado keed ke atu mme akama ñkpọ ekọñ amọ. <verse eid="1SA 16:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 16:22" />Ndin Sọọl amaadọñ utom anọ Yesi ate, “Yak Defid aba ye ami sia ami mmenem esịd ye anye.”<verse eid="1SA 16:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 16:23" />Ini keed akeedodo sịbidịd a-atooho Abasi adoroke Sọọl ke idem, Defid ayaaben ndidoudʌk amọ abre. Ntoro ke idem adiifeere Sọọl; ayaafọn anye ke idem, ñko idiọọk sịbidịd ado ayaakpọñ anye.<verse eid="1SA 16:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 16" />
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="1SA 17" />
  <para style="s1">Defid ye Koloyad</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 17:1" />Akem mbon Filistia emaebok mbon ekọñ ammọ yak eka ekọñ enyʌñ ekeboho ke Soko ke Yuda. Ammọ emaenịm nnaaekọñ ke Efes Damịm, ke ufọọd Soko ye Aseka. <verse eid="1SA 17:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 17:2" />Sọọl ye nditọ Isrel emaeboho enyʌñ enịm nnaaekọñ ke abedeñ Ela enyʌñ ebeeñe idem edinwana ye mbon Filistia. <verse eid="1SA 17:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 17:3" />Mbon Filistia ekeba ke abod ñkañ keed ke ini nditọ Isrel ekebaaha ke abod ñkañ uko, ndin abedeñ akebakka ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 17:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 17:4" />Awo uko ekọñ keed a-akekereke Koloyad, awo Kad, amaawuọ ato ke nnaaekọñ mbon Filistia adi. Unyọñ amọ akedo kubid itiokeed ye udomo span keed.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte mita 3</char></note> <verse eid="1SA 17:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 17:5" />Anye amaanyʌñ ayara itam ukpemeiwuod ake brọns anyʌñ asịne afọñidem ekọñ brọns a-anieghe udob sekel tọsịn ition (5,000);<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 58</char></note> <verse eid="1SA 17:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 17:6" />ke ukod amọ anye amaasịne ñkpọukod brọns, ñko anyan ukwak brọns amaakọñọ atọ atekke anye ke edem. <verse eid="1SA 17:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 17:7" />Eto eduad amọ akeba nte eto udọk afọñ, inua eduad amọ amaadoppo sekel ikie itiokeed (600)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 6.9</char></note>. Andikama atuekọñ amọ amaasaña anye ke iso.<verse eid="1SA 17:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 17:8" />Koloyad amaada anyʌñ abọọñ ñkpo anọ mbon ekọñ Isrel, “Nsoo ido nọ ndufo ewuọ edi enyʌñ eda ke udịm eyem ekọñ? Nte ami ndooho awo Filistia ñko nte ndufo idoññoke nditọufọk Sọọl? Isio awo yak adi ambịne miin. <verse eid="1SA 17:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 17:9" />Adieke anye anwanake anyʌñ añwot miin, ñnyịn iyaidoñño ifʌn ndufo; ado ami ñkpekan anye ñwot, ndufo eyaedoñño ifʌn ñnyịn enyʌñ enam ñkpọ inọ ñnyịn.” <verse eid="1SA 17:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 17:10" />Ndin awo Filistia ado amaabo, “Usen mfịn ami mmemia ata ye mbon ekọñ Isrel! Innọ miin awo yak ñnyịn inwana emọ-emọ.” <verse eid="1SA 17:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 17:11" />Ke ammọ adikikop mme ikọ awo Filistia ado, Sọọl ye afịd mbon Isrel emaeyeeme nsia ndin idem amaanyʌñ anyeñ ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 17:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 17:12" />Ndin Defid akedo ayịn awo Efrad a-akekereke Yesi, a-aketooho Betlehem ke Yuda. Yesi akenie nditọ ideen itiaita, ñko ke ini Sọọl anye amaanekke asọñ. <verse eid="1SA 17:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 17:13" />Akpa nditọ Yesi ita emaekeene Sọọl ekaa ekọñ: Akpan amọ akedo Eliab; Udọ amọ ado Abinadab; etəkudọ akedo Sama. <verse eid="1SA 17:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 17:14" />Defid akedo andikisịp ñkan. Awo ita se ikikpon ikan emaekeene Sọọl, <verse eid="1SA 17:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 17:15" />ado ubaak ini Defid amaasitịmme edem akpọñ Sọọl adikikpeme ufene ete amọ ke Betlehem.<verse eid="1SA 17:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 17:16" />Ke usen aba awo Filistia ado amaasiwuọ adida afịd ubakusen ye ndubiayio.<verse eid="1SA 17:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 17:17" />Akem Yesi amaabo Defid ayịn amọ, “Ben ufọb abakpa ami ke udomoñkpọ efa<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 16</char></note> ye eboho uyo duob ami sọp idem sọk nditọeka mfo ke nnaaekọñ ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 17:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 17:18" />Ben mme nsọọñ mmọọñeba duob ami sọk adaiwuod ekọñ ake ikpeghe ammọ. Se naña nditọeka mfo ideen eba nyʌñ ben ikọ nsọọñọidem dindọkkọ. <verse eid="1SA 17:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 17:19" />Ammọ mmọdo eba ye Sọọl ye afịd ideen ke Isrel ke abedeñ Ela enwana ye mbon Filistia.”<verse eid="1SA 17:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 17:20" />Ke usiere ubakusen Defid amaayaak udịmedọñ asịn ke ubọk akpemeedọñ, atʌm idem adakka, kpa naña Yesi akedọkkọ anye. Anye amaakesịm nnaaekọñ kpa ke idaha mbon ekọñ Isrel ekewuọñọke eka itie ekọñ ammọ, ke ekwaaha ñkpo ekọñ. <verse eid="1SA 17:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 17:21" />Isrel ye mbon Filistia ekesʌk edʌt udịm ekọñ ammọ, esak iso ese emọ-emọ. <verse eid="1SA 17:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 17:22" />Defid amaayaak mme ñkpọ se anye akekama abono ye mme akpeme ñkpọ, afeghe akaa udịmekọñ akebịp nditọeka amọ ideen naña ñkpọ aba ye ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 17:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 17:23" />Ke anye akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ ye ammọ, Koloyad, awo Filistia, a-atooho Kad, a-adooho andikan amaawuọ ke udịm amọ ada asaña-asaña anyʌñ akwaaha ñkpo amọ naña asidak anam, ndin Defid amaakop. <verse eid="1SA 17:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 17:24" />Ini akeedodo nditọ Isrel esikịtte ete ado, afịd ammọ esifeeñe ke ntak akpọsọñ ndịk.<verse eid="1SA 17:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 17:25" />Ndin nditọ Isrel ekesʌk ebo, “Emekịt naña awo ami asʌk akaiso awuọ adi? Anye awuọ adi adimia ata ye Isrel. Adidem ayaanọ awo a-awotto ete ami ekamba inie. Anye ayaanyʌñ anọ anye ayịn awonwaan amọ ke ndọ anyʌñ asio ekpək amọ ke ukpe taks ke Isrel.”<verse eid="1SA 17:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 17:26" />Defid amaabịp ideen e-ekedaaha ediana anye, “Nsoo ke ediinam inọ awo a-awotto awo Filistia anyʌññọ adooro abuud asio ke Isrel? Anie ido awo Filistia, ake miifọọrọke edʌd, nọ anye akpedimia ata ye mbon ekọñ aduuwem Abasi?”<verse eid="1SA 17:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 17:27" />Ammọ emaemaana etañ enọ anye se ammọ eketatañ ebo anye, “Ami ado se ediinam inọ awo adiiwot anye.”<verse eid="1SA 17:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 17:28" />Ke Eliab akpaneka Defid akekoppo naña anye atañ ikọ ye ideen ado, anye amaanekke ayat esịd ye anye anyʌñ abịp anye, “Nsoo inam afo awuọ adi mmi? Ñko mme edọñ ado ke anaan afo akeyaak asịn anie ke ubọk? Ami mmediọọñọ iseri mfo ye naña afo akpon ibak ke esịd mfo; afo akedi adidise ekọñ kpọd.”<verse eid="1SA 17:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 17:29" />Defid amaabo, “Nsoo ke ami nam idaha ado? Idooho se nsio ukpọk uyio?” <verse eid="1SA 17:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 17:30" />Anye amaakanna iso abịne awo mfen anyʌñ aketọọñọ kpa nneme ado, ndin mme ideen ado emaebọọrọ anye kpa nte akekpa. <verse eid="1SA 17:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1SA 17:31" />Emaeketañ se Defid aketañ enọ Sọọl, Sọọl amaanyʌñ adọñ ekoot anye.<verse eid="1SA 17:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="1SA 17:32" />Defid amaabo Sọọl, “Yak awo akuuduọọk idodanyen ke ntak awo Filistia ami; ayịnufọk mfo ayaakenwana ye anye.”<verse eid="1SA 17:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="1SA 17:33" />Sọọl amaabọọrọ Defid, “Afo uduukanna uwuọ ubịne awo Filistia ami ukunwana ye anye; afo ado etək akparawa, ñko anye ado awo anwan tọọñọ ke uyịn amọ.”<verse eid="1SA 17:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="1SA 17:34" />Ado Defid amaabo Sọọl, “Ayịnufọk mfo asikpeme mme edọñ ete amọ. Ke ini ekpe me amọnikọd akediighe adiben edọñ keed ke atu udịmedọñ, <verse eid="1SA 17:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="1SA 17:35" />ami mmaawuọ mbịne anye, ñkeyʌppọ anye ñnyʌñ mfịppe edọñ ado ke inua amọ nsio. Ke ini anye akannake ambịne miin, ami mmaamʌm anye ided, ñyʌppọ anye ñwot. <verse eid="1SA 17:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="1SA 17:36" />Ayịnufọk mfo awot naña iba, ekpe ye amọnikọd; ndin awo Filistia ammiifọọrọke edʌd mi adiiba nte keed ke atu ammọ, sia anye amaamia ata ye mbonekọñ aduuwem Abasi. <verse eid="1SA 17:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="1SA 17:37" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> a-akeñnyaañake miin asio ke ubọk ekpe ye ubọk amọnikọd ado ayaanyaaña miin asio ke ubọk awo Filistia ami.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 17:37">Sọọl amaabo Defid, “Kaa yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aba ye afo.”<verse eid="1SA 17:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="1SA 17:38" />Ndin Sọọl amaasịn Defid ikpaukod ekọñ amọ ke ukod. Anye asịn anye afọñidem ekọñ ukwak ye ufʌk iwuod brọns ke iwuod. <verse eid="1SA 17:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="1SA 17:39" />Defid amaafaak akañkañ amọ ke afọñ amọ anyʌñ anwana adisaña ñkanna sia mme afọñ ado ye mme ñkpọ ekọñ ado ikimegheke anye.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 17:39">Anye amaabo Sọọl, “Ami ñkanna nsịne nsaña, sia adooho immegheke miin.” Ke ntoro anye amaasioño ammọ afep. <verse eid="1SA 17:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="1SA 17:40" />Ndin anye amaaben esañ amọ akama ke ubọk, asat ndọnọ itiad ition ke idịm, adọñ ammọ ke mben ekpad akpemeedọñ amọ ndin, ye ikañakpọ amọ ke ubọk amọ, anye amaasaña abịne awo Filistia ado.<verse eid="1SA 17:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="1SA 17:41" />Se etatañ ami awo Filistia ado, ye akama atuekọñ amọ ke iso amọ, ekesʌk esaña ekpere Defid. <verse eid="1SA 17:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="1SA 17:42" />Awodeen Filistia amaase Defid adọọk ase asuuhọ, adikịt ke anye ado idaha idaha etək akparawa, akekoppo nsọñidem anyʌñ ayaiya, ndin anye ase anye ke ndek. <verse eid="1SA 17:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="1SA 17:43" />Anye amaabo Defid, “Ami ndo ewa, nọ afo akama eto awuọ ambịne miin?” Ndin awo Filistia ado amaasuuñọ Defid ke anyịñ mme abasi amọ. <verse eid="1SA 17:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="1SA 17:44" />Awodeen Filistia amaabo Defid, “Saña di mmi ndin ami ñyaanọ mme inuen ye mme ndiọi unam abʌkidem mfo yak eta!”<verse eid="1SA 17:44" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" sid="1SA 17:45" />Defid amaadọkkọ awo Filistia ado ate, “Afo adi ambịne miin ye eduad ye akañkañ ye usaam, ado ami ndi ubịne fiin ke anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan, Abasi mbon ekọñ Isrel, a-afo amiaha ata. <verse eid="1SA 17:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="1SA 17:46" />Mfịn ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayauyaak fiin ansịn miin ke ubọk, ami ñyauwot fiin ñnyʌñ ukpịkke fiin iwuod. Ataa mfịn ami ñyaayaak akpo mbon ekọñ mbon Filistia nnọ mme inuen ye ndiọi unam, ndin afịd ederimbod eyaediọọñọ ke Abasi mmọdo aba ke Isrel. <verse eid="1SA 17:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="1SA 17:47" />Afịd mbon e-ebohoke mi eyaediọọñọ ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> idatta akañkañ me eduad inyaaña awo; sia ekọñ ami ado ake <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin anye ayaanyʌñ iyaak afịd ndufo ansịn miin ke ubọk.”<verse eid="1SA 17:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="1SA 17:48" />Nte awo Filistia akesañake akpere adinwana ye anye, Defid amaafeghe usọp-usọp akaa utịd edem udịmekọñ adikisoobo ye anye. <verse eid="1SA 17:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="1SA 17:49" />Defid asịn ubọk ke ekpad amọ anyʌñ asio itiad, afʌñ anyʌñ atop atọ awo Filistia ado ke akoiso. Itiad ado amaatịkke adʌk anye akoiso, anye anyʌñ aduọ akʌp iso ke isọñ.<verse eid="1SA 17:49" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="1SA 17:50" />Ntoro ke Defid akedat ikañakpọ ye itiad akan awo Filistia ubọk; ke unana eduad ke ubọk amọ anye amaanua awo Filistia atọ anyʌñ awot anye.<verse eid="1SA 17:50" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="1SA 17:51" />Defid amaafeghe akeda awo Filistia ke idem. Anye amaamʌm eduad Filistia ado adʌt asio ke efọk. Ke anye amaakewot anye, anye amaakama eduad ado akpịkke anye iwuod.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 17:51">Ke mbon Filistia ekekịtte ke awo uko mmimọ akpa ammọ emaekanna iso efeeñe. <verse eid="1SA 17:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="1SA 17:52" />Ndin ideen Isrel ye Yuda emaedakka ke anyọñ ekpọk ukịbe enyʌñ efeeñe ebịne mbon Filistia tutu ekewuọ ntondʌk Kad<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:52 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido ke usʌk mme ikpañwed Septuakin; Ke Hibru ake abedeñ</char></note> ye inuaatob Ekrọn. Mbon ñkpa ammọ emaeduọññọ ke usʌñ Saaraim ye Kad ye Ekrọn. <verse eid="1SA 17:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="1SA 17:53" />Ke ini Isrel eketooho edibịne mbon Filistia edi, ammọ emaebịme itie nnaaekọñ ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 17:53" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" sid="1SA 17:54" />Defid amaaben iwuod awo Filistia ado anyọñ akaa ke Yeruselem; anye amaanyʌñ asịn ñkpọ ekọñ Filistia ado ke atayad amọ.<verse eid="1SA 17:54" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="55" style="v" sid="1SA 17:55" />Naña Sọọl aseeghe Defid naña awuọ akaa adikisoobo ye awo Filistia ado, anye amaabịp Abna, adaiso udịmekọñ amọ, “Abna, akparawa ako ado ayịn anie awo?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 17:55">Abna amaabọọrọ, “Maama uwem mfo, Adidem, ami ndiọọñọke.”<verse eid="1SA 17:55" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" sid="1SA 17:56" />Adidem amaabo, “Yem usʌñ diọọñọ ayịn awo se akparawa ami ado.”<verse eid="1SA 17:56" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" sid="1SA 17:57" />Akem ke Defid akesʌkkọ anyọñ adiwot awo Filistia ado adi, Abna amaaben anye adibịne Sọọl, kpa naña Defid akesʌk akama iwuod awo Filistia ado.<verse eid="1SA 17:57" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" sid="1SA 17:58" />Sọọl amaabịp anye, “Akparawa, afo ado ayịn anie awo?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 17:58">Defid amaabọọrọ, “Ami ndo ayịn ayịnufọk mfo Yesi ake Betlehem.”<verse eid="1SA 17:58" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 17" />
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="1SA 18" />
  <para style="s1">Sọọl Akop Ndịk abaña Defid</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 18:1" />Ke Defid amaaketañ ikọ ama ye Sọọl, ukpọñ Yọnatan amaadiyịre keed ye ukpọñ Defid, anye amaanyʌñ ama anye nte idem amọ. <verse eid="1SA 18:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 18:2" />Tọọñọ ke usen ado Sọọl amaanịm Defid ye anye inyʌññọ iyaak anye anyọñ ufọk abịne ekpək amọ. <verse eid="1SA 18:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 18:3" />Ndin Yọnatan amaanam edioomo ye Defid sia adooho anye amaanekke ama anye nte idem amọ. <verse eid="1SA 18:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 18:4" />Yọnatan amaasioño ewịra anye akesịneke ayaak anọ Defid, ye afọñidem amọ ye eduad ye utịgha ye ñkpahaisịn amọ.<verse eid="1SA 18:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 18:5" />Sutọ utom se Sọọl akedọdọñ anye, Defid amaanam anye anie edikan tutu ado se Sọọl anọ anye ekamba itie ke atu mbon ekọñ. Ñkpọ ami amaanem mbon ekọñ ye mme adaaha ekọñ Sọọl esịd ñko.<verse eid="1SA 18:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 18:6" />Ke ini mme ideen ado enyọññọ edi ke Defid amaakewot awo Filistia ado, ibaan emaewuọñọ ke afịd idʌñ ke Isrel ekesoobo ye Adidem Sọọl ekwọ ikwọ enyʌñ enek unek, ye ikwọ idaara ye ibịd ye ñkpọ mbre. <verse eid="1SA 18:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 18:7" />Naña ammọ ekenekke, ammọ emaekwọ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 18:7">“Sọọl awot ke mme tọsịn keed (1,000) amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 18:7">ndin Defid ke mme tọsịn duob (10,000) amọ.”<verse eid="1SA 18:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 18:8" />Esịd amaanekke ayat Sọọl; ikwọ ami amaanekke adiọọk anye esịd. “Ammọ ebat mme tọsịn duob (10,000) enọ Defid ado ebat mme tọsịn (1,000) kpọd edian ennọ miin. Nsoo mfen ke anye akeme adinie imiidooho abioubọọñ?” <verse eid="1SA 18:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 18:9" />Ndin tọọñọ ke ini ado kaa iso, Sọọl amaanekke atịñ anyen ase Defid.<verse eid="1SA 18:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 18:10" />Edem usen ado idiọọk<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Se ke 1 Sa 16:14</char></note> sịbidịd a-aketooho Abasi amaadidoro Sọọl ke idem. Anye amaatañ prọfesi ke ufọk amọ, ke ini Defid akebreke ndidoudʌk naña anye akesinam. Sọọl amaakama eduad ke ubọk. <verse eid="1SA 18:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 18:11" />Ndin Sọọl amaatop eduad ado, abo idem amọ, “Ami ñyaakịm Defid ndian ke ndibene.” Ado Defid amaafep anye akañ iba.<verse eid="1SA 18:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 18:12" />Sọọl amaakop ndịk abaña Defid sia adooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaaba ye Defid ado amaadakka akpọñ Sọọl. <verse eid="1SA 18:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 18:13" />Akem Sọọl amaabịne Defid asio akpọñ anye anyʌñ anam Defid etubom tọsịn ideen duob (10,000), ndin Defid amaadat mbon abio usʌñ ke mme anwan ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 18:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 18:14" />Ke afịd se Defid akenam anye amaanie edikan sia adooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaaba ye anye. <verse eid="1SA 18:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 18:15" />Ke ini Sọọl akekịtte naña anye anie edikan, anye amaabaak anye. <verse eid="1SA 18:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 18:16" />Ado afịd Isrel ye Yuda emaema Defid, sia adooho anye akewuọ iso anọ ammọ ke isañ ekọñ ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 18:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 18:17" />Sọọl amaabo Defid, “Sese Merab adiaha mmi. Ami ñyaayaak anye unọ fiin yak adọ; ukweeñe ñkpọ ado afo adinam ñkpọ innọ miin ye uko inyʌñ inwana mme ekọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.” Sia Sọọl amaakere ke esịd amọ, “Ami ndiidịppeke ubọk mmi ntuuk anye. Yak mbon Filistia enam ado!”<verse eid="1SA 18:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 18:18" />Ado Defid amaabo Sọọl, “Ami ndo anie awo, ñko ekpək mmi me ubon mmi edo nsoo ke Isrel, yak ado se ami ndiido ebe ayịn adidem?” <verse eid="1SA 18:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 18:19" />Ke ntoro<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18:19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido Kpa ye ado</char></note> ini akekem se enọ Merab adiaha Sọọl yak adọ Defid, emaekappa eben anye enọ Adriel awo Mehola ke ndọ.<verse eid="1SA 18:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 18:20" />Ado ayịn awonwaan Sọọl, Maikal amaama Defid, ndin ke ini etañña enọ Sọọl, amaanem anye esịd. <verse eid="1SA 18:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 18:21" />Sọọl amaakere, “Ami ñyaayaak Maikal nnọ Defid, nọ ato do Maikal aba nte afia anọ anye, ñko nọ ato do ubọk mbon Filistia adoro anye ke idem.” Ke ntoro, Sọọl amaabo Defid, “Idahami afo amenie ufañ mfen adido ukod mmi.”<verse eid="1SA 18:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 18:22" />Ndin Sọọl amaabo mbon utom amọ: “Ndufo etañ ikọ ye Defid ke ndịbe ebo, ‘Sese adidem uma fiin, ñko nditọutom amọ afịd uma fiin; ke ntak ado do ebe ayịn amọ.’ ”<verse eid="1SA 18:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 18:23" />Mme isʌñutom Sọọl emaetañ ikọ ami enọ Defid. Ado Defid amaabo, “Ndufo ekere ke amem awo adido ebe ayịn adidem? Ami ndo ayịn uweene ñko ami ndooho awuọ etob awo.”<verse eid="1SA 18:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 18:24" />Ke ini nditọufọk Sọọl edọkkọke anye se Defid abo, <verse eid="1SA 18:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 18:25" />Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “Tañ nọ Defid bo ke, ‘Adidem iyemme ekọmudua mfen nte ñkpọ ndọ ikan edʌd idem ideen mbon Filistia ikie, nọ adat ado asio usiene ye mme asua amọ.’ ” Uduak Sọọl akedo Defid adiduọ ndʌk ubọk mbon Filistia.<verse eid="1SA 18:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 18:26" />Ke ini mbon utom Sọọl ekedọkkọke Defid ñkpọ ami, esịd amaanem anye adido ebe ayịn adidem. Ñko mbemiso ini ekenọọhọ aboiyo, <verse eid="1SA 18:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 18:27" />Defid amaadat mme ideen amọ esaña keed ewuọ ekewot mbon Filistia ikie iba (200) eben edʌd idem ideen ammọ edi. Ammọ emaebat ayọhọ ibad enọ adidem nọ ato do Defid ado ebe ayịn amọ. Ndin Sọọl amaayaak ayịn amọ awonwaan Maikal anọ Defid ke ndọ.<verse eid="1SA 18:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 18:28" />Ke ini Sọọl akediọọñọke ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmọdo ye Defid ñko ke ayịn amọ awonwaan Maikal ama Defid, <verse eid="1SA 18:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 18:29" />Sọọl adineenekke abaak Defid, ndin anye ado asua amọ ke afịd usen uwem amọ.<verse eid="1SA 18:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 18:30" />Akem mme adaiso ekọñ mbon Filistia emaekaa iso enwana ekọñ, ñko kwa naña ammọ enwana, Defid amaanie edikan akan afịd mme ikpọawo Sọọl, ndin anyịñ amọ amaanyʌñ awuọ etob.<verse eid="1SA 18:30" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 18" />
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="1SA 19" />
  <para style="s1">Sọọl Anwana Adiwot Defid</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 19:1" />Sọọl amaadọkkọ Yọnatan ye afịd mbon utom amọ abo yak ewot Defid. Ado Yọnatan amaanekke ama Defid. <verse eid="1SA 19:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 19:2" />Yọnatan amaanyʌñ adʌt Defid utọñ abo, “Sọọl ete mmi ayem usʌñ naña uwot fiin. Kpeme idem ñkpọñ ubakusen; kaa ke yem itie dịbe ñnyʌñ ba do. <verse eid="1SA 19:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 19:3" />Ami ñyaawuọ ñkeda ye ete mmi ke inwañ a-afo abaaha. Ami ñyaadọkkọ anye ubaña fiin ñyaanyʌñ ndudọkkọ fiin se ido esịd amọ.”<verse eid="1SA 19:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 19:4" />Yọnatan amaatañ eti ikọ abaña Defid anọ ete amọ Sọọl amaanyʌñ abo anye, “Yak adidem akuunam Defid idiọọkñkpọ nte keed; anye udueghe fiin, ñko se anye anam aba ufọn unọ fiin eti-eti. <verse eid="1SA 19:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 19:5" />Anye akekama uwem amọ ke ubọk idaha anye akewotto awo Filistia ado. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanọ afịd Isrel ekamba adikan, ndin afo amaakịt anyʌñ anem esịd. Nsoo ndin ido ntak ake afo akpenamma awodeen nte Defid ammiidueghe, idiọọkñkpọ, ke adiwot anye ke unana ntak?”<verse eid="1SA 19:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 19:6" />Sọọl amaakpañ utọñ akop se Yọnatan aketañ anyʌñ ata unwọñọ abo: “Ke adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aduuho uwem, awo idiiwotto Defid.”<verse eid="1SA 19:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 19:7" />Ke emaaha ado Yọnatan amaakoot Defid adọkkọ anye afịd se ammọ ekeneme. Anye amaaben anye adibịne Sọọl, Defid akeba ye Sọọl nte naña akedo akpa.<verse eid="1SA 19:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 19:8" />Ini keed mfen ekọñ amaatịppe, Defid amaanyʌñ akenwana ye mbon Filistia. Anye amaawot ammọ tutu ammọ efeeñe ke iso amọ.<verse eid="1SA 19:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 19:9" />Ado idiọọk<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19:9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">See 1 Sa 16:14 ye mme itie mfen se etañ ebaña</char></note> sịbidịd a-atooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadidoro Sọọl ke idem ke ini anye aketieghe ke ufọk amọ akama eduad amọ ke ubọk. Ke ini Defid akebreke ndidoudʌk, <verse eid="1SA 19:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 19:10" />Sọọl amaanwana adikịm Defid ndian ke ndibene ye eduad amọ, ado naña Sọọl akekịmme eduad ado asịn ke ndibene, Defid amaafep. Akonayio ado Defid amaafeghe abọkkọ Sọọl.<verse eid="1SA 19:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 19:11" />Sọọl amaadọñ ideen ekaa ufọk Defid ekekpeme ndin ewot anye ubakusen. Ado Maikal, anwaan Defid amaadʌt anye utọñ, “Adieke afo umuufegheke uyem itọñ uwem mfo akonayio ami, ñkpọñ ayaakpa.” <verse eid="1SA 19:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 19:12" />Ke ntoro Maikal amaasuuk Defid asio ke ubenafịm ndin anye afeghe asop. <verse eid="1SA 19:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 19:13" />Ndin Maikal amaaben ubobodñkpọ anịm ke akwañ nnaa amọ, amaaben ewịra afʌk anyʌñ aben ided ebod adot ke iwuod amọ.<verse eid="1SA 19:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 19:14" />Ke ini Sọọl akedọññọ ideen yak ekemʌm Defid, Maikal amaabo, “Idem isọññọ anye.” <verse eid="1SA 19:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 19:15" />Ndin Sọọl amaadọñ ideen ado etịmme eka ekekịt Defid anyʌñ abo ammọ, “Iben anye insọk miin ke ñkpana amọ nọ ami ñwot anye.” <verse eid="1SA 19:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 19:16" />Ado ke ini ideen ado edʌkkọ eka, ubobodñkpọ mmọ ke akwañ adoro, ñko ke iwuod amọ akedo ided ebod.<verse eid="1SA 19:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 19:17" />Sọọl amaabo Maikal, “Ntak afo akembiañake miin ntom-o anyʌñ asio asua mmi yak afeghe asop?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 19:17">Maikal amaabo anye, “Anye akembo miin, ‘yak ami mfeghe ñwuọ. Ntaha ami ñkpuwotto fiin-e?’ ”<verse eid="1SA 19:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 19:18" />Ke ini Defid akefegheke abọkkọ, anye amaadibịne Samwel ke Rama akedọkkọ anye afịd se Sọọl akenam anye. Ndin anye ye Samwel emaedaaña ekaiya Naiyọd ekeba do. <verse eid="1SA 19:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 19:19" />Etob amaadisịm Sọọl ke, “Defid mmọdo ke Naiyọd ke Rama”; <verse eid="1SA 19:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 19:20" />ke ntoro anye amaadọñ ideen yak ekemʌm Defid. Ado ammọ ekekịt mme prọfed nte eda etañ uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ye Samwel ke atu ammọ nte adaiwuod, Sịbidịd Abasi amaadʌk mme ideen Sọọl ke idem, ammọ ñko emaetañ uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 19:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 19:21" />Emaeketañ se ikiba enọ Sọọl, ndin anye amaadọñ ideen mfen ewakka ekan ado, ammọ emaenyʌñ etañ uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñko. Sọọl amaamaana adọñ ideen ayọhọ akañ ita, ammọ ekesʌk etatañ uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 19:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 19:22" />Ke akpatre, anye amaadakka ke idem amọ akaa Rama anyʌñ akaa ekamba ube mmọọñ a-abaaha ke Seku. Anye amaanyʌñ abịp, “Samwel ye Defid ebañña ke uke?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 19:22">Ammọ emaebo, “Ko ke Naiyọd ke Rama.”<verse eid="1SA 19:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 19:23" />Ke ntoro Sọọl amaadika Naiyọd ke Rama. Ado Sịbidịd Abasi amaadidoro anye ñko ke idem, anye amaasaña atañ prọfesi tutu anye akesịm Naiyọd. <verse eid="1SA 19:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 19:24" />Anye amaasịññe afọñ amọ, anye amaanyʌñ atañ prọfesi ke iso Samwel. Anye akenaa ifed afịd uweemeayio ado ye afịd akonayio ado. Ntak ami anam mme awo ebo, “Nte Sọọl ñko akeene asịne ke atu mme prọfed?”<verse eid="1SA 19:24" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 19" />
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="1SA 20" />
  <para style="s1">Defid ye Yọnatan</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 20:1" />Ndin Defid amaafeghe akpọñ Naiyọd ke Rama adibịne Yọnatan akebịp, “Nsoo ke ami nnam? Nsoo ido ndudue mmi? Ndue die ete mfo yak ado se anye ayem adiñwot miin?”<verse eid="1SA 20:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 20:2" />Yọnatan amaabọọrọ, “Tutu amama! Afo uduukpaaha! Se, ete mmi isinamma ñkpọ ndomokeed, ekamba me etək, ke anye imiinamma yak ami ndiọọñọ. Ntaha anye akpendịppe miin anye ami-e? Idooho ntoro!”<verse eid="1SA 20:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 20:3" />Ado Defid amaata unwọñọ abo, “Ete mfo adiọọñọ mfọn-mfọn ke ami mmekịt mfọn ke iso mfo, ndin anye abo idem amọ ‘Inaaha Yọnatan adiọọñọ abaña ami imiidooho anye ayaafʌhọ.’ Ado adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aduuho uwem afo anyʌñ adu uwem, ikpad keed aba ke ufọọd mmi ye ñkpa.”<verse eid="1SA 20:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 20:4" />Yọnatan amaabo Defid, “Se adodo ake afo ayemme ami nam unọ, ami ñyaanam unọ.”<verse eid="1SA 20:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 20:5" />Ke ntoro Defid amaabo Yọnatan, “Sese, ñkpọñ ado usọrọ Ufa Afiọñ, ndin akpena nte ami ndia udia ye adidem; ado yak ñka ñkedịbe ke inwañ tutu ndubiayio edem ñkpọñ amaaboiyo. <verse eid="1SA 20:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 20:6" />Adieke ete mfo añyemme miin ke usʌñ ndomokeed, bo anye, ‘Defid amaanekke añkpeiye miin abo yak ikaa Betlehem, abio amọ, sia adooho esʌk enam uwa afịd isua do enọ afịd ubon amọ.’ <verse eid="1SA 20:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 20:7" />Adieke anye abooho ‘A-anekke afọn,’ awuọñọ ayịnufọk mfo a-abọkkọ. Ado adieke anye awọttọ iyadesịd, afo ayaadiọọñọ ke anye a-abiide adinnọmọ miin. <verse eid="1SA 20:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 20:8" />Amaado afo, wọt ayịnufọk mfo mfọn, sia afo amedʌk edioomo ye anye ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Adieke adooho ami mmedue, ñwot miin ke idem mfo! Ntak a-afo añyaaha miin anọọ ete mfo-o?”<verse eid="1SA 20:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 20:9" />Yọnatan amaabo, “Tutu amama! Akpedo ami mmaanie ataa etək ifiọk mbaña ke ete mmi abiide aduwot fiin, nte ami ñkpudọkkọke fiin?”<verse eid="1SA 20:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 20:10" />Defid amaabịp Yọnatan ate, “Anie adindọkkọ miin adieke ete mfo ubọọrọke fiin uyad-uyad?”<verse eid="1SA 20:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 20:11" />Yọnatan amaabo Defid, “Di! Yak ñnyịn isaña keed ika inwañ.” Ndin ammọ emaesaña ntoro ekaa inwañ.<verse eid="1SA 20:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 20:12" />Ndin Yọnatan amaabo Defid, “Ami mmenwọñọ ke anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi Isrel, mbo ke akpanikọ ke ami ñyaatañ esịd ete mmi unọ fiin idaha ntom edem ñkpọñ! Adieke anye adiifọn ye afo, ado nte ami ndiinọọhọ etob ñnyʌñ nnam afo adiọọñọ? <verse eid="1SA 20:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 20:13" />Ado adieke ete mmi ayemme adunam fiin ibak, yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amia Yọnatan ufen, ekamba, adieke ami mmennamma yak afo adiọọñọ ñnyʌñ nnam yak afo anyọñ ke emem. Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aba ye afo kpa naña anye aba ye ete mmi. <verse eid="1SA 20:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 20:14" />Ado ñwọt miin mfọnido nte mfọnido ake <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adaña ini nte ami mbaaha ke uwem, mbaak ediñwot miin, <verse eid="1SA 20:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 20:15" />kuunyʌñ utre mfọnido mfo ye ekpək mmi, akpọkọm idaha <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakpịkke afịd mme asua Defid isio ke iso isọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 20:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 20:16" />Ke ntoro, Yọnatan amaanam edioomo ye ufọk Defid, abo, “Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> asio usiene ye mme asua Defid.” <verse eid="1SA 20:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 20:17" />Ñko Yọnatan amaanam Defid amaana asọọñọ unwọñọ amọ ke ima anọ anye, sia adooho anye amaama anye nte naña anye akema idem amọ.<verse eid="1SA 20:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 20:18" />Ndin Yọnatan amaabo Defid, “Ñkpọñ ado usọrọ Ufa Afiọñ. Eyauyem fiin, sia ñkpọitie mfo adiina ukpọk. <verse eid="1SA 20:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 20:19" />Edem ñkpọñ, ke idaha ndubiayio, kaa itie a-afo akedịbeke ke ini mfịna ami aketọọñọke, nyʌñ kaa kebet ke itie itiad Esel. <verse eid="1SA 20:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 20:20" />Ami ñyaatop idañ ita ke mben amọ nte ntop ñkpọ se ñkịt. <verse eid="1SA 20:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 20:21" />Ndin ami ñyaadọñ etəkayịn awodeen mbo, ‘Kaa keyem mme idañ ado.’ Adieke mbooho anye, ‘Se ke idañ ado aba ke mbeñ ubọk mfo umi,’ ndin di, sia adooho adaña ini nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aduuho uwem afo amebọkkọ, ikọ inyʌññọ iba. <verse eid="1SA 20:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 20:22" />Ado adieke mbooho akparawa ado ‘Se ke idañ ado uboiyo fiin,’ ana afo aka sia adooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ubịne fiin asio. <verse eid="1SA 20:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 20:23" />Ndin ke abaña ñkpọ se ami ye afo ikineme, toiyo ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado ntiense ñnyịn ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="1SA 20:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 20:24" />Ke ntoro Defid amaadịbe ke inwañ, ndin ke ini usọrọ Ufa Afiọñ amaakedi, adidem amaasuuk atie adidia ñkpọ. <verse eid="1SA 20:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 20:25" />Adidem amaatie ke itie a-anye asitieghe ke mben ndibene a-asakkaiso ase Yọnatan, ndin Abna amaatie adiana Sọọl, ado itie Defid akena ukpọk. <verse eid="1SA 20:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 20:26" />Sọọl ikitañña ikọ nte keed usen ado, sia anye akekere ke anie se itịppe inọ Defid a-anamma yak anye imiisanake, ke akpanikọ, ana ado anye isanake. <verse eid="1SA 20:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 20:27" />Ado edem usen ado, ayọhọ usen iba ke afiọñ, itie Defid akesʌk ana ukpọk. Ndin Sọọl amaabo Yọnatan ayịn amọ, “Nsoo inam yak ayịn Yesi imiidieghe usọrọ, mfịn me ñkpọñ a-akeboiyoke?”<verse eid="1SA 20:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 20:28" />Yọnatan amaabọọrọ Sọọl, “Defid amaanekke ambeeñe miin abo yak imọ ika Betlehem. <verse eid="1SA 20:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 20:29" />Anye amaabo, ‘Yak ami ñka, sia adooho ekpək ñnyịn eyem inam uwa ke abio ñko ayịneka mmi awodeen abo ke ana ami mba do. Adieke ami ñkịtte mfọn ke iso mfo, yak ami ñka ñkekịt nditọeka mmi ideen.’ Ntak ado anam anye idiighe ididia ñkpọ ke akpokoro adidem.”<verse eid="1SA 20:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 20:30" />Sọọl amaabịmme iyadesịd ye Yọnatan ndin anye amaabo anye, “Afo ayịn ukwañ ye atreutọñ awonwaan ami! Ado nte ami ndiọọñọke ke afo ada ye ayịn Yesi adat ndọk asọk idem mfo ye eka a-akumanna fiin? <verse eid="1SA 20:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1SA 20:31" />Adaña nte ayịn Yesi aduuho ke ederimbod, afo me abioubọọñ mfo idiisọọñọke ida. Idahami dọñ awo yak aben anye ansọk miin, sia ana anye akpa!”<verse eid="1SA 20:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="1SA 20:32" />Yọnatan amaabịp Sọọl, ete amọ, abo, “Nsoo ido ntak afo ayemme adiwot anye? Nsoo ke anye anam?” <verse eid="1SA 20:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="1SA 20:33" />Ado Sọọl amaatop eduad amọ ayem adiwot anye. Do ke Yọnatan adiọọñọ ke ete imọ ayem adiwot Defid.<verse eid="1SA 20:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="1SA 20:34" />Yọnatan amaadakka akpọñ akpokoro ado ke akpọsọñ ifiobesịd; ke usen usọrọ ado ayọhọ iba anye ikidiaha ñkpọ, sia anye amaafʌhọ abaña naña ete amọ akenam ñkpọ ndọk-ndọk ye Defid.<verse eid="1SA 20:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="1SA 20:35" />Ke ubakusen, Yọnatan amaawuọ akaa inwañ adikisoobo ye Defid. Anye amaaben etəkayịn awodeen asaña keed, <verse eid="1SA 20:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="1SA 20:36" />ndin anye amaabo etəkayịn awodeen ado, “Feghe kaa keyem mme idañ ake ami antoppo do.” Naña ayịn ado afeghe aka, anye amaatop idañ abọhọ anye. <verse eid="1SA 20:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="1SA 20:37" />Ke ini ayịn ado akesịmme itie idañ Yọnatan akeduọhọ, Yọnatan amaada akoot anye, “Nte idañ ado inaaha ke iso mfo?” <verse eid="1SA 20:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="1SA 20:38" />Ndin Yọnatan amaabọñ “Sọsọp! Sọp kaa! Kuutre!” Ayịn awodeen ado amaaben idañ atịmme abịne eteufọk amọ. <verse eid="1SA 20:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="1SA 20:39" />(Ayịn awodeen ado ikidiọọñọke ñkpọ ndomokeed ibaña afịd ami; Yọnatan ye Defid ikpọọñ ekediọọñọ.) <verse eid="1SA 20:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="1SA 20:40" />Ndin Yọnatan amaanọ ayịn ado mme ñkpọ ekọñ amọ anyʌñ abo, “Ben ammọ tịmme nyọñ abio.”<verse eid="1SA 20:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="1SA 20:41" />Ke ayịn ado amaakenyọñ, Defid amaadakka ada ke usuuk-usuuk edem itiad anyʌñ anuuk iwuod anọ Yọnatan akañ ita, iso amọ ase isọñ. Ndin ammọ emaetʌm emọ-emọ inua enyʌñ etua, ado Defid aketua akan.<verse eid="1SA 20:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="1SA 20:42" />Yọnatan amaabo Defid, “Kaa ke emem, sia adooho ñnyịn awo iba iminwọñọ adido ufan ke anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ibo, ‘<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado ntiense ke ufọọd mmi ye afo, ñko ke ufọọd emana mmi ye emana mfo ke nsi-nsi.’ ” Ndin Defid amaakpọñ, ñko Yọnatan atịmme anyọñ abio<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20:42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke ikpañwed Hibru udịmikọ ami a-adooho 1 Sam 20:24 ewet 1 Sa 21:1.</char></note>.<verse eid="1SA 20:42" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 20" />
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="1SA 21" />
  <para style="s1">Defid ke Nọb</para>
  <para style="p">
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">21: </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke ikpañwed Hibru udịmikọ ami a-adooho 1 Sa 21:1-15 ewet 1 Sa 21:2-16.</char>
    </note> <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 21:1" />Defid amaakaa Nọb, abịne Ahimelek a-akedooho aku. Ahimelek amaadịkke ke ini anye akịtte Defid amaanyʌñ abịp, “Nsoo inam afo asaña ikpọọñ? Nsoo ido awo imiisañake ye afo?”<verse eid="1SA 21:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 21:2" />Defid amaabọọrọ Ahimelek a-akedooho aku abo, “Adidem andọñ miin utom anyʌñ ambo, ‘Inaaha awo adiọọñọ abaña utom ami udọññọ fiin mi.’ Akpedo ideen mmi, mmebo ammọ yak edi embịne ke itie keed. <verse eid="1SA 21:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 21:3" />Ndin idahami, nsoo ke afo anie ke ubọk? Nnọ miin ebok uyo ition, me ñkpọ keed akeedodo se iba.”<verse eid="1SA 21:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 21:4" />Ado aku amaabọọrọ Defid ate, “Ami nnieghe ñkaña uyo ke ubọk; ado naña adodo adisana uyo mmọdo aba mi, ado yak ado ke ideen ado inaaha ye ibaan.”<verse eid="1SA 21:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 21:5" />Defid amaabọọrọ aku, “Ke akpanikọ esiben ibaan ikpọñ ñnyịn ini keed akeedodo ami ñwuọhọ. Ideen edo ndisana akpekọm ammọ eka utom i-imiisanake. Nwaanwa dise ndin ke utom usen mfịn!” <verse eid="1SA 21:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 21:6" />Ke ntoro aku amaanọ anye adisana uyo, sia uyo mfen imiikibaaha do ibọhọke Uyo Iso Abasi ekebenne esio ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ekenyʌññọ enịm ufiob uyo ke usen ekebenne esio.<verse eid="1SA 21:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 21:7" />Ndin ayịnufọk Sọọl keed mmọdo akeba usen ado, ekekọp anye enịm ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; anye akedo Dook awo Edọm, etubom mme akpemeedọñ Sọọl.<verse eid="1SA 21:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 21:8" />Defid amaabịp Ahimelek, “Afo unieghe eduad me akañkañ mi? Ami ñkikamake akañkañ mmi me ñkpọ ekọñ mfen ndomokeed ndi, sia adooho utom adidem akedo usọp-usọp.”<verse eid="1SA 21:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 21:9" />Aku amaabọọrọ, “Akañkañ Koloyad awo Filistia a-afo akewotto ke Abedeñ Ela mmọ mi; e-ewañ anye ke afọñ enịm ke edem afọñ aboditọñ. Akpedo afo ameyem anye, ben; akañkañ mfen ibaaha mi ke imiibọhọke anye ado.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 21:9">Defid amaabo, “Ibaaha se iba nte anye ado; ben anye nnọ miin.”<verse eid="1SA 21:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Defid ke Kad</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 21:10" />Usen ado Defid amaafeghe abọkkọ Sọọl adibịne Akis adidem Kad. <verse eid="1SA 21:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 21:11" />Ado nditọufọk Akis emaebo anye, “Idooho Defid ido ami, adidem isọñ ami? Idooho anye ke ammọ ekwọ ebaña ke unek ammọ:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 21:11">“ ‘Sọọl awot ake amọ ke mme tọsịn keed,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 21:11">ado Defid awot ake amọ ke mme tọsịn duob’?”<verse eid="1SA 21:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 21:12" />Defid amaaben ikọ ami asịn ke esịd ndin idem anyeñ anye abaña Akis adidem Kad. <verse eid="1SA 21:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 21:13" />Ke ntoro anye amaanam ñkpọ nte awo iwuod imiifọnnọ ke iso ammọ; ndin ke idaha anye asịneke ke ubọk ammọ anye anam nte ido idaad, aduut ñkpọ ke inuaatob ado anyʌñ anam etab atọi anye ke ñwaebek.<verse eid="1SA 21:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 21:14" />Akis amaabo nditọufọk amọ “Sese ete ami! Iwuod amọ ifọnnọ! Nsoo inam eben anye ensọk miin? <verse eid="1SA 21:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 21:15" />Ado nte ami mmenekke nnana mme idaad yak ado se ndufo eben awo ami edi yak adinam utọ ñkpọ ami ke iso mmi? Ana nte awo ami adʌk adi ufọk mmi?”<verse eid="1SA 21:15" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 21" />
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="1SA 22" />
  <para style="s1">Defid ke Adulam ye ke Mispa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 22:1" />Defid amaakpọñ Kad afeghe abọkkọ akaa abaitiad ke Adulam. Ke ini nditọeka amọ ideen ye mbon ufọk ete amọ ekoppo ebaña, ammọ emaekaa ebịne anye do. <verse eid="1SA 22:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 22:2" />Afịd mbon nnananyen ye mbon isʌñ ye afịd awo se imiikoppo uyʌkkọ emaeda ekanna anye, ndin anye akedo adaiso ammọ. Ñkpọ nte ideen ikie inaañ (400) ekebañña ye anye.<verse eid="1SA 22:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 22:3" />Ake adakka do Defid amaadika Mispa ke Mọb anyʌñ akebo adidem Mọb “Afo akpaayak ete ye eka mmi ediba ye afo tutu ami ndiọọñọ se Abasi adiinam ye ami?” <verse eid="1SA 22:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 22:4" />Ke ntoro anye amaakpọñ ammọ ye adidem Mọb, ndin ammọ emaeba ye anye ke adaña ini Defid akebaaha ke akpọsọñ itie amọ.<verse eid="1SA 22:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 22:5" />Ado prọfed Kad amaabo Defid, “Kuutie ke akpọsọñ itie. Dakka kaa isọñ Yuda.” Defid ndin amaadakka anyʌñ akaa akai Hered.<verse eid="1SA 22:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Sọọl Awot mme Aku ake Nọb</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 22:6" />Akem Sọọl amaakop ke emaekịt Defid ye mme ideen amọ. Ndin Sọọl mmọdo aketie, akama eduad ke ubọk, ke idak eto tamaris ke abod ke Kibie, ye mbon utom amọ ke ñkañ amọ. <verse eid="1SA 22:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 22:7" />Sọọl amaabo ammọ, “Ikpañ utọñ, mme ideen Benyamin! Nte ayịn Yesi ayainọ afịd ndufo mme inwañ ye mme inwañ fain? Nte anye ayaanam ndufo edo mme adaiso mme tọsịn (1,000) ye mme adaiso mme ikie (100)? <verse eid="1SA 22:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 22:8" />Ntak ado anam nọ afịd ndufo edʌk adu ibak embaña miin? Ibaaha awo se indọkkọ miin idaha ayịn mmi anamma edioomo ye ayịn Yesi. Ibaaha awo ndufo se ikere ñkpọ imbaña miin me indọkkọ miin ibo ke akpan mmi adọñ ayịnufọk mmi abo adịbe ambet nọ ato do anye annam miin ñkpọ, naña anye anam mfịn ami.”<verse eid="1SA 22:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 22:9" />Ado Dook awo Edọm, a-akedaaha ye mbon utom Sọọl, amaabo, “Ami mmaakịt ayịn Yesi naña adibịne Ahimelek ayịn Ahitub ke Nọb. <verse eid="1SA 22:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 22:10" />Ahimelek amaabịp se ido uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anọ anye; anye amaanyʌñ anọ anye eduad Koloyad awo Filistia.”<verse eid="1SA 22:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 22:11" />Ndin adidem amaadọñ ekoot Ahimelek ayịn Ahitub a-akedooho aku ye afịd ideen ke ekpək ammọ, e-ekedoññoke aku ke Nọb, afịd ammọ emaenyʌñ edi ebịne adidem. <verse eid="1SA 22:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 22:12" />Sọọl amaabo, “Kpañ utọñ idahami, ayịn Ahitub.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 22:12">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Ii abọọñ mmi.”<verse eid="1SA 22:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 22:13" />Sọọl amaabo anye, “Nsoo inam afo adʌk adu ambaña miin, afo ye ayịn Yesi, anọ anye uyo ye eduad amaana abịp iso Abasi anọ anye, nọ ato do anye atreutọñ ye ami anyʌñ ada ambet miin, ukem-ukem naña anye anam mfịn ami?”<verse eid="1SA 22:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 22:14" />Ahimelek amaabọọrọ adidem abo, “Anie ke atu nditọufọk mfo inam akpanikọ nte Defid, ebe ayịn adidem, etubom mbon ukpeme mfo ye awo a-anieghe ukpono eti-eti ke atu ufọk mfo? <verse eid="1SA 22:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 22:15" />Nte usen ado akedo akpa ami ñkeyemme iso Abasi nnọ anye? Ke akpanikọ idooho! Ke adidem adot ayịnufọk amọ uyio me mbon ufọk ete amọ ndomokeed, sia ayịnufọk mfo idiọọñọke ñkpọ ndomokeed ibaña se itịppe ami.”<verse eid="1SA 22:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 22:16" />Ado adidem amaabo, “Ahimelek ana nte afo akpa, afo ye afịd ufọk mfo.”<verse eid="1SA 22:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 22:17" />Ndin adidem amaabo mbon ukpeme e-ekedaaha ke ñkañ amọ: “Iwọññọ iwoot mme aku <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> sia ammọ ñko eda ke ñkañ Defid. Ammọ emaediọọñọ ke anye afefeghe ado ammọ indọkkọke.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 22:17">Ado mbon utom adidem ikiyemme edidịppe ubọk ñwot mme aku <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="1SA 22:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 22:18" />Ndin adidem amaanọ Dook uyio abo, “Afo kanna kịm mme aku woot.” Ke ntoro Dook awo Edọm amaakanna akuum ammọ abono. Usen ado anye amaawot ideen anaañ mme ition e-ekesịneke afọñ aboditọñ ake linen. <verse eid="1SA 22:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 22:19" />Anye amaanyʌñ adat akañkañ asobo Nọb, abio mme aku, ye mme ideen ye ibaan ammọ, mme ntəkayịn ye mme nsekayịn ye mme enañ ye mme dọñki ye mme edọñ ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 22:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 22:20" />Ado ayịn Ahimelek ayịn Ahitub keed, a-akekereke Abiata amaabọkkọ afeghe akediana ye Defid. <verse eid="1SA 22:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 22:21" />Abiata amaadọkkọ Defid ke Sọọl amaawot mme aku <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="1SA 22:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 22:22" />Ndin Defid amaabo Abiata, “Usen ado, ke ini Dook awo Edọm akebaaha do, ami mmaadiọọñọ ke anye ayaadọkkọ Sọọl. Ami ndo ntak ñkpa afịd ekpək ndufo. <verse eid="1SA 22:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 22:23" />Ba ye ami; kuukop ndịk. Awo akeedodo a-ayemme uwot fiin ayem iñwot miin ñko. Afo ayaabọkkọ ye ami.”<verse eid="1SA 22:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 22" />
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="1SA 23" />
  <para style="s1">Defid Anyaaña Keila</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 23:1" />Ke ini ekedọkkọke Defid ebo, “Sese, mbon Filistia esʌk enwana ekọñ ye mbon Keila ñko esʌk ebịme afe ubeek abakpa ammọ,” <verse eid="1SA 23:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 23:2" />Defid amaabịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abo, “Ami ñka ñkenwana ye mbon Filistia ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 23:2">
    <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo anye, “Kaa ke anwana ye mbon Filistia ami nyʌñ nyaaña Keila.”<verse eid="1SA 23:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 23:3" />Ado mme ideen Defid emaebo anye, “Mi ke Yuda ñnyịn isʌk ikop ndịk. Nwaanwa dise, adieke ñnyịn ikaaha Keila ikinwana ye mbon ekọñ Filistia!”<verse eid="1SA 23:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 23:4" />Ini keed mfen Defid amaabịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabọọrọ anye, “Sọiyọ kaa ke Keila, sia ami ñyaayaak mbon Filistia usịn fiin ke ubọk.” <verse eid="1SA 23:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 23:5" />Ke ntoro, Defid ye mme ideen amọ emaekaiya Keila, ekenwana ye mbon Filistia enyʌñ ekoono ufene ammọ. Anye amaanịm ekamba unọmọ anọ mbon Filistia ado anyaaña mbon Keila <verse eid="1SA 23:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 23:6" />(Ndin Abiata ayịn Ahimelek amaaben afọñ aboditọñ akama akaa Keila idaha anye afegheke abịne Defid ke Keila.)<verse eid="1SA 23:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Sọọl Abịne Defid</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 23:7" />Emaedọkkọ Sọọl ke Defid aka Keila, ndin anye amaabo, “Abasi ayaak anye ansịn miin ke ubọk, sia adooho Defid asịn idem amọ ke ñkpakọb ke anye adifeghe ñkaa abio a-anieghe itịm ye eto usịn usʌñ.” <verse eid="1SA 23:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 23:8" />Akem Sọọl amaakoot afịd mbon ekọñ amọ abo ediika ekọñ, yak esuuhọ eka Keila ekekanna Defid ye mbon amọ ekʌk.<verse eid="1SA 23:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 23:9" />Ke ini Defid akekoppo ke Sọọl asʌk aduak idiọọkñkpọ ibaña imọ, anye amaabo Abiata a-akedooho aku, “Ben afọñ aboditọñ ado di.” <verse eid="1SA 23:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 23:10" />Defid amaabo, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi Isrel, ayịnufọk mfo akop ke akpanikọ ke Sọọl aduak adidi Keila adisobo abio ado ke ntak mmi. <verse eid="1SA 23:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 23:11" />Mbon se ito Keila eyaesuuk iwuod enọ anye? Sọọl ayaasọiyọ idi naña ayịnufọk mfo akop? <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi Isrel tañ wọt awo mfo.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 23:11">Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>amaabo, “Anye ayaadi.”<verse eid="1SA 23:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 23:12" />Defid amaana abịp, “Mbon e-etooho Keila eyaeñyaak miin ye mme ideen mmi enọ Sọọl?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 23:12">Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabo, “Ammọ eyaiyaak.”<verse eid="1SA 23:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 23:13" />Ke ntoro Defid ye ideen amọ, e-ekeyọhọke ñkpọ nte ikie itiokeed (600), emaekpọñ Keila ekaa iso esaña ke itie ke itie. Ke ini ekedọkkọke Sọọl ebo ke Defid amaafeghe akpọñ Keila, anye ikiikaaha do aba.<verse eid="1SA 23:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 23:14" />Defid akedʌñ ke akpọsọñ itie ke anaan ikọd ye ke abod Akpautatan Siif. Ke usen ke usen Sọọl amaakaa iso ayem anye, ado Abasi ikiyakka Defid isịn anye ke ubọk.<verse eid="1SA 23:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 23:15" />Idaha Defid akebaaha ke Hores ke Akpautatan Siif, anye amaakop ke<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23:15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido idem amaanyeñ anye sia</char></note> Sọọl amaadi adidat uwem imọ. <verse eid="1SA 23:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 23:16" />Ñko ayịn Sọọl Yọnatan amaakaa abịne Defid ke Hores akenwam anye adisọọñọ idem ke Abasi. <verse eid="1SA 23:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 23:17" />Anye amaabo, “Kuukop ndịk. Sọọl ete mmi iduutuuho fiin ubọk. Afo ayaado adidem ke Isrel, ndin ami ñyaado udiana mfo. Kpa ete mmi Sọọl adiọọñọ ntoro.” <verse eid="1SA 23:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 23:18" />Ammọ awo iba emaenam edioomo ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Ndin Yọnatan amaanyọñ ufọk ado Defid amaasuuk aba ke Hores.<verse eid="1SA 23:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 23:19" />Mbon Siif emaedakka edọọk ebịne Sọọl ke Kibie enyʌñ ekebo, “Nte Defid idịbeke ke atu ñnyịn ke akpọsọñ itie ke Hores, ke abod Hakila, ke edem Yesimọn? <verse eid="1SA 23:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 23:20" />Sọiyọ di adidem ñnyịn, ini akeedodo a-afo amaaha adidi, ndin adiido ubiọñutom ñnyịn adiyaak anye usịn fiin ke ubọk.”<verse eid="1SA 23:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 23:21" />Sọọl amaabọọrọ, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> idiọñ ndufo naña ndufo ekere embaña miin. <verse eid="1SA 23:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 23:22" />Ndufo ikaa ikibọ afịd etob ibaña anye. Iduuñọ idiọọñọ nte Defid asika ye mbon se isikịt anye do. Ammọ endọkkọ miin ebo ke anye akara ñkara eti-eti. <verse eid="1SA 23:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 23:23" />Iduuñọ idiọọñọ afịd itie udịbe se anye asiba ndin itịmme imbịne miin ye akpanikọ. Ndin ami ñyaikeene ndufo ñkaa; adieke anye abaaha ke isọñ ado, ami ñyaayem anye nsio ke afịd esiin idịd Yuda.”<verse eid="1SA 23:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 23:24" />Ndin ammọ emaedọñ idem eboiyo Sọọl iso ekaa Siif. Idaha ntom Defid ye ideen amọ ekeba ke Akpautatan Maon, ke Araba edem usuuk Yesimọn. <verse eid="1SA 23:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 23:25" />Sọọl ye ikọd amọ emaetọọñọ uyeb, ndin ke ini edọkkọke Defid ebaña, anye amaasọiyọ akaa ekamba itiad keed akeba ke Akpautatan Maon. Ke ini Sọọl akekoppo ami anye amaadika Akpautatan Maon adibịne Defid.<verse eid="1SA 23:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 23:26" />Sọọl amaakesaña ke mbeñ ekamba abod ñkañ keed, ndin Defid ye ikọd amọ ekeba ke mbeñ ñkañ uko, eyem usʌñ usọp-usọp naña efeghe ebọkkọ Sọọl. Ke Sọọl ye ikọd amọ emaekekpere Defid ye ikọd amọ adimʌm ammọ, <verse eid="1SA 23:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 23:27" />asañautom amaabịne Sọọl adibo, “Sọp idem di! Mbon Filistia ebịme edọñọ abio.” <verse eid="1SA 23:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 23:28" />Ndin Sọọl amaatịmme akpọñ adibịne Defid anyʌñ adika adisoobo ye mbon Filistia. Ntak e-ekoodo itie ami Sela Hamalekod<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23:28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Sela Hamalekod awuọñọ itiad ubakka</char></note> adodo. <verse eid="1SA 23:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 23:29" />Defid amaanyʌñ awuọ akpọñ ndo akedʌñ ke akpọsọñ itie ake En Kedi.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23:29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Hibru ufañ ami 1 Sa 23:29 ewet nte 1 Sa 24:1</char></note><verse eid="1SA 23:29" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 23" />
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="1SA 24" />
  <para style="s1">Defid Asuuk Uwem Sọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">24: </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Hibru ufañ ami 1 Sa 24:1-22 ewet nte 1 Sa 24:2-23</char>
    </note> <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 24:1" />Ke Sọọl amaakenyọñ adibịne mbon Filistia adi, emaedọkkọ anye ebo “Defid aba ke Akpautatan En Kedi.” <verse eid="1SA 24:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 24:2" />Ndin Sọọl amaaben iwaad esọññọ idem, awo tọsịn ita (3,000) ato ke afịd Isrel anyʌñ adakka isañ adikiyem Defid ye ikọd amọ ke ñkpere mme abaitiad itie mme Ebod Ikọd.<verse eid="1SA 24:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 24:3" />Anye amaadisịm mme abaedọñ e-ebaññake ke usʌñ; abaitiad amaaba do, ndin Sọọl amaadʌk akaa adikikeñ idem. Defid ye ideen amọ ekeba ke ataa edem abaitiad ado. <verse eid="1SA 24:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 24:4" />Ideen ado emaebo, “Mfịn ado usen <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aketañña abaña idaha anye akubooho, fiin ‘Ami ñyaayaak mme asua mfo usịn fiin ke ubọk yak afo anam ammọ naña afo ama.’ ” Ndin Defid asọọp ke ndịbe akekpịkke mben afọñ Sọọl.<verse eid="1SA 24:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 24:5" />Akema ado esịd amaaduọ Defid ke anye adikpịkke mben afọñidem Sọọl. <verse eid="1SA 24:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 24:6" />Anye amaabo ideen amọ, “<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akan ami adinam eteufọk mmi utọ ñkpọ ado, awo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayette adan, me adituuk anye ubọk; sia adooho anye ado awo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayet adan.” <verse eid="1SA 24:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 24:7" />Ke ikọ ami Defid amaasua anọ mme ideen amọ usọp-usọp. Ñko ikiyakka ammọ enwana ye Sọọl. Ndin Sọọl amaakpọñ abaitiad ado akaa uwa amọ.<verse eid="1SA 24:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 24:8" />Ndin Defid amaawuọ ke abaitiad akeda abọọñ akoot Sọọl, “Adidem abọọñ mmi!” Ke ini Sọọl akannake anyen ase edem, Defid amaanyuuk iwuod asịn ke isọñ anyʌñ aduọ asịn iso ke isọñ. <verse eid="1SA 24:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 24:9" />Anye amaabo Sọọl, “Ntak a-afo asinịmme ke awo amaubo fiin ‘Defid a-abiide adunọmọ fiin’? <verse eid="1SA 24:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 24:10" />Usen mfịn afo amekịt ke anyen mfo naña <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> uyaak fiin ansịn miin ke ubọk ke abaitiad. Usʌk awo emaebo yak ami uwot fiin, ado ami mmaunịm fiin uwem; Ami mmaabo idem mmi, ‘Ami ndiituuhọ abọọñ mmi sia anye ado awo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakeyet adan.’ <verse eid="1SA 24:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 24:11" />Sese, ete mmi, se utọñ afọñ mfo ke ubọk mmi! Ami mmaakpịkke utọñ afọñ mfo ado ñkuwotto fiin. Se, ke ñkpọ nte keed ibaaha ke ubọk mmi awọttọ ke ami mmudue fiin me ke mme ntịdutọñ. Ami udueghe fiin, ado afo asʌk ayem adiñwot miin. <verse eid="1SA 24:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 24:12" />Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akpe ikpe ke ufọọd mmi ye afo. Ñko yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> asio usiene idiọọk a-afo annamma miin, ado ubọk mmi iduutuuho fiin. <verse eid="1SA 24:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 24:13" />Nte akaan ikọ esed a-abooho, ‘Idiọọk ñkpọ ato ke idiọọk awo,’ ke ntoro ubọk mmi iduutuuho fiin.”<verse eid="1SA 24:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 24:14" />“Adidem Isrel awuọ ayem anie awo? Anie ke afo abịne? Adukpo ewa? Abịne ndañ? <verse eid="1SA 24:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 24:15" />Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado akpe ikpe iwuod ñnyịn anyʌñ ase ke ufọọd ñnyịn. Yak anye anduuñọ miin anyʌñ anam unen. Yak anye antoppo miin ikpe ke adinsio miin ke ubọk mfo.”<verse eid="1SA 24:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 24:16" />Ke Defid amaaketañ ado ama, Sọọl amaabịp, “Defid ayịn mmi, uyio mfo adodo?” Ndin anye amaatua ke akpọsọñ uyio. <verse eid="1SA 24:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 24:17" />Anye amaabo Defid, “Afo amenen añkan miin. Afo ameñwọt miin mfọn, ado ami mmenam idiọọk ye afo. <verse eid="1SA 24:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 24:18" />Afo amendọkkọ miin abaña mfọn a-afo akefọnnọ ye ami; <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amañyaak miin usịn fiin ke ubọk, ado afo uñwotto miin. <verse eid="1SA 24:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 24:19" />Ke ini awo akịtte asua amọ, anye asiyaak anye adakka ke imiinamma anye ñkpọ? Yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> unọ fiin eti utịb ke naña afo anam ñkpọ ye ami mfịn ami. <verse eid="1SA 24:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 24:20" />Ami mmediọọñọ ke afo ayaado adidem ke Isrel ñko ke abioubọọñ Isrel adiisọọñọ ida ke ubọk mfo. <verse eid="1SA 24:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 24:21" />Idahami nwọñọ ñkpọ nnọ miin ke anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> bo ke imọ idiiwotto ubon mmi me isọọk anyịñ mmi isio ke ekpək ete mmi.”<verse eid="1SA 24:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 24:22" />Ndin Defid amaanọ Sọọl unwọñọ amọ. Akem Sọọl atịmme anyọñ ufọk ke ini Defid ye mme ideen amọ emaekedọọk ekaa akpọsọñ itie ado.<verse eid="1SA 24:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 24" />
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="1SA 25" />
  <para style="s1">Defid, Nabal ye Abikel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 25:1" />Akem Samwel amaakpa, ndin afịd Isrel emaeboho atọ keed adifʌhọ anye; ammọ emaenyʌñ ebuuk anye ke isọñ idʌñ amọ ke Rama. Ndin Defid amaasaña asọiyọ adʌk Akpautatan Paran.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ye mme ikpañwed Septuakin; mme ikpañwed Septuakin mfen ado Maon</char></note><verse eid="1SA 25:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 25:2" />Akem awo keed amaaba ke Maon, a-akenieghe inie eti-eti ke Kamel, amaanekke amọinyọ. Anye amaanie ebod tọsịn keed (1,000), ye edọñ tọsịn ita (1,000), anye akefatta ammọ ided ke Kamel. <verse eid="1SA 25:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 25:3" />Anyịñ amọ akedo Nabal; anwaan amọ akekere Abikel. Anye akedo awo ifiọk ye uyaiya anwaan, ado ebe amọ akedo ataa asọñido awo ke mme adinam amọ, anye aketo aduuk Kaleb.<verse eid="1SA 25:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 25:4" />Ke ini Defid akesʌkkọ aba ke anaan, anye amaakop ke Nabal asʌk afat edọñ ided. <verse eid="1SA 25:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 25:5" />Ndin Defid amaadọñ ñkparawa ideen duob anyʌñ abo, “Ikaa ibịne Nabal ke Kamel ikikọọm anye innọ. <verse eid="1SA 25:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 25:6" />Ibo anye: ‘Itọñ uwem usọñ fiin! Idem usọñ fiin ye afịd ufọk mfo! Yak idem usọñ fiin ye afịd ufọk mfo!<verse eid="1SA 25:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 25:7" />“ ‘Ndin ami mmekop ke idahami ado ini ufat edọñ ided. Idaha mme akpemeedọñ mfo ekebaaha ye ñnyịn, ñnyịn ikidiọọhọ ye ammọ, ñko afịd ini ammọ ekebaaha ke Kamel ñkpọ ammọ ndomokeed ikisoppo. <verse eid="1SA 25:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 25:8" />Bịp nditọufọk mfo ke ammọ eyaudọkkọ fiin. Ke ntak ado fọn ido ye ideen mmi, sia adooho ñnyịn idi ke ini usọrọ. Mbọk nọ nditọufọk mfo ye Defid ayịn mfo se adodo udʌkkọ fiin ubọk.’ ”<verse eid="1SA 25:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 25:9" />Ke ini ideen Defid ekedisịmme ammọ emaenọ Nabal etob Defid. Ndin esọñ eda ebet ibọọrọ.<verse eid="1SA 25:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 25:10" />Nabal amaabọọrọ nditọ Defid, “Anie ido Defid ami? Anie ido ayịn Yesi ami? Uwak nditọufọk ediañña ekpọñ mme eteufọk amọ ke mme ini ami. <verse eid="1SA 25:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 25:11" />Ntaha ami ñkpebenne uyo ye mmọọñ mmi, ye unam a-ami ñkewotto nnọ mbon e-efatta edọñ mmi ided ñyaak nnọ ideen e-etooho itie ami ndiidiọọñọke edi-e?”<verse eid="1SA 25:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 25:12" />Mme ideen Defid emaekanna iso etịmme edem enyọñọ. Ekekesịm ammọ emaetañ afịd se anye aketañ enọ Defid. <verse eid="1SA 25:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 25:13" />Ndin Defid amaabo mme ideen amọ, “Ndufo keedekeed ibọbọ akañkañ ndufo!” Ammọ emaenyʌñ enam ntoro, Defid ñko amaanyʌñ abọbọ ake amọ. Ñkpọ nte ideen ikie inaañ (400) emaekeene Defid ke ini ikie iba (200) ekesuuhọ eba ekpeme ñkpọ ammọ.<verse eid="1SA 25:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 25:14" />Keed ke atu mme nditọufọk Nabal amaadọkkọ Abikel, anwaan Nabal, “Defid akedọñ mme isʌñutom eto ke anaan edinọ eteufọk ñnyịn ekọọm amọ, ado anye akenọ ammọ usọñanyen. <verse eid="1SA 25:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 25:15" />Ado ibon ado emaenekke efọn ye ñnyịn. Ammọ ikidiọọhọ ido ye ñnyịn, ñko afịd ini ake ñnyịn ikibaaha do ye ammọ ñkpọ ñnyịn ndomokeed ikisoppo. <verse eid="1SA 25:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 25:16" />Akonayio ye uweemeayio ammọ ekedo nte ndibene inọ ñnyịn afịd ini ake ñnyịn ikiseeghe ufene ñnyịn ikpere ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 25:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 25:17" />Ndin kere nyʌñ se se afo akpekan anam, sia unọmọ mmọdo ana anọ eteufọk ñnyịn ye afịd ufọk amọ. Anye ado ataa awo ibak a-adooho awo ndomokeed ikanna itañ ikọ ye anye.”<verse eid="1SA 25:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 25:18" />Abikel amaadịppe idem ini keed. Anye amaaben uyo ikie iba (200) ye ukọd ke ikịm iba, ye edọñ ition ediọññọ ema ye udomo ufọfọb abakpa ition<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25:18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte kilokram 27</char></note> ye uyo resịn ikie (100) ye uyo enyịmmeke fik ikie iba (200) anyʌñ abọp ammọ ke mme dọñki. <verse eid="1SA 25:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 25:19" />Ndin anye amaabo nditọufọk amọ, “Itọọñọ isañ; ami ñyaikeene ndufo ke edem.” Ado anye ikidọkkọke ebe amọ Nabal.<verse eid="1SA 25:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 25:20" />Nte anye asʌkkọ awat dọñki amọ aka ke abod abedeñ, sese Defid asọiyọke ke mi adi ye mme ideen amọ, ñko anye amaasoobo ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 25:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 25:21" />Defid akesʌk abo, “Ami ado utak-utak, afịd naña ñkekpeme mme inie amọ ke anaan mbaak ñkpọ ndomokeed adisop. Anye añkpe miin usiene idiọọk ke eti ñkpọ a-ami ñkenamma. <verse eid="1SA 25:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 25:22" />Yak Abasi amia Defid ufen, ñko ntoro akpọsọñ-akpọsọñ, adieke adooho asịm ubakusen ami nsʌhọ ayaara ndomokeed ke atu afịd se inie anye!”<verse eid="1SA 25:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 25:23" />Ke ini Abikel akekịtte Defid, anye amaasọiyọ ke dọñki amọ usọp-usọp anyʌñ asuuk iwuod asịn ke isọñ ke iso Defid. <verse eid="1SA 25:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 25:24" />Anye amaaduọ anye ke ukod ate: “Abọọñ mmi feen nọ ayịnufọk mfo, ndin yak ami ntañ ikọ unọ fiin; kop se ayịnufọk mfo anie aditañ. <verse eid="1SA 25:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 25:25" />Mbọk abọọñ mmi, kuukpañ utọñ unọ ibak ete ado Nabal. Anye aba nte anyịñ amọ, anyịñ amọ awuọñọ ntʌn, ñko ndisịme akeene anye. Amaado ami, ñkekịtte ideen abọọñ mmi akedọññọ. <verse eid="1SA 25:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 25:26" />Ndin idahami, abọọñ mmi, adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mfo aduuho uwem sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mfo amaunọ adikan ke adukpan fiin adiduọk iyiib ye adidat ubọk mfo nsio usiene nnọ idem mfo, yak mme asua mfo ye afịd mbon se ukọbọ fiin eba nte Nabal. <verse eid="1SA 25:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 25:27" />Ndin yak enọ ami, ake ayịnufọk mfo abenne asọk abọọñ mi, ado se enọ mme ideen u-ukeeneke fiin.<verse eid="1SA 25:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 25:28" />“Mbọk dakka nọ ayịnufọk mfo ke naña udue. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mfo ayaanam itie ubọọñ abọọñ mmi akpeene ke isọñ, sia adooho afo anwana ekọñ anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñko ukwañido ndomokeed idiibaaha ke uwem mfo adaña nte afo abaaha ke uwem. <verse eid="1SA 25:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 25:29" />Akpekọm awo ubịne fiin adiben uwem mfo nsio, uwem abọọñ mmi ayaabọbọ asịne ke abek uwem <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mfo, ado amaado uwem mme asua mfo, anye ayaatop aduọọk nte itiad esioho ke esịd ekpad. <verse eid="1SA 25:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 25:30" />Ke ini <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anamma afịd nti ñkpọ ake anye akenwọñọke anọ abọọñ mmi anyʌñ anam anye ado andikara ke Isrel, <verse eid="1SA 25:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1SA 25:31" />abọọñ mmi idiinieghe ke esịd amọ ñkpọ iduọesịd a-atooho ke uduọk iyiib ntịme-ntịme me ke adisio usiene nnọọ idem amọ. Ñko ke ini <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adiinọ abọọñ mmi mfọn adikan, toiyo ayịnufọk mfo.”<verse eid="1SA 25:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="1SA 25:32" />Defid amaabo Abikel, “Ekọọm anie <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi Isrel, ake udọññọ fiin mfịn ami yak adisoobo ye ami. <verse eid="1SA 25:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="1SA 25:33" />Yak adidiọñ usịm fiin ke adinen ikpe mfo ye ke afo adinam yak ami ñkuuduọk iyiib. <verse eid="1SA 25:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="1SA 25:34" />Imiidooho, ke akpanikọ adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi Isrel aduuho uwem, anye añkpan miin adunọmọ fiin, akpedo afo ukusọppọ uduñkịt miin ibaaha ayaara ufọk Nabal se ikpikiba ke uwem ke usiere usen.”<verse eid="1SA 25:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="1SA 25:35" />Ndin Defid amaabọi anye se anye akekoono aben asọk anye amaanyʌñ abo, “Nyọñ ufọk ke emem. Ami mmekop ikọ mfo ñnyʌñ unọ fiin se afo abeeñe.”<verse eid="1SA 25:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="1SA 25:36" />Ke ini Abikel akekaaha abịne Nabal anye mmọdo akeba ke ufọk asʌk adia usọrọ nte ake adidem. Anye amaanekke akpa mmịn anyʌñ aba ke ataa ekamba inemesịd. Ke ntak ado Abikel ikidọkkọke anye ñkpọ ndomokeed tutu ayio asiere. <verse eid="1SA 25:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="1SA 25:37" />Ndin ke ubakusen, ke ini ukọd amaakefuño Nabal, anwaan amọ amaadọkkọ anye afịd mme ñkpọ ami, ndin esịd amaaduọ anye, anye adiba nte itiad. <verse eid="1SA 25:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="1SA 25:38" />Ñkpọ nte usen duob akeboiyo <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaayʌppọ Nabal ndin anye amaakpa.<verse eid="1SA 25:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="1SA 25:39" />Ke ini Defid akekoppo ke Nabal akpa, anye amaabo, “Ekọọm anie <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ake atọhọke utọk iwuod mmi ye Nabal ke anye adinam ñkpọ insịn miin ke ndek. Anye atre ayịnufọk amọ adinam idiọọk anyʌñ aben idiọọk ido Nabal adot anye ke iwuod amọ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 25:39">Ndin Defid amaadọñ utom anọ Abikel abo yak anye ado anwaan imọ. <verse eid="1SA 25:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="1SA 25:40" />Nditọufọk amọ emaekaa Kamel enyʌñ ekebo Abikel, “Defid idọñ ñnyịn abo iduben fiin idi nte anwaan amọ.”<verse eid="1SA 25:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="1SA 25:41" />Anye amaasuuk iso asịn ke isọñ amaanyʌñ abo, “Ami ndo ayịnufọk mfo ndin mmenyʌñ mbeeñe idem adinam afịd se afo atañ ñnyʌñ ñyet ukod nditọufọk abọọñ mmi.” <verse eid="1SA 25:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="1SA 25:42" />Abikel amaasọsọp adọọk adoro ke dọñki anyʌñ asaña ye nditọufọk ibaan amọ ition ye isʌñutom Defid akaa akedo anwaan Defid. <verse eid="1SA 25:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="1SA 25:43" />Defid amaanyʌñ adọdọ Ahinoam awonwaan Yesriil, ndin ammọ awo iba ekedoñño ibaan amọ. <verse eid="1SA 25:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="1SA 25:44" />Ado Sọọl amaaben ayịn awonwaan amọ Maikal, anwaan Defid anọ Paltiel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25:44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ado Palti, asʌk ado kpa Paltiel</char></note> ayịn awodeen Lais, a-aketooho Kalim.<verse eid="1SA 25:44" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 25" />
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="1SA 26" />
  <para style="s1">Defid Amaana Ayaak Uwem Sọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 26:1" />Mbon Siif emaekaa ebịne Sọọl ke Kibie ekebo, “Idooho Defid adịbe ke abod Hakila, a-asakkaiso ase Yesimọn?”<verse eid="1SA 26:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 26:2" />Ke ntoro Sọọl amaadidakka akaa Akpautatan Siif, ye mbon ekọñ Isrel tọsịn ita (3,000) ake anye akesatta asio, adikiyem Defid ke ndo. <verse eid="1SA 26:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 26:3" />Sọọl amaanam itie nnaa amọ ke mben usʌñ ke abod Hakila a-aseeghe Yesimọn, ado Defid akeba ke anaan. Ke ini anye akịtte ke Sọọl ikeene imọ adi ndo, <verse eid="1SA 26:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 26:4" />Defid amaadọñ mbon uyeb anyʌñ adiọọñọ ke akpanikọ ke Sọọl amaadiwuọ.<verse eid="1SA 26:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 26:5" />Ndin Defid amaasaña awuọ akaa itie nte Sọọl akenịm itie nnaa amọ. Anye amaakịt itie nte Sọọl ye Abna ayịn Nee, adaiso mbon ekọñ, ekesuuk enaa. Sọọl akena ke esịd itie nnaa, ndin mbon ekọñ emaenaa ekanna anye ekʌk.<verse eid="1SA 26:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 26:6" />Defid amaabịp Ahimelek awo Hed ye Abisai ayịn Seruya, ayịneka awodeen Yoab, “Anie awo idiñkeene miin ikaa nnaaekọñ Sọọl?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 26:6">Abisai amaabo, “Ami ñyaukeene ñka.”<verse eid="1SA 26:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 26:7" />Ke ntoro Defid ye Abisai emaekaa itie ekọñ akonayio, ndin do ke Sọọl akenaa asʌk adaiya ke esịd itie nnaa ndin eduad amọ awʌhọ ke isọñ ke mben iwuod amọ. Abna ye mbon ekọñ emaenyʌñ enaa ekpere anye.<verse eid="1SA 26:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 26:8" />Abisai amaabo Defid, “Mfịn Abasi ayaak asua mfo usịn fiin ke ubọk. Yak ndat eduad ñkịm anye ndian ke isọñ ini keed; ami ndiikịmme anye akañ iba.”<verse eid="1SA 26:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 26:9" />Ado Defid amaabo Abisai, “Kuusobo anye! Anie ikpikan ituuk awo se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakeyet adan ndin atre adidue isob?” <verse eid="1SA 26:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 26:10" />Defid amaabo, “Adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abaaha ke uwem, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke idem amọ adiiwot anye, imiidooho ntoro ini amọ ayaadi ndin anye ayaakpa, imiidooho anye ayaakaa ekọñ aketak. <verse eid="1SA 26:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 26:11" />Ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akan ami adituuk awo ake <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakeyet adan ubọk. Ndin dịppe eduad ye atu mmọọñ a-anaaha do akpere iwuod amọ di yak inyọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 26:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 26:12" />Ndin Defid amaadịppe eduad ye atu mmọọñ akekpereke iwuod Sọọl, ndin ammọ enyʌñ edaaña. Ikibaaha awo se ikikịt me idiọọñọ ibaña, ikinyʌññọ iba awo se ikidemme. Afịd ammọ ekesʌk edaiya, sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaatọ ammọ idab ammọ enekke edaiya.<verse eid="1SA 26:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 26:13" />Ndin Defid amaakaaña ada ke edem ñkañ uko ke anyọñ abod ke itie a-akemaanake asanna; ekamba ukpa amaanaa ke ufọọd ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 26:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 26:14" />Defid amaada akoot mbon ekọñ ye Abna ayịn Nee, “Abna, afo ubooho umbọọrọ miin?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 26:14">Abna amaabọọrọ, “Afo ado anie a-akoodo adidem?”<verse eid="1SA 26:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 26:15" />Defid amaabo Abna, “Afo ado awodeen, idooho ntoro? Ñko anie awo iba nte afo ke Isrel? Ntaha afo umuukukpemeke adidem abọọñ mfo? Awo amaadi adiwot adidem abọọñ mfo. <verse eid="1SA 26:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 26:16" />Se afo anam ifọnnọ. Adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aduuho uwem, afo ye ideen mfo ana ekpañña, sia ndufo ikikpemeke eteufọk ndufo, anye ake <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akeyette adan. Ise ikanna idem ndufo. Mmọ eduad ye atu mmọọñ adidem e-ekebonoke ekpere iwuod amọ?”<verse eid="1SA 26:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 26:17" />Sọọl amaadiọọñọ uyio Defid anyʌñ abo, “Defid ayịn mmi, uyio mfo adodo.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 26:17">Defid amaabọọrọ “Ii anye ke do adidem abọọñ mmi.” <verse eid="1SA 26:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 26:18" />Anye amaamaana adian do, “Nsoo ido ntak abọọñ mmi adubịnneke ayịnufọk amọ? Nsoo ke ami nnam, ñko nsoo idiọọk ke ami ndue? <verse eid="1SA 26:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 26:19" />Ndin yak adidem abọọñ mmi akpañ utọñ anọ ikọ ayịnufọk amọ. Adieke adooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> udọọñ fiin yak ambịne miin, yak anye abọ uwa. Ado adieke adooho ke usʌñ ndomokeed anye ado awo anam ami, yak isuuñọ akeene ammọ ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>! Ammọ embịne miin mfịn esio ke udeeme mmi ke inie <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ndin ammọ embo miin, ‘kaa ke kpono abasi mfen.’ <verse eid="1SA 26:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 26:20" />Ndin kuuyak nọ iyiib mmi aduọkkọ ke isọñ anyọọñ akpọñ iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Adidem Isrel amaawuọ adi adiyem ndañ, nte awo ayem asasa inuen ke mme ikpọabod.”<verse eid="1SA 26:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 26:21" />Ndin Sọọl amaabo, “Ami mmenam idiọọkñkpọ. Defid ayịn mmi tịmme di. Sia adooho afo amedat uwem mmi nte ñkpọuto mfịn ami, ami ndiiyemme unọmọ fiin aba. Ke akpanikọ ami mba nte ndisịme mmenyʌñ nnekke ndue.”<verse eid="1SA 26:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 26:22" />Defid amaabọọrọ, “Sese eduad adidem mi. Yak awo keed ke atu ñkparawa ndufo akanna adibọ. <verse eid="1SA 26:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 26:23" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anọ afịd awo utịb adinenido ye akpanikọ ammọ. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amauyaak fiin ansịn miin ke ubọk mfịn ami, ado ami ndiinyanna ubọk ntuuk anye ake <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakeyet adan. <verse eid="1SA 26:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 26:24" />Kpa naña ami mbat uwem mfo nte ekamba ñkpọ mfịn ami, ñko yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abat uwem mmi nte ekamba ñkpọ ndin añnyaaña miin asio ke afịd afanekọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 26:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 26:25" />Ndin Sọọl amaabo Defid, “Yak adidiọñ usịm fiin, Defid ayịn mmi; afo ayaanam ekamba ñkpọ anyʌñ anie edikan.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 26:25">Ke ntoro Defid amaakaa uwa amọ, Sọọl amaanyʌñ atịmme anyọñ ufọk.<verse eid="1SA 26:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 26" />
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="1SA 27" />
  <para style="s1">Defid ke Atu Mbon Filistia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 27:1" />Ado Defid amaakere ke esịd amọ abo, “Usen keed, Sọọl ayansobo miin. Akpan ñkpọ se ami ñkpenam ado ami adifeghe mbọkkọ ñkaa idʌñ mbon Filistia. Ndin ayaakak Sọọl adiñyem miin ke Isrel, ami ñyaanyʌñ mfiọnnọ ñwuọ ke ubọk amọ.”<verse eid="1SA 27:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 27:2" />Ke ntoro, Defid ye mme ideen ikie itiokeed (600) e-ekebaaha ye anye emaekpọñ ekanna ebịne Akis ayịn Maok adidem Kad. <verse eid="1SA 27:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 27:3" />Defid ye ikọd amọ emaedʌñ ke Kad ye Akis. Awodeen keedekeed amaaba ye ubon ammọ, Defid amaanyʌñ anie ibaan amọ iba: Ahinoam awonwaan Yesriil ye Abikel awonwaan Kamel, ebekpa Nabal. <verse eid="1SA 27:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 27:4" />Ke ini ekedọkkọke Sọọl ke Defid amaafeghe akaa Kad, anye ikiyemme anye aba.<verse eid="1SA 27:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 27:5" />Ndin Defid amaabo Akis, “Adieke ami nnieghe mfọniso ke iso mfo, yak ennọ miin itie ke abio keed ke idʌñ ami, yak ami ñkedʌñ do. Ntak a-ayịnufọk mfo akpedʌññọ ke abio adidem ye afo-o?”<verse eid="1SA 27:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 27:6" />Ke ntoro ke usen ado Akis amaanọ anye Siklak, ndin tọọñọ ke ini ado anye adinie mme ndidem Yuda. <verse eid="1SA 27:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 27:7" />Defid amaadʌñ ke idʌñ mbon Filistia isua keed ye afiọñ inaañ.<verse eid="1SA 27:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 27:8" />Akem Defid ye ikọd amọ emaedọọk ekaa ekenwana ekọñ ye mbon Kesọọ, mbon Kees ye mbon Amalek. (Tọọñọ ke ayio esed ibon ami ekedʌñ ke isọñ a-adatta akesịm Sọọ ye Iyib.) <verse eid="1SA 27:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 27:9" />Ini akeedodo Defid amaanwana idʌñ, anye ikisisʌhọke awodeen me awonwaan uwem, ado amaakoono mme edọñ, ufene, mme dọñki, ye mme kamel ye mme afọñ. Ndin anye amaatịmme anyọñ Akis.<verse eid="1SA 27:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 27:10" />Ke ini Akis akebịppe, “Uke ke afo akekesuan mfịn?” Defid ayaabo, “Ñnyịn ikidʌk edem Nekef ke Yuda” usʌk “edem usuuk Yerameel” usʌk “edem mbon Keen.” <verse eid="1SA 27:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 27:11" />Anye ikisʌhọke awodeen me awonwaan ndomokeed ye uwem nọ ato do eben edi Kad, sia anye amaakere, “Ammọ ekeme editañ mbo se ‘Defid akenam ado ami.’ ” Ndin adinam amọ akesido ami adaña ini anye akebaaha ke abio Filistia. <verse eid="1SA 27:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 27:12" />Ndin Akis amaanịm ikọ Defid ke akpanikọ amaanyʌñ abo idem amọ, “Anye anam aduuk amọ nditọ Isrel esua anye, ke ntak ado anye adiido ayịnufọk mmi ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="1SA 27:12" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 27" />
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="1SA 28" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 28:1" />Adikem ke ini ado mbon Filistia ebono mbon ekọñ ammọ edika ñkenwana ye mbon Isrel. Akis amaabo Defid, “Ana afo adiọọñọ ke afo ye ikọd mfo ana eñkeene miin ke isañ ekọñ ami.”<verse eid="1SA 28:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 28:2" />Defid amaabo, “Ndin afo ayaakịt ke idem mfo se ayịnufọk mfo akeme adinam.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:2">Akis amaabọọrọ, “Afọn, ami ñyaunịm fiin nte awoukpeme mmi ke nsi-nsi.”<verse eid="1SA 28:2" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Sọọl ye Abiaidiọñ ke Endọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 28:3" />Ndin Samwel amaakpa, afịd Isrel emaetua anye enyʌñ ebuuk anye ke isọñ emana amọ ke Rama. Sọọl amaabịne mme nsañaekpo ye mme mbiaidiọñ asioño ke idʌñ.<verse eid="1SA 28:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 28:4" />Mbon Filistia emaebono edi edinam nnaaekọñ ke Sunem, ke ini Sọọl akebokko afịd Isrel anyʌñ anịm nnaaekọñ ke Kilboa. <verse eid="1SA 28:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 28:5" />Ke ini Sọọl akekịtte udịmekọñ Filistia, idem amaanyeñ anye; ndịk amaayọhọ anye esịd. <verse eid="1SA 28:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 28:6" />Sọọl amaabịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, ado <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikibọọrọke anye ke ndab me ke Urim me ato ke mme prọfed. <verse eid="1SA 28:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 28:7" />Sọọl ndin amaabo mme mbon utom amọ, “Iyem awonwaan a-adooho akịdñkukịd innọ miin, nọ ato do ami ñkebịp anye.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:7">Ammọ emaebo, “Keed mmọdo ke Endọ.”<verse eid="1SA 28:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 28:8" />Ke ntoro Sọọl amaakpəho idem amọ, asịne mme afọñ mfen, ndin ke akonayio anye ye ideen iba emaekaa ebịne awonwaan ado. Anye amaabo “Se ñkukịd nnọ miin, nyʌñ koot anye a-ami mboho nsiak anyịñ nnọ.”<verse eid="1SA 28:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 28:9" />Ado awonwaan ado amaabo, “Ke akpanikọ afo amediọọñọ se Sọọl akenam. Anye amaasioño mbon nsañaekpo ye mme mbiaidiọñ ke isọñ. Ntak a-afo akọọhọ afia ñkpa anọọ adiñwot miin-e?”<verse eid="1SA 28:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 28:10" />Sọọl amaanwọñọ ñkpọ ke anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, “Ke akpanikọ adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abaaha ke uwem, awo iduunọọhọ fiin ufen ke ntak ami.”<verse eid="1SA 28:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 28:11" />Ndin awonwaan ado amaabịp, “Anie ke ami ndiikoot nsio unọ fiin?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:11">Anye amaabo, “Koot Samwel sio.”<verse eid="1SA 28:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 28:12" />Ke ini awonwaan ado akịtte Samwel, anye amaatua ke akpọsọñ uyio anyʌñ abo Sọọl, “Ntaha afo ambiañake miin-e? Afo ado Sọọl!”<verse eid="1SA 28:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 28:13" />Adidem Sọọl amaabo anye, “Kuukop ndịk. Nsoo ke afo akịt?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:13">Awonwaan ado amaabọọrọ, “Ñkịt awo nte ekpo<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido kịt sịbidịd; me kịt mme abasi</char></note> naña ato isọñ adọọk adi.”<verse eid="1SA 28:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 28:14" />Anye amaabịp, “Anye aba nte nsoo ñkpọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:14">Anye amaabo, “Akaanadeen a-asịneke ewịra asʌk awuọ adi.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:14">Ndin Sọọl amaadiọọñọ ke ado Samwel, ñko anye amaasuuk iwuod asịn ke isọñ ndin amaaduọ akʌp iso ke isọñ.<verse eid="1SA 28:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 28:15" />Samwel amaabo Sọọl, “Nsoo ido ntak a-afo amfịnake miin ke adiñkoot miin nsio?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:15">Sọọl amaabo, “Ami mba ke ekamba mfịna. Mbon Filistia esʌk enwana ye ami, ñko Abasi adakka añkpọñ miin. Anye imbọọrọke miin aba, imbọọrọke ito prọfed me ke ndab. Ke ntoro ami ukoot fiin yak andọkkọ se mbiinam.”<verse eid="1SA 28:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 28:16" />Samwel amaabo, “Nsoo inam afo ambịp miin, idahami a-adooho <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakedakka ukpọñ fiin anyʌñ akanna ado asua mfo? <verse eid="1SA 28:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 28:17" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> anam se anye akekama inua mmi atañ. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abakka abioubọọñ asio ke ubọk mfo anyʌñ ayaak anọ mbọhọidʌñ mfo, Defid. <verse eid="1SA 28:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 28:18" />Sia adooho afo ukukoppo item unọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> me adinam se anye akeyem ke iyadesịd amọ ke abaña mbon Amalek, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> u-unam fiin ntom mfịn ami. <verse eid="1SA 28:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 28:19" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayauyaak fiin ye mbon Isrel asịn ke ubọk mbon Filistia, ndin ñkpọñ afo ye ayịn mfo eyaeba ye ami. <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaanyʌñ ayaak mbon ekọñ Isrel asịn ke ubọk mbon Filistia.”<verse eid="1SA 28:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 28:20" />Ini keed ini keed Sọọl amaanyanna aduọ ke isọñ, ayọhọ ye ndịk ke ntak ikọ se Samwel aketañ. Inweek ikibaaha anye aba, sia adooho anye ikidiaha ñkpọ ndomokeed afịd usen ado ye afịd akonayio ado.<verse eid="1SA 28:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 28:21" />Ke ini awonwaan ado akediighe abịne Sọọl anyʌñ adikịt ke idem anekke anyeñ anye, anye amaabo, “Sese ayịnufọk mfo akop item unọ fiin. Ñkekama uwem mmi ke ubọk mmi nnam se afo akebo yak nam. <verse eid="1SA 28:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 28:22" />Mbọk ndin afo ñko nyʌñ kop uyio ayịnufọk mfo nyʌñ yak ami unọ fiin ndidia yak adia nọ afo anie inweek asaña atịmme anyọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 28:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 28:23" />Anye amaasịn anyʌñ abo, “Ami ndiidiaha ñkpọ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 28:23">Ado ikọd amọ emaediana ye awonwaan ado ekpeiye anye, ndin anye amaakop uyio ammọ. Anye amaadakka ada ke isọñ atie ke ifịm.<verse eid="1SA 28:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 28:24" />Awonwaan ado amaanie ñyịn enañ e-ekekʌkkọ ke ufọk, anye amaaben usọp-usọp awot. Anye amaaben ndomuyo, anuakka akama anam uyo se yiis imiisịneke. <verse eid="1SA 28:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 28:25" />Ndin anye amaaben adidot Sọọl ye ikọd amọ ke iso ammọ ediaha. Kpa akonayio ado ammọ emaedaaña enyọñọ.<verse eid="1SA 28:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 28" />
  <chapter number="29" style="c" sid="1SA 29" />
  <para style="s1">Akis Anọ Defid Atịmme Anyọñ Siklak</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 29:1" />Mbon Filistia emaekoot afịd mbon ekọñ ammọ ebʌk ke Afek, ndin Isrel emaenịm nnaaekọñ ammọ ke Yesriil. <verse eid="1SA 29:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 29:2" />Nte mme mbọọñ Filistia ekesañake ke ikie (100) ke ikie (100) ye ke tọsịn (1,000) ke tọsịn (1,000), Defid ye mme ikọd amọ ekesaña ke edem ye Akis. <verse eid="1SA 29:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 29:3" />Mme adaiso mbon ekọñ Filistia emaebịp, “Mme anie ido mbon Hibru ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 29:3">Akis amaabọọrọ, “Nte idooho Defid a-akedooho anam utom Sọọl adidem Isrel ado ami? Anye a-ababa ye ami akan isua keed, ndin tọọñọ anye akekpọñ Sọọl adiba ye ami tutu idahami, ami ñkịtte ndudue ndomokeed nto anye.”<verse eid="1SA 29:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 29:4" />Ado mme adaiso mbon ekọñ Filistia emaeyat esịd ye Akis enyʌñ ebo, “Nọ awo ami atịmme anyọñ, yak anye atịmme akeba ke itie a-afo akebooho anye aba. Inaaha anye asaña ye ñnyịn aka ekọñ, imiidooho ntoro anye ayaakanna ada anwana ye ñnyịn ke ini enwanake ekọñ. Anye akpenam die atịmme anie mfọn ato eteufọk amọ akan anye adikpịkke iwuod ideen ñnyịn? <verse eid="1SA 29:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 29:5" />Idooho kpa Defid ami ke ekekwọ ebaña ke ikwọ ammọ idaha eboho</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1SA 29:5">“ ‘Sọọl amaawot mme tọsịn (1,000) amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1SA 29:5">ndin Defid amaawot mme tọsịn duob (10,000) amọ?’ ”<verse eid="1SA 29:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 29:6" />Ke ntoro, Akis amaakoot Defid anyʌñ abo anye, “Adaña nte <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> aduuho uwem, afo amenen ke mme edinam mfo, ñko ami ñkpaama afo asaña ye ami ke atu ekọñ ami. Tọọñọ ke usen afo akediighe ambịne miin tutu mfịn ami, ami ñkịtte ndudue ndomokeed uto fiin, ado mme adaiwuod uyemme fiin. <verse eid="1SA 29:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 29:7" />Tịmme edem idahami nyọñ ke emem; kuunam ñkpọ ndomokeed se iyat mme adaiwuod Filistia.”<verse eid="1SA 29:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 29:8" />Ado Defid amaabịp Akis, “Nsoo ke ami nam? Nsoo utọ idiọọk ke afo akịt ato awo mfo tọọñọ ke usen a-ami ñkidiighe ubịne fiin tutu idahami? Ntaha ami ndiikeeneke ñkenwana ye mme asua adidem ye abọọñ mmi-e?”<verse eid="1SA 29:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 29:9" />Akis amaabọọrọ Defid, “Ami mmediọọñọ ke afo amefọn ke iso mmi nte enyere Abasi; ado mme adaiso ekọñ mbon Filistia ebo, ‘Inaaha anye asaña ye ñnyịn aka ekọñ.’ <verse eid="1SA 29:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 29:10" />Ndin bak dakka da, ye nditọufọk eteufọk mfo ekedieghe ye afo, nyʌñ nyọñ ubakusen ayio amaanwaña.”<verse eid="1SA 29:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 29:11" />Ke ntoro Defid ye mme ikọd amọ emaedakka eda ubakusen enyʌñ etịmme enyọñ idʌñ mbon Filistia, mbon Filistia emaenyʌñ edọọk ekaa Yesriil.<verse eid="1SA 29:11" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 29" />
  <chapter number="30" style="c" sid="1SA 30" />
  <para style="s1">Defid Asobo Mbon Amalek</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 30:1" />Defid ye mme ideen amọ emaekesịm Siklak ke ayọhọ usen ita. Akem mbon Amalek emaekenwana ekọñ ye Nekef ye Siklak. Ammọ emaesuan Siklak enyʌñ efọp anye, <verse eid="1SA 30:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 30:2" />ñko emaenyʌñ emʌm ibaan ye afịd awo mfen se ikiba do, ntək ye usọñ. Ammọ ikiwotto awo ndomokeed, ado emaeben ammọ enyọñọ nte mbuodekọñ.<verse eid="1SA 30:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 30:3" />Ke ini Defid ye ideen amọ ekesịmme abio Siklak, ammọ emaekịt ke ikañ amaasobo anye enyʌñ ekịt ke emaetañ ibaan ammọ ye nditọ ideen ye nditọ ibaan ammọ nte ifʌn. <verse eid="1SA 30:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 30:4" />Ke ntoro, Defid ye ikọd amọ emaetuaha tutu adudu ibaaha ammọ aba ke idem editua. <verse eid="1SA 30:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 30:5" />Emaemʌm ibaan Defid naña iba, Ahinoam awonwaan Yesriil ye Abikel, ebekpa Nabal awonwaan Kamel. <verse eid="1SA 30:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 30:6" />Defid amaanekke akịt ukuud sia ideen ado emaetañ ebaña editọọñ anye ke itiad; sia adooho esịd amaanekke ayat ammọ keedekeed ke ntak nditọ ammọ ideen ye ibaan. Ado Defid amaakop uko ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi amọ.<verse eid="1SA 30:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 30:7" />Ndin Defid amaabo aku Abiata, ayịn Ahimelek. “Ben afọñ aboditọñ nsọk miin.” Abiata amaaben asọk anye, <verse eid="1SA 30:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 30:8" />ndin Defid amaabịp <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abo, “Ami mbịne mbon ekọñ ami? Nte ami ñyaasịme ammọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 30:8">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Bịne ammọ. Afo ayaasịme ammọ anyʌñ abọi afịd ñkpọ.”<verse eid="1SA 30:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 30:9" />Defid ye ideen ikie itiokeed (600) emaesaña ye anye ekesịm Abedeñ Besọọ, ake usʌk ekesuuhọ eba. <verse eid="1SA 30:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 30:10" />Ke Besọọ awo ikie iba (200) ke atu ammọ ikikanna ikaaña abedeñ sia adooho idem amaanekke amem ammọ, ado Defid ye ideen ikie inaañ (400) ako emaekaa iso ebịne.<verse eid="1SA 30:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 30:11" />Ammọ emaekịt awo Iyib ke inwañ enyʌñ eben anye esọk Defid. Ammọ emaenọ anye mmọọñ nọ anwọñ ye ndidia nọ adia, <verse eid="1SA 30:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 30:12" />enọ anye ubaak ebok fik ye ebok resịn iba. Anye amaadia anyʌñ anie inweek, sia adooho anye ikidiaha ñkpọ ndomokeed ikinyʌññọ inwọñ ñkpọ ndomokeed ke usen ita ye akonayio ita.<verse eid="1SA 30:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 30:13" />Defid amaabịp anye abo, “Anie awo unie fiin? Afo ato uke?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 30:13">Anye amaabo, “Ami ndo awo Iyib, afʌn awo Amalek. Eteufọk mmi amansaana miin asuuk idaha udọñọ akentọọñọke ke ñkpọ nte usen ita a-akeboiyoke. <verse eid="1SA 30:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1SA 30:14" />Ñnyịn ikikaa ekọñ ke Nekef ake mbon Kered, usʌk itie a-anieghe mbon Yuda ye Nekef ake Kaleb. Ñko ñnyịn imaifọp Siklak.”<verse eid="1SA 30:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1SA 30:15" />Defid amaabịp anye, “Afo akpamben miin akewọt mbon ekọñ ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 30:15">Anye amaabọọrọ, “Nwọñọ nnọ miin ke iso Abasi bo ke imọ idiñwotto miin idiinyʌññọ iñyaak miin inọ eteufọk mmi, ndin ami ñyauben fiin ñkaa mbịne ammọ.”<verse eid="1SA 30:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1SA 30:16" />Anye amaaben Defid akaa, ndin sese ammọ mi emaesuana eyọhọ afịd itie ado, esʌk edia ñkpọ, esʌk enwọñ ñkpọ enyʌñ esʌk enam idaara ke ntak uwak mbịme se ammọ ekekoono enyọñ eto isọñ Filistia ye ke Yuda. <verse eid="1SA 30:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1SA 30:17" />Defid amaanwana ye ammọ tọọñọ ke utekke ndubiayio tutu akesịm ndubiayio edem usen, ñko ibaaha awo se ikibọkkọ, ibọhọke ideen ikie inaañ (400) e-ekewatta ke kamel efeeñe. <verse eid="1SA 30:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1SA 30:18" />Defid amaabọi afịd ñkpọ se mbon Amalek ekekoono, anye amaanyʌñ abọ ibaan amọ iba. <verse eid="1SA 30:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1SA 30:19" />Ñkpọ ndomokeed ikisoppo: iwaad ye mme usọñ, nditọ ideen ye nditọ ibaan, mbịme me ñkpọ ndomokeed mfen se ammọ ekeben. Defid amaakoono afịd se ekebọọ anyọñ adi. <verse eid="1SA 30:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1SA 30:20" />Anye amaakoono afịd udịmedọñ ye udịmenañ, ndin ideen amọ emaewat ammọ eboiyo iso mme ufene mbon ako, ete, “Ami ado mbịme Defid.”<verse eid="1SA 30:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1SA 30:21" />Ndin Defid amaadisịm ideen ikie iba (200) ado ake idem akenekkeke amem adikeene anye, e-ekenyʌññọ esʌhọ ke Abedeñ Besọọ. Ammọ emaewuọñọ edi edisoobo Defid ye mme ikọd amọ ekesañake ye anye. Akem Defid akesaña akpere ammọ, anye amaabịp ammọ naña idem ammọ aba. <verse eid="1SA 30:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1SA 30:22" />Ado afịd mbon idiọọk esịd ye mbon ntịme ke atu mbon se ikikeene Defid emaebo, “Sia ammọ imiikikeeneke ñnyịn ika, ñnyịn idiideemeke mbịme se ñnyịn inie inọ ammọ. Ado awodeen keedekeed akeme adiben anwaan ye nditọ ammọ ñnyọñ.”<verse eid="1SA 30:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1SA 30:23" />Defid amaabọọrọ, “Iyoo, ikiinam ntoro nditọeka mmi, ñkpọ ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inọọ ñnyịn. Anye amaikpeme ñnyịn anyʌñ ayaak mbon ekọñ ekedieghe mfịna ye ñnyịn isịn ñnyịn ke ubọk. <verse eid="1SA 30:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1SA 30:24" />Anie adiikpañ utọñ inọ se afo atañ? Udeeme ñkpọ awo se ikitie ikpeme ñkpọ ñnyịn ye ake awo akewuọhọ aka ekọñ adiido ukem. Afịd awo ediinie ukem-ukem.” <verse eid="1SA 30:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1SA 30:25" />Defid amaanam yak ami ado ewʌhọ ye ido ke Isrel tọọñọ ke usen ado tutu ke usen mfịn.<verse eid="1SA 30:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1SA 30:26" />Ke ini Defid akesịmme Siklak, anye amaanọ usʌk mbịme ado esọk mme ñkpisọñ ke Yuda, e-ekedooho mme ufan amọ, ate, “Sese enọ ake ndufo mi a-atooho mbịme mbon usua <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.”<verse eid="1SA 30:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1SA 30:27" />Defid amaanọ esọk mbon e-ekebaaha ke Beteel, Ramọd Nekef ye Yattia; <verse eid="1SA 30:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1SA 30:28" />anọ esọk mbon e-ebaaha ke Sifmod, Estemoa <verse eid="1SA 30:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1SA 30:29" />ye Rakal; anọ esọk mbon ake idʌñ mbon Yerameel ye mbon Keen; <verse eid="1SA 30:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1SA 30:30" />anọ esọk mbon e-ebaaha ke Họma, Bọọ Asan, Atak <verse eid="1SA 30:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1SA 30:31" />ye Hibrọn; ye mbon se ikiba ke afịd abio se Defid ye ikọd amọ ekesaña ekanna.<verse eid="1SA 30:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 30" />
  <chapter number="31" style="c" sid="1SA 31" />
  <para style="s1">Sọọl Awot Idem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1SA 31:1" />Akem mbon Filistia emaenwana ye nditọ Isrel; nditọ Isrel emaefeeñe ke iso ammọ, ndin uwak emaekpañña ke abod Kilboa. <verse eid="1SA 31:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1SA 31:2" />Mbon Filistia emaesọọñọ ebịne Sọọl ye nditọ ideen amọ, ndin ammọ emaewot nditọ ideen amọ Yọnatan, Abinadab ye Malki-Sua. <verse eid="1SA 31:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1SA 31:3" />Ekọñ ami amaasọñ adudu ke ukañ Sọọl, ndin ke ini mme atobidañ ekekanna anye ubọk, ammọ emaenọ anye unan ekamba-ekamba.<verse eid="1SA 31:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1SA 31:4" />Sọọl amaabo abiom ñkpọekọñ amọ, “Sio akañkañ mfo nyʌñ ñwot miin, imiidooho ntoro mbon ammiifọọrọke edʌd ami eyaediñwot miin enyʌñ ensappa miin.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1SA 31:4">Ado abiom ñkpọekọñ amọ amaakop akpọsọñ ndịk ndin asịn adinam ntoro; ke ntoro Sọọl amaaben akañkañ amọ anyʌñ akịm idem amọ awot. <verse eid="1SA 31:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1SA 31:5" />Ke ini abiom ñkpọekọñ akekịtte ke Sọọl amaakpa, anye ñko amaaduọ akʌbọ ke akañkañ amọ anyʌñ akeene akpa. <verse eid="1SA 31:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1SA 31:6" />Ndin Sọọl ye nditọ ideen amọ ita ye abiom ñkpọekọñ amọ ye afịd ideen amọ emaekpañña kpa ke usen keed ado.<verse eid="1SA 31:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1SA 31:7" />Ke ini nditọ Isrel e-ekebaaha ke mben abedeñ ke edem Yọdan ekekịtte ke mbon ekọñ nditọ Isrel emaefeeñe ñko ke Sọọl ye nditọ ideen amọ emaekpañña, ammọ emaekpọñ mme abio ammọ efeeñe, ndin mbon Filistia ediben edʌñọ.<verse eid="1SA 31:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1SA 31:8" />Edem usen, ke mbon Filistia emaekedi edisịññe ñkpọ ke idem mme akpañkpa, ammọ emaekịt ke Sọọl ye nditọ ideen amọ ita emaekpañña ke abod Kilboa. <verse eid="1SA 31:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1SA 31:9" />Ammọ emaekpịkke anye iwuod enyʌñ eben ñkpọekọñ amọ, ndin edọñ isʌñutom eka afịd abio mbon Filistia ekesuan etob ami ke atu mme ubobodñkpọ ammọ ye mbon ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 31:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1SA 31:10" />Ammọ emaesịn ñkpọekọñ amọ ke itieukpono Astọred emaenyʌñ ebọp idem amọ edian ke ndibene Bed San.<verse eid="1SA 31:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1SA 31:11" />Ke ini mbon Yabes Kilied ekekoppo se mbon Filistia ekenam Sọọl, <verse eid="1SA 31:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1SA 31:12" />afịd mme akop uko mbon ekọñ ammọ emaewuọñọ esaña afịd akonayio ekaa Bed San. Ammọ emaekekọññọ mme akpo Sọọl ye ake nditọ ideen amọ ke ndibene Bed San enyʌñ ediben ekaa Yabes itie e-ekefọppọ ammọ. <verse eid="1SA 31:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1SA 31:13" />Ndin ammọ emaekoono mme akpọ ammọ ekebuuk ke idak eto tamaris ke Yabes, ndin ammọ emaetie utreudia usen itiaba.<verse eid="1SA 31:13" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1SA 31" />
</usx>